ta.\n    28→*   **Blocks 1 & 30:** drawing & text_block — Project Location Map and associated scale/coordinate data. VISION for the spatial layout of the site relative to major cross streets (Manchaca, Clawson Rd, 290); READ Block 30 for Mapsco #614S and Grid #G19.\n    29→*   **Blocks 8 & 31:** text_block — Environmental status notes. READ to confirm the site is in the West Bouldin Creek Watershed, is outside the 100-year floodplain, and is not in the Edwards Aquifer zone.\n    30→*   **Blocks 16, 17, 25, 26, 27:** various — Project-specific requirements and waivers. READ for specific stipulations including private hydrant maintenance (Block 16), private biofiltration pond maintenance (Block 17), parkland dedication fees for 39 units (Block 25), a specific DCM waiver (Block 26), and Traffic Control Plan requirements (Block 27).\n    31→*   **Block 5:** table — Revisions/Corrections. READ to confirm no revisions have been logged yet.\n    32→*   **Blocks 2, 3, 9-14, 18-24, 28-29, 32, 33:** various — Boilerplate, Administrative Notes, and Seals. READ selectively if reviewing general contractor responsibilities, standard city ordinances (lead-free water, recycling, USTs), engineer certifications, liability disclaimers, or standard erosion control notes. Includes empty approval stamps and review tables.\n    33→\n    34→---\n    35→\n    36→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    37→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"edb3a0f3-a37f-439a-848a-31f49210e3a7","uuid":"7df7125d-e7da-4549-9598-5162d559c9b1","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-01/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 1 — Cover\n\nCover sheet containing project details, location map, and sheet index.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis is the cover sheet for the Valley View Townhomes site plan (SP-2025-0126C). It serves as the primary reference document for the project, containing the sheet index, site development data, fire department requirements, a location map, and required municipal compliance notes.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   Project Area: 2.16 Acres\n*   Limits of Construction: 2.26 Acres\n*   Total Residential Units: 39 units\n*   Total Plan Sheets: 39 sheets\n*   Fire Flow Demand (@ 20 psi): 3000 GPM (Reduced to 1500 GPM with sprinkler system)\n*   Building Fire Area: 13,344 s.f.\n*   Occupancy Classification: R3\n*   Construction Classification: Type V-B\n*   Sprinkler System Type: NFPA 13D\n*   Private Hydrants: 1\n*   Mapsco / City of Austin Grid: #614S / #G19\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 15:** text_block — Project title, address (3759 Valley View Road), and permit number (SP-2025-0126C). READ for core project identification.\n*   **Block 4:** table — Site Development Data. READ for project team contact information, legal description, and exact acreage values. \n*   **Block 6:** table — Sheet List Table. READ to understand the structure of the 39-page drawing set and locate specific disciplines (grading, drainage, landscaping, etc.).\n*   **Block 7:** table — Austin Fire Department requirements. READ for specific fire design codes, fire flow demands (in GPM), and building classification data.\n*   **Blocks 1 & 30:** drawing & text_block — Project Location Map and associated scale/coordinate data. VISION for the spatial layout of the site relative to major cross streets (Manchaca, Clawson Rd, 290); READ Block 30 for Mapsco #614S and Grid #G19.\n*   **Blocks 8 & 31:** text_block — Environmental status notes. READ to confirm the site is in the West Bouldin Creek Watershed, is outside the 100-year floodplain, and is not in the Edwards Aquifer zone.\n*   **Blocks 16, 17, 25, 26, 27:** various — Project-specific requirements and waivers. READ for specific stipulations including private hydrant maintenance (Block 16), private biofiltration pond maintenance (Block 17), parkland dedication fees for 39 units (Block 25), a specific DCM waiver (Block 26), and Traffic Control Plan requirements (Block 27).\n*   **Block 5:** table — Revisions/Corrections. READ to confirm no revisions have been logged yet.\n*   **Blocks 2, 3, 9-14, 18-24, 28-29, 32, 33:** various — Boilerplate, Administrative Notes, and Seals. READ selectively if reviewing general contractor responsibilities, standard city ordinances (lead-free water, recycling, USTs), engineer certifications, liability disclaimers, or standard erosion control notes. Includes empty approval stamps and review tables.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":37,"startLine":1,"totalLines":37}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776954225842,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0112iZ3BR1rJ9NDumMRLiLYK","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Site Plan Facts\n     2→\n     3→# Facts — Valley View Townhomes (SP-2025-0126C)\n     4→**3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX 78704**\n     5→\n     6→---\n     7→\n     8→## Discrepancies\n     9→\n    10→- **Easement (Greenbelt Access & Use, Instrument 2010070731):** A perpetual, no-build greenbelt easement covering 0.31 acres (13,524 sq ft) of the NE interior of Lot 1 is NOT depicted on the submitted site plan and is NOT in the COA GIS easement layer. County clerk research confirms it is real, recorded, and perpetual. Must be depicted before approval.\n    11→- **Easement (City of Austin Drainage, Instrument 2011021137):** A perpetual City of Austin drainage easement covering 0.130 acres (5,670 sq ft) of the NE corner of Lot 1 is NOT depicted on the submitted site plan and is NOT in the COA GIS easement layer. County clerk research confirms it is real, recorded, and perpetual. Must be depicted before approval.\n    12→- **Combined NE no-build zone (~0.44 ac):** Together, the two easements above encumber approximately 0.44 acres (~19%) of the NE portion of the 2.16-acre site. Neither is shown on submitted plans. Proposed building layout must be evaluated against both easement footprints.\n    13→- **Acreage:** Site plan states 2.16 ac; 2019 deed/survey states 2.158 ac; TCAD states 2.1970 ac; COA GIS parcel measures 2.111 ac (91,944 sq ft). If the controlling acreage is 2.111 ac (GIS), the IC calculation based on 2.16 ac should be rechecked.\n    14→- **10' Wastewater Easement (Vol 73/76, C8S-75-160):** COA GIS shows this plat-dedicated easement running across the parcel. Not confirmed on the submitted site plan. Site plan notes \"must verify no conflicts.\"\n    15→- **25' Drainage Easement and 7.5' PUE (Vol 64/13, C8-71-079):** GIS shows these easements (from the Cortez Heights plat) running across the NE boundary of Lot 1. Not verified on site plan. Precise location relative to proposed improvements must be confirmed.\n    16→- **FIRM Panel Number:** Site plan cites Panel #48453C0585H (effective September 26, 2008). FloodPro returns null for both FIRM_PANEL and EFFECTIVE_DATE. Must be independently verified on FEMA Flood Map Service Center.\n    17→- **Demolition permit number:** Site plan cites \"2022-101266 BP\" as the demolition permit. Amanda shows 2022-101266 as a Plumbing Permit (Repair); the actual demolition building permit is 2022-096813 BP (Final). Actual demolition is confirmed complete.\n    18→\n    19→---\n    20→\n    21→## Property\n    22→\n    23→- **Address:** 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX 78704\n    24→- **Parcel ID (GeoID):** 0406100252\n    25→- **Legal Description:** Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision, Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas\n    26→- **Subdivision:** Mecey Subdivision (File No. C8S-75-100)\n    27→- **Plat Instrument:** Vol 73 / Pg 76 (Instrument 418356), filed 1975-12-11\n    28→- **County:** Travis\n    29→- **Site Area (site plan):** 2.16 acres\n    30→- **Site Area (2019 deed/survey):** 2.158 acres\n    31→- **Site Area (TCAD):** 2.1970 acres (95,701 sq ft)\n    32→- **Site Area (COA GIS parcel):** 2.111 acres (91,944 sq ft)\n    33→- **Limits of Construction:** 2.26 acres\n    34→- **Survey of Record (likely):** 2018 CDS Survey, Project No. 18-03-0225:021\n    35→- **Current Land Use:** Vacant land (formerly assisted living / nursing care facility; demolished June 2022)\n    36→\n    37→## Ownership\n    38→\n    39→- **Owner:** WM 41 Austin RE, LLC\n    40→- **Owner Mailing Address:** 500 West 5th Street, Ste. 1010, Austin, TX 78701\n    41→- **Acquisition Deed:** Instrument 2019197883 — Special Warranty Deed from SHG Resources LP to WM 41 Austin RE LLC (2019-12-11). Property conveyed