{"level":30,"time":1776954235682,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_014T49FfQVBjEy98TFDgTGx9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. From facts.md, I've learned:\n\n**Key Facts for Applicability:**\n- **Address:** 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX 78704\n- **Zoning:** MF-2 (Multi-Family Residence — Medium Density)\n- **Regulating Plan:** None (key! This means no Plaza Saltillo TOD, no NBG applies)\n- **Proposed Use:** 39 multi-family townhome units\n- **Proposed Features:** Stacked biofiltration / detention pond\n\n**Utility/Infrastructure Related:**\n- **Roadway Classification for Valley View Road:** ASMP Level 1 — Local Street (NOT a CTC, NOT an Urban Roadway within Subchapter E)\n- **Hill Country Roadway Corridor:** Not mentioned in facts — but I should check if within 1000 feet of any Hill Country Roadways\n- **Street Trees in ROW:** Not explicitly mentioned in facts\n- **Transformer/AE equipment:** Sheet 21 shows \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" with transformers and meters — this suggests electrical infrastructure is proposed\n- **Parking:** Site has parking (parking areas mentioned)\n- **Detention pond:** Yes — biofiltration/detention pond proposed (Sheet 15, 16)\n\n**What doesn't apply based on regulating plans:**\n- EL-2.5 (Plaza Saltillo TOD Core Transit Corridor) — N/A — site is NOT in Plaza Saltillo TOD\n- EL-2.6 (Plaza Saltillo TOD Pedestrian Priority Streets) — N/A — site is NOT in Plaza Saltillo TOD\n- EL-2.7 (Plaza Saltillo TOD Local Streets) — N/A — site is NOT in Plaza Saltillo TOD\n- EL-2.8 (NBG Zoning District) — N/A — site is NOT in NBG district\n\n\n- EL-2.1 (CTC/Urban Roadway) — Valley View Road is classified as a local street, so this likely doesn't trigger unless Subchapter E has broader application\n- EL-2.3 and EL-2.4 (ROW undergrounding requirements) — Both tied to CTC or Urban Roadway designations, which don't apply here\n\nStill need to verify whether the site falls within 1000 feet of any Hill Country Roadways for EL-2.2 applicability, and confirm what EL-2.9 covers.\n\nSeveral provisions appear relevant: the proposed detention pond means EL-2.10 requires checking that utilities don't run underneath it. If street trees with designated planting zones exist, EL-2.11 and EL-2.12 could apply. EL-2.13 depends on whether parkland is present on the site. Light rail corridors aren't a concern based on the facts provided. However, EL-2.15 stands out as likely applicable since the facts document multiple easements that haven't been verified against the site plan. EL-2.16 appears to address items within utility easements and needs further review.\n\nAdditional provisions to evaluate include potential private utilities in public rights-of-way, abandoned utilities that might block clearances, and public utilities not properly terminated. Underground storage tanks aren't mentioned in the facts, so EL-2.20 is unlikely. Power pole relocation could be necessary depending on utility coordination efforts. Sheet 21 shows transformers on the site, making EL-2.22 regarding transformer pad clearances and easements likely applicable. Tree well electrical outlets and utility routing through parking areas may also warrant attention depending on the landscape and parking layout.\n\nI need to cross-reference the electrical design plan, landscape plan, and plat to verify utility routing details and confirm which provisions actually apply.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8435,"cache_read_input_tokens":33381,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8435},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"sessi