{"level":30,"time":1776954247121,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LTy4DzUU6q3bBEVFKHEkeq","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 15 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 2: diagram — Calculations for a partial biofiltration pond, detailing drainage area data, water quality control calculations, biological elements calculations, and related parameters like volumes, areas, and flow rates.\n     4→\n     5→**APPENDIX R-6**\n     6→**PARTIAL BIOFILTRATION POND CALCULATIONS**\n     7→\n     8→**DRAINAGE AREA DATA:**\n     9→Drainage Area to Control: 1.48 ac\n    10→Drainage Area Impervious Cover: 86.09 %\n    11→1.27 ac\n    12→Capture Depth (0.5\"+(IC-20)/100)): 1.16 in\n    13→25 year Design Flow Rate (Q25): 14.27 cfs\n    14→100 year Peak Flow Rate (Q100): 18.83 cfs\n    15→\n    16→**WATER QUALITY CONTROL CALCULATIONS:**\n    17→| | Required | Provided |\n    18→|---|---|---|\n    19→| Water Quality Volume = (CD*DA*3630) | 6,237 cf | 6,388 cf |\n    20→| For Partial Sedimentation Pond Volume Min = 20% WQV | 1,278 cf | 2,632 cf |\n    21→| Filtration Pond Area (See ECM Section 1.6.7.C, EQ C-3) = WQV/(4+1.33*H) | 721 sf | 831 sf |\n    22→| Water Quality Elevation | 675.57 ft msl | |\n    23→| Elevation of Splitter Box/Overflow Weir (>WQ ELEV) | 675.65 ft msl | |\n    24→| Length of Splitter Weir | N/A (Stacked) ft | |\n    25→| Required Head to pass the Peak Flow (Q100) | N/A ft | |\n    26→| Pond Freeboard Provided to pass Peak Flow (Q100) | N/A ft | |\n    27→| Maximum Ponding Depth above Sand Bed (H) = (18-Max Ponding Depth) | >1 ft | 3.65 ft |\n    28→\n    29→**BIOLOGICAL ELEMENTS CALCULATIONS:**\n    30→Surface Area of Sedimentation Pond\n    31→= (Sedimentation Area) 1,024 sf\n    32→\n    33→Sedimentation Pond Plantings\n    34→Min = (10% of Sedimentation Biofiltration Area) 102 Plants 107 Plants\n    35→\n    36→Filtration Pond Plantings\n    37→Min = (20% of Filtration Area) 166 Plants 171 Plants\n    38→\n    39→## Block 3: drawing — This section contains a site plan for Unit 501, showing the layout of the area including retaining walls, a pond, and various drainage features. Key elements include PVC pipes, rip-rap, cleanouts, and specific elevations (e.g., TW 681.00, FG 672.00). It also notes a 'Biofiltration Media' area and details like a 'Pond Outfall Weir' and 'Concrete Structural Retaining Wall'.\n    40→\n    41→A detailed site plan drawing showing Unit 501. It includes property lines, topographic lines, and various infrastructure elements.\n    42→\n    43→Key features labeled:\n    44→- Unit 501\n    45→- Stone Pavers\n    46→- Fire Pit\n    47→- Concrete Splash Pad\n    48→- Pond Outfall Weir See Detail on Sheet 16\n    49→- Top of Biofiltration Media El = 672.00\n    50→- Cleanout (Typ) FL 6\": 669.75\n    51→- MUTCD Compliant Vertical Water Surface Marker Per DCM 8.3.3(B)(8)\n    52→- 6\" PVC Raised Outlet Pipe See Detail 1.6.7.C-3 FL In 6\": 669.31\n    53→- Discharge PVC Through Wall Install 6\" Threaded Cap on End of PVC with 1.33\" Hole Drilled in Bottom of Cap FL In 6\": 670.50\n    54→- 3' x 4' Concrete Splash Pad w/ 3' wide Rip-Rap\n    55→- 26.08 lf 6\" Perforated PVC @ 1.27%\n    56→- 6.58 lf 6\" PVC @ 1.00%\n    57→- 6.42 lf 6\" PVC @ 1.00%\n    58→- 26.08 lf 6\" Perforated PVC @ 1.00%\n    59→- Rock Flow Spreader 6\"-12\"(H) x 3'(W) 5-8\" Dia. Rock\n    60→- 6' Wide Rock Rip-Rap 5-8\" Dia. Rock\n    61→- 63.64 lf 24\" HDPE @ 1.35%\n    62→- 24\" Pipe Through Pond Wall FL In 24\": 672.94\n    63→- Concrete Structural Retaining Wall w/ Fall Protection Railing (By Others)\n    64→- End Retaining Wall\n    65→- 8' Wide Concrete Maintenance Path\n    66→- Pond Maintenance Gate 2-4' Swing Gates\n    67→- 8' Wide Maintenance Ramp 4:1 Max Slope\n    68→- Ramp Landing\n    69→- Sedimentation\n    70→- Create Swale to Direct Flows Along Pond Wall\n    71→\n    72→Various elevations are marked, such as TW 681.00, FG 672.00, FG 672.94, etc.\n    73→\n    74→## Block 5: table — A table showing the stage, area, and storage for the filtration pond at different elevations.\n    75→\n    76→**FILTRATION POND:**\n    77→\n    78→| Stage (ft msl)* | Area (sf) | Storage (cf) |\n    79→|---|---|---|\n    80→| 672.00 | 831 | 0 |\n    81→| 673.00 | 831 | 831 |\n    82→| 674.00 | 831 | 1,661 |\n    83→| 675.00 | 831 | 2,492 |\n    84→| 676.00 | 831 | 3,323 |\n    85→| 677.00 | 831 | 4,153 |\n    86→| 677.50 | 831 | 4,568 |\n    87→\n    88→*in one foot or less increments\n    89→\n    90→## Block 6: table — A table presenting variables and their values for a falling head orifice calculation. It includes surface area, orifice coefficient, head values, time, and calculated orifice area and diameter. Below the table is the formula used for the calculation.\n    91→\n    92→**Falling Head Orifice Calculator**\n    93→\n    94→| Surface Area (sq. ft.) | | 1942 |\n    95→| Orifice coefficient (use 0.6 per DCM) | | 0.6 |\n    96→| $h_1$ (ft) | | 5.15 |\n    97→| $h_2$ (ft) | | 0 |\n    98→| t (hrs.) | | 48 |\n    99→| $A_o$ orifice area (sq. ft.) | | 0.011 |\n   100→| Orifice diameter (in.) | | 1.39 |\n   101→\n   102→$$A_o = \\frac{-2A}{C_d * t * \\sqrt{2g}} * [\\sqrt{h_2} - \\sqrt{h_1}]$$\n   103→\n   104→## Block 7: table — Two tables providing calculations for a 100-year event. The top table details 'Biofiltration Entrance' with Entrance Velocity and D50 Rock Rip-Rap calculations. The bottom table details 'Pond Outfall' with Exit Velocity and D50 Rock Rip-Rap calculations.\n   105→\n   106→| Biofiltration Entrance (100-yr) |\n   107→|---|---|\n   108→| **Entrance Velocity Calculation** | **D50 Rock Rip-Rap Calculation** |\n   109→| Q100= 18.83 cfs | Q100= 18.83 cfs |\n   110→| L= 18 feet | A= 13.5 sf |\n   111→| D= 0.75 feet | V= 1.39 fps |\n   112→| V= 1.39 fps | D50= 0.25 in |\n   113→\n   114→| Pond Outfall (100-yr) |\n   115→|---|---|\n   116→| **Exit Velocity Calculation** | **D50 Rock Rip-Rap Calculation** |\n   117→| Q100= 15.60 cfs | Q100= 15.60 cfs |\n   118→| L= 12 feet | A= 9.0 sf |\n   119→| D= 0.75 feet | V= 1.73 fps |\n   120→| V= 1.73 fps | D50= 0.39 in |\n   121→\n   122→## Block 8: table — A table showing the stage, area, and storage for the sedimentation pond at different elevations.\n   123→\n   124→**SEDIMENTATION POND:**\n   125→\n   126→| Stage (ft msl)* | Area (sf) | Storage (cf) |\n   127→|---|---|---|\n   128→| 672.00 | 0 | 0 |\n   129→| 673.00 | 1,024 | 512 |\n   130→| 674.00 | 1,060 | 1,554 |\n   131→| 675.00 | 1,096 | 2,632 |\n   132→| 676.00 | 1,132 | 3,747 |\n   133→| 677.00 | 1,169 | 4,897 |\n   134→| 677.50 | 1,189 | 5,487 |\n   135→\n   136→## Block 9: table — A table outlining the required characteristics for biofiltration medium, including percentages of different soil components and testing criteria.\n   137→\n   138→**Table 1 - Biofiltration Medium Characteristics**\n   139→\n   140→| Parameter | Results* | Criteria | Criteria Met?* |\n   141→|---|---|---|---|\n   142→| Percent Sand + Coarse Fragments (ASTMD-422) | | 70 - 90% | |\n   143→| Percent Clay (< 0.002 mm) | | 3 - 10% | |\n   144→| Percent Silt + Clay (< 0.05 mm) | | ≤ 27% | |\n   145→| Percent Organic Matter (ASTM D-2974) | | 0.5 - 5% | |\n   146→| Is any \"Red Death\" included in medium? | | None allowed | |\n   147→| Is the mixture free of trash, stones, weeds, or other undesirable material? | | None allowed | |\n   148→| Is the medium well-mixed and homogenous? | | Must be homogenous | |\n   149→\n   150→## Block 10: table — A table summarizing discharge flow rates in cfs for different analysis points (Ex POA 1, Ex POA 2, Ex POA 3) across 2-year, 10-year, 25-year, and 100-year storm events, based on Atlas 14 data.\n   151→\n   152→**Discharge Summary**\n   153→| Analysis Point | Atlas 14 - Storm Water Flows (cfs) |\n   154→|---|---|\n   155→| | 2-yr | 10-yr | 25-yr | 100-yr |\n   156→| Ex POA 1 | 8.06 | 12.87 | 16.06 | 21.46 |\n   157→| Pro POA 1 | 7.72 | 12.34 | 15.65 | 21.14 |\n   158→| Ex POA 2 | 1.17 | 1.91 | 2.37 | 3.17 |\n   159→| Pro POA 2 | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.00 |\n   160→| Ex POA 3 | 0.90 | 1.41 | 1.75 | 2.31 |\n   161→| Pro POA 3 | 0.23 | 0.43 | 0.55 | 0.77 |\n   162→\n   163→## Block 11: table — A table showing water quality pond water surface elevations, including depth, area, and storage for different elevations. It also specifies the required and provided WQV (Water Quality Volume) elevations.\n   164→\n   165→**Water Quality Pond Water Surface Elevations**\n   166→| Elevation (ft) | Depth (ft) | Area (sf) | Storage (cf) |\n   167→|---|---|---|---|\n   168→| 672.00 | 0.00 | 831 | 0 |\n   169→| 673.00 | 1.00 | 1,854 | 1343 |\n   170→| 674.00 | 2.00 | 1,891 | 3215 |\n   171→| 675.00 | 3.00 | 1,927 | 5124 |\n   172→| 676.00 | 4.00 | 1,963 | 7069 |\n   173→| 677.00 | 5.00 | 1,999 | 9050 |\n   174→| 677.50 | 5.50 | 2,020 | 10055 |\n   175→| **675.57** | **WQV ELEV (Required)** | | **6237** |\n   176→| **675.65** | **WQV ELEV (Provided)** | | **6388** |\n   177→\n   178→## Block 12: table — Tables detailing the stage vs. storage and outflow summary for an onsite detention pond. It includes elevations, areas, volumes, event frequencies, and outflow rates.\n   179→\n   180→**Onsite Detention Pond**\n   181→\n   182→| Stage vs. Storage | | | Outflow Summary | | |\n   183→|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   184→| **Elevation** | **Area** | **Volume** | **Event** | **Elevation** | **Flow** |\n   185→| *ft* | *sf* | *cu.ft.* | *yr* | *ft* | *cfs* |\n   186→| 675.65 | 1939 | 0 | 2 | 676.25 | 6.24 |\n   187→| 676 | 1963 | 683 | 10 | 676.45 | 9.65 |\n   188→| 677 | 1999 | 2,664 | 25 | 676.57 | 11.85 |\n   189→| 677.5 | 2020 | 3,669 | 100 | 676.75 | 15.60 |\n   190→\n   191→## Block 13: table — A table detailing the requirements for high flow filter fabric, specifying test methods and criteria for properties like fabric weight, UV radiation stability, mullen burst strength, and water flow rate.\n   192→\n   193→**TABLE 2: HIGH FLOW FILTER FABRIC REQUIREMENTS**\n   194→\n   195→| Property | Test Method | Requirements |\n   196→|---|---|---|\n   197→| Fabric Weight | >D 3776 | 3.0 ounces/square yard minimum |\n   198→| Ultraviolet (UV) Radiation Stability | D 4355 | 70% strength retained minimum, After 500 hours in xenon arc device |\n   199→| Mullen Burst Strength | D 3786 | 120 pound per square inch minimum |\n   200→| Water Flow Rate | D 4491 | 275 gallons/minute/square feet minimum |\n   201→\n   202→## Block 14: text_block — A cross-sectional diagram illustrating a partial sedimentation/biofiltration pond setup. It shows a sedimentation chamber, a filtration basin, a splitter box, and a separator element with hedgerow.\n   203→\n   204→[Diagram of a partial sedimentation/biofiltration pond] \n   205→Labels include: \n   206→- Flow Spreader \n   207→- Splitter \n   208→- Sedimentation Chamber \n   209→- Filtration Basin \n   210→- WQV Elevation \n   211→- Separator Element With Hedgerow \n   212→- 5' x 8' Rock Flow Spreader \n   213→- 2' MIN \n   214→- Hedgerow \n   215→- Biofiltration Medium Bed \n   216→- Inflow \n   217→- 6-12\" \n   218→- PVC Underdrain Piping \n   219→- Outflow \n   220→\n   221→Figure 1.6.7.C-2: Partial Sedimentation/Biofiltration Pond. \n   222→\n   223→Figures provided are schematic only to show general design elements. A splitter box is not required per ECM 1.6.7.C.3.A when utilizing stack detention. A flow spreader can be utilized in place of the splitter box.\n   224→\n   225→## Block 15: text_block — A single sentence noting a regulatory compliance requirement for biofiltration medium.\n   226→\n   227→Biofiltration medium shall comply with ECM 1.6.7.C.4(A).\n   228→\n   229→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b6f63193-ad83-4c2c-8030-773d2a7b74d6","uuid":"bcc8a138-bb78-4be5-80d5-55affb2cc896","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-15/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 15 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 2: diagram — Calculations for a partial biofiltration pond, detailing drainage area data, water quality control calculations, biological elements calculations, and related parameters like volumes, areas, and flow rates.\n\n**APPENDIX R-6**\n**PARTIAL BIOFILTRATION POND CALCULATIONS**\n\n**DRAINAGE AREA DATA:**\nDrainage Area to Control: 1.48 ac\nDrainage Area Impervious Cover: 86.09 %\n1.27 ac\nCapture Depth (0.5\"+(IC-20)/100)): 1.16 in\n25 year Design Flow Rate (Q25): 14.27 cfs\n100 year Peak Flow Rate (Q100): 18.83 cfs\n\n**WATER QUALITY CONTROL CALCULATIONS:**\n| | Required | Provided |\n|---|---|---|\n| Water Quality Volume = (CD*DA*3630) | 6,237 cf | 6,388 cf |\n| For Partial Sedimentation Pond Volume Min = 20% WQV | 1,278 cf | 2,632 cf |\n| Filtration Pond Area (See ECM Section 1.6.7.C, EQ C-3) = WQV/(4+1.33*H) | 721 sf | 831 sf |\n| Water Quality Elevation | 675.57 ft msl | |\n| Elevation of Splitter Box/Overflow Weir (>WQ ELEV) | 675.65 ft msl | |\n| Length of Splitter Weir | N/A (Stacked) ft | |\n| Required Head to pass the Peak Flow (Q100) | N/A ft | |\n| Pond Freeboard Provided to pass Peak Flow (Q100) | N/A ft | |\n| Maximum Ponding Depth above Sand Bed (H) = (18-Max Ponding Depth) | >1 ft | 3.65 ft |\n\n**BIOLOGICAL ELEMENTS CALCULATIONS:**\nSurface Area of Sedimentation Pond\n= (Sedimentation Area) 1,024 sf\n\nSedimentation Pond Plantings\nMin = (10% of Sedimentation Biofiltration Area) 102 Plants 107 Plants\n\nFiltration Pond Plantings\nMin = (20% of Filtration Area) 166 Plants 171 Plants\n\n## Block 3: drawing — This section contains a site plan for Unit 501, showing the layout of the area including retaining walls, a pond, and various drainage features. Key elements include PVC pipes, rip-rap, cleanouts, and specific elevations (e.g., TW 681.00, FG 672.00). It also notes a 'Biofiltration Media' area and details like a 'Pond Outfall Weir' and 'Concrete Structural Retaining Wall'.\n\nA detailed site plan drawing showing Unit 501. It includes property lines, topographic lines, and various infrastructure elements.\n\nKey features labeled:\n- Unit 501\n- Stone Pavers\n- Fire Pit\n- Concrete Splash Pad\n- Pond Outfall Weir See Detail on Sheet 16\n- Top of Biofiltration Media El = 672.00\n- Cleanout (Typ) FL 6\": 669.75\n- MUTCD Compliant Vertical Water Surface Marker Per DCM 8.3.3(B)(8)\n- 6\" PVC Raised Outlet Pipe See Detail 1.6.7.C-3 FL In 6\": 669.31\n- Discharge PVC Through Wall Install 6\" Threaded Cap on End of PVC with 1.33\" Hole Drilled in Bottom of Cap FL In 6\": 670.50\n- 3' x 4' Concrete Splash Pad w/ 3' wide Rip-Rap\n- 26.08 lf 6\" Perforated PVC @ 1.27%\n- 6.58 lf 6\" PVC @ 1.00%\n- 6.42 lf 6\" PVC @ 1.00%\n- 26.08 lf 6\" Perforated PVC @ 1.00%\n- Rock Flow Spreader 6\"-12\"(H) x 3'(W) 5-8\" Dia. Rock\n- 6' Wide Rock Rip-Rap 5-8\" Dia. Rock\n- 63.64 lf 24\" HDPE @ 1.35%\n- 24\" Pipe Through Pond Wall FL In 24\": 672.94\n- Concrete Structural Retaining Wall w/ Fall Protection Railing (By Others)\n- End Retaining Wall\n- 8' Wide Concrete Maintenance Path\n- Pond Maintenance Gate 2-4' Swing Gates\n- 8' Wide Maintenance Ramp 4:1 Max Slope\n- Ramp Landing\n- Sedimentation\n- Create Swale to Direct Flows Along Pond Wall\n\nVarious elevations are marked, such as TW 681.00, FG 672.00, FG 672.94, etc.\n\n## Block 5: table — A table showing the stage, area, and storage for the filtration pond at different elevations.\n\n**FILTRATION POND:**\n\n| Stage (ft msl)* | Area (sf) | Storage (cf) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 672.00 | 831 | 0 |\n| 673.00 | 831 | 831 |\n| 674.00 | 831 | 1,661 |\n| 675.00 | 831 | 2,492 |\n| 676.00 | 831 | 3,323 |\n| 677.00 | 831 | 4,153 |\n| 677.50 | 831 | 4,568 |\n\n*in one foot or less increments\n\n## Block 6: table — A table presenting variables and their values for a falling head orifice calculation. It includes surface area, orifice coefficient, head values, time, and calculated orifice area and diameter. Below the table is the formula used for the calculation.\n\n**Falling Head Orifice Calculator**\n\n| Surface Area (sq. ft.) | | 1942 |\n| Orifice coefficient (use 0.6 per DCM) | | 0.6 |\n| $h_1$ (ft) | | 5.15 |\n| $h_2$ (ft) | | 0 |\n| t (hrs.) | | 48 |\n| $A_o$ orifice area (sq. ft.) | | 0.011 |\n| Orifice diameter (in.) | | 1.39 |\n\n$$A_o = \\frac{-2A}{C_d * t * \\sqrt{2g}} * [\\sqrt{h_2} - \\sqrt{h_1}]$$\n\n## Block 7: table — Two tables providing calculations for a 100-year event. The top table details 'Biofiltration Entrance' with Entrance Velocity and D50 Rock Rip-Rap calculations. The bottom table details 'Pond Outfall' with Exit Velocity and D50 Rock Rip-Rap calculations.\n\n| Biofiltration Entrance (100-yr) |\n|---|---|\n| **Entrance Velocity Calculation** | **D50 Rock Rip-Rap Calculation** |\n| Q100= 18.83 cfs | Q100= 18.83 cfs |\n| L= 18 feet | A= 13.5 sf |\n| D= 0.75 feet | V= 1.39 fps |\n| V= 1.39 fps | D50= 0.25 in |\n\n| Pond Outfall (100-yr) |\n|---|---|\n| **Exit Velocity Calculation** | **D50 Rock Rip-Rap Calculation** |\n| Q100= 15.60 cfs | Q100= 15.60 cfs |\n| L= 12 feet | A= 9.0 sf |\n| D= 0.75 feet | V= 1.73 fps |\n| V= 1.73 fps | D50= 0.39 in |\n\n## Block 8: table — A table showing the stage, area, and storage for the sedimentation pond at different elevations.\n\n**SEDIMENTATION POND:**\n\n| Stage (ft msl)* | Area (sf) | Storage (cf) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 672.00 | 0 | 0 |\n| 673.00 | 1,024 | 512 |\n| 674.00 | 1,060 | 1,554 |\n| 675.00 | 1,096 | 2,632 |\n| 676.00 | 1,132 | 3,747 |\n| 677.00 | 1,169 | 4,897 |\n| 677.50 | 1,189 | 5,487 |\n\n## Block 9: table — A table outlining the required characteristics for biofiltration medium, including percentages of different soil components and testing criteria.\n\n**Table 1 - Biofiltration Medium Characteristics**\n\n| Parameter | Results* | Criteria | Criteria Met?* |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Percent Sand + Coarse Fragments (ASTMD-422) | | 70 - 90% | |\n| Percent Clay (< 0.002 mm) | | 3 - 10% | |\n| Percent Silt + Clay (< 0.05 mm) | | ≤ 27% | |\n| Percent Organic Matter (ASTM D-2974) | | 0.5 - 5% | |\n| Is any \"Red Death\" included in medium? | | None allowed | |\n| Is the mixture free of trash, stones, weeds, or other undesirable material? | | None allowed | |\n| Is the medium well-mixed and homogenous? | | Must be homogenous | |\n\n## Block 10: table — A table summarizing discharge flow rates in cfs for different analysis points (Ex POA 1, Ex POA 2, Ex POA 3) across 2-year, 10-year, 25-year, and 100-year storm events, based on Atlas 14 data.\n\n**Discharge Summary**\n| Analysis Point | Atlas 14 - Storm Water Flows (cfs) |\n|---|---|\n| | 2-yr | 10-yr | 25-yr | 100-yr |\n| Ex POA 1 | 8.06 | 12.87 | 16.06 | 21.46 |\n| Pro POA 1 | 7.72 | 12.34 | 15.65 | 21.14 |\n| Ex POA 2 | 1.17 | 1.91 | 2.37 | 3.17 |\n| Pro POA 2 | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.00 |\n| Ex POA 3 | 0.90 | 1.41 | 1.75 | 2.31 |\n| Pro POA 3 | 0.23 | 0.43 | 0.55 | 0.77 |\n\n## Block 11: table — A table showing water quality pond water surface elevations, including depth, area, and storage for different elevations. It also specifies the required and provided WQV (Water Quality Volume) elevations.\n\n**Water Quality Pond Water Surface Elevations**\n| Elevation (ft) | Depth (ft) | Area (sf) | Storage (cf) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 672.00 | 0.00 | 831 | 0 |\n| 673.00 | 1.00 | 1,854 | 1343 |\n| 674.00 | 2.00 | 1,891 | 3215 |\n| 675.00 | 3.00 | 1,927 | 5124 |\n| 676.00 | 4.00 | 1,963 | 7069 |\n| 677.00 | 5.00 | 1,999 | 9050 |\n| 677.50 | 5.50 | 2,020 | 10055 |\n| **675.57** | **WQV ELEV (Required)** | | **6237** |\n| **675.65** | **WQV ELEV (Provided)** | | **6388** |\n\n## Block 12: table — Tables detailing the stage vs. storage and outflow summary for an onsite detention pond. It includes elevations, areas, volumes, event frequencies, and outflow rates.\n\n**Onsite Detention Pond**\n\n| Stage vs. Storage | | | Outflow Summary | | |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Elevation** | **Area** | **Volume** | **Event** | **Elevation** | **Flow** |\n| *ft* | *sf* | *cu.ft.* | *yr* | *ft* | *cfs* |\n| 675.65 | 1939 | 0 | 2 | 676.25 | 6.24 |\n| 676 | 1963 | 683 | 10 | 676.45 | 9.65 |\n| 677 | 1999 | 2,664 | 25 | 676.57 | 11.85 |\n| 677.5 | 2020 | 3,669 | 100 | 676.75 | 15.60 |\n\n## Block 13: table — A table detailing the requirements for high flow filter fabric, specifying test methods and criteria for properties like fabric weight, UV radiation stability, mullen burst strength, and water flow rate.\n\n**TABLE 2: HIGH FLOW FILTER FABRIC REQUIREMENTS**\n\n| Property | Test Method | Requirements |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fabric Weight | >D 3776 | 3.0 ounces/square yard minimum |\n| Ultraviolet (UV) Radiation Stability | D 4355 | 70% strength retained minimum, After 500 hours in xenon arc device |\n| Mullen Burst Strength | D 3786 | 120 pound per square inch minimum |\n| Water Flow Rate | D 4491 | 275 gallons/minute/square feet minimum |\n\n## Block 14: text_block — A cross-sectional diagram illustrating a partial sedimentation/biofiltration pond setup. It shows a sedimentation chamber, a filtration basin, a splitter box, and a separator element with hedgerow.\n\n[Diagram of a partial sedimentation/biofiltration pond] \nLabels include: \n- Flow Spreader \n- Splitter \n- Sedimentation Chamber \n- Filtration Basin \n- WQV Elevation \n- Separator Element With Hedgerow \n- 5' x 8' Rock Flow Spreader \n- 2' MIN \n- Hedgerow \n- Biofiltration Medium Bed \n- Inflow \n- 6-12\" \n- PVC Underdrain Piping \n- Outflow \n\nFigure 1.6.7.C-2: Partial Sedimentation/Biofiltration Pond. \n\nFigures provided are schematic only to show general design elements. A splitter box is not required per ECM 1.6.7.C.3.A when utilizing stack detention. A flow spreader can be utilized in place of the splitter box.\n\n## Block 15: text_block — A single sentence noting a regulatory compliance requirement for biofiltration medium.\n\nBiofiltration medium shall comply with ECM 1.6.7.C.4(A).\n\n","numLines":229,"startLine":1,"totalLines":229}}}
