ility crossings. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the proposed infrastructure and intersections with existing easements and lines.\n    21→* **Block 3**: notes — Restrained Joints Specification. Details the requirement to restrain all bends, tees, and valves using specific SPL standards (WW-27F or WW-27A). READ the block content for the approved mechanical joint restraint standards.\n    22→* **Block 4**: notes — Benchmarks. Provides the elevation reference points for the site. READ the block content for exact elevations and datum (NAVD 88).\n    23→* **Block 5**: notes — Water Tap Note. Contains instructions for replacing the existing AC pipe with DI pipe. READ the block content for strict asbestos handling and disposal requirements.\n    24→* **Block 6**: notes — Legend. Defines linetypes and symbols used in the plan view. READ the block content to accurately interpret the utility lines (Water, Wastewater, Storm, Electric) in Block 2.\n    25→* **Block 7**: notes — PRV Note. READ the block content for the specific pressure threshold (65 psi) that requires the installation of a pressure reducing valve.\n    26→* **Block 9**: notes — Void and Water Flow Mitigation. READ the block content for the trenching depth threshold (> 5 feet) that triggers a mandatory inspection by a licensed geologist.\n    27→* **Blocks 8, 10, 11, 12, 13**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Includes the legal description, standard disclaimers regarding existing utility locations, general verification notes, the PE Seal for Jason K. Rodgers, and the Texas 811 logo. READ the block content only if verifying administrative details, legal descriptions, or standard utility coordination notes.\n    28→\n    29→---\n    30→\n    31→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    32→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51587e83-ba72-4647-83cb-6d408affd332","uuid":"8442aeec-3adf-4cc1-a283-40b5b3b3d370","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-20/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 20 — Utility Tap Public Plan & Profile\n\nUtility tap public plan and profile for townhomes project.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the public plan and profile for a proposed utility tap (Water Line A) for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the connection to an existing AC water main, the transition to new DI pipe, and the installation of a new fire demand meter, vault, and fire hydrant.\n\n**Key values:**\n* Proposed Pipe Segments: 47.0 lf of 8\" DI (@ 0.00% slope), 5.0 lf of 6\" DI (@ -0.00% slope), 12.0 lf of 6\" DI (@ 0.00% slope), 3.0 lf of 6\" C900, 5.0 lf of 6\" C900\n* Flowline Elevations: FL 8\" = 674.33', FL In 6\" = 674.42', FL Out 6\" = 674.42'\n* Restraints: 52' of restraints required from Sta 0+00 to Sta 0+52\n* Benchmarks: BM #1 = 678.52' (NAVD 88), BM #2 = 681.08' (NAVD 88)\n* Pressure Reducing Valve (PRV) Threshold: 65 psi\n* Geologist Inspection Trench Depth Threshold: > 5 feet\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n* **Block 1**: drawing — Profile View of Water Line A (Wtr-Ln-A). Shows the vertical alignment of the proposed water line from station 0+00 to 0+75, including the transition from AC to DI pipe, reducers, and the meter vault. Use VISION to examine the pipe slopes and relationship to the existing/proposed ground surfaces, and READ for exact flowline elevations, lengths, and the 52' restraint dimension.\n* **Block 2**: drawing — Plan View of Utility Tap. Top-down layout showing the proposed connection to the existing 6\" water line, the new fire hydrant, vault, and various utility crossings. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the proposed infrastructure and intersections with existing easements and lines.\n* **Block 3**: notes — Restrained Joints Specification. Details the requirement to restrain all bends, tees, and valves using specific SPL standards (WW-27F or WW-27A). READ the block content for the approved mechanical joint restraint standards.\n* **Block 4**: notes — Benchmarks. Provides the elevation reference points for the site. READ the block content for exact elevations and datum (NAVD 88).\n* **Block 5**: notes — Water Tap Note. Contains instructions for replacing the existing AC pipe with DI pipe. READ the block content for strict asbestos handling and disposal requirements.\n* **Block 6**: notes — Legend. Defines linetypes and symbols used in the plan view. READ the block content to accurately interpret the utility lines (Water, Wastewater, Storm, Electric) in Block 2.\n* **Block 7**: notes — PRV Note. READ the block content for the specific pressure threshold (65 psi) that requires the installation of a pressure reducing valve.\n* **Block 9**: notes — Void and Water Flow Mitigation. READ the block content for the trenching depth threshold (> 5 feet) that triggers a mandatory inspection by a licensed geologist.\n* **Blocks 8, 10, 11, 12, 13**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Includes the legal description, standard disclaimers regarding existing utility locations, general verification notes, the PE Seal for Jason K. Rodgers, and the Texas 811 logo. READ the block content only if verifying administrative details, legal descriptions, or standard utility coordination notes.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":32,"startLine":1,"totalLines":32}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776954264683,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01FdW1g46hkLNQ7KtXhm4CVU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good understanding of the site. Let me assess what I've learned so far:\n\n**Site Context:**\n- Address: 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX 78704\n- Zoning: MF-2 (Multi-Family)\n- No Regulating Plan (NOT in Plaza Saltillo TOD, NBG, or Hill Country Corridors)\n- Valley View Road is a LOCAL STREET (not a CTC or Urban Roadway per Subchapter E)\n- 39 townhome units, 8 buildings\n- Multiple existing easements on site (electric, drainage, water, greenbelt access)\n- Detention/biofiltration pond in NE corner\n\n**Documents available:**\n- Sheet 21: Electrical Design Plan (transformers, electrical routing)\n- Sheet 9: Site Plan (general layout)\n- Sheet 31: Landscape Plan (street trees, planting zones)\n- Sheet 2: Plat (easements)\n- Sheet 19-20: Utility Tap Plans (water/wastewater connections)\n- Sheet 15-16: Detention Pond Plans\n\n**Applicability Assessment:**\n\nNow let me go through each checklist item:\n\n**EL-2.1** (CTC/Urban Roadway undergrounding): NOT APPLICABLE\n- Site fronts Valley View Road (LOCAL STREET, not a CTC or Urban Roadway)\n- The utility undergrounding requirement under Subchapter E § 2.2.2.B.3.a only applies to CTCs or Urban Roadways within the Subchapter E boundary polygon\n\n**EL-2.2** (Hill Country Corridor): NEED TO VERIFY\n- Site is on Valley View Road in South Austin\n- Hill Country corridors: Loop 360, RM 620, RM 2222, RM 2244, or Southwest Parkway\n\n\n- Valley View Road doesn't appear to be within 1,000 feet of any of these\n\n**EL-2.3, EL-2.4** (ROW undergrounding on CTC/Urban Roadway): NOT APPLICABLE\n- Same as EL-2.1\n\n**EL-2.5-2.8** (Plaza Saltillo TOD, NBG): NOT APPLICABLE\n- No Regulating Plan listed in facts.md\n\n**EL-2.9** (10-foot overhead utility zone): May apply if overhead utilities remain\n- Need to check electrical plan for overhead utilities\n\n**EL-2.10** (Utilities under pond):\n- Site has detention/biofiltration pond in NE corner, so I need to verify utilities don't route under the pond\n\n**EL-2.11-2.12** (AW in planting zones): May apply if street trees in ROW\n- Need to check landscape plan for ROW trees\n\n**EL-2.13** (Transformers in parkland): Applicable if parkland adjacent\n- Facts.md indicates parkland deficiency with two polygon features intersecting the parcel, so I should verify whether transformers are located in parkland\n\n**EL-2.14** (Light rail coordination): NOT LIKELY APPLICABLE\n- Site is not near any light rail corridors\n\n**EL-2.15** (Easement boundary in ROW): NEED TO CHECK\n- Multiple easements exist on site per facts.md, need to verify their boundaries don't encroach into proposed ROW\n\n**EL-2.16** (Items in easements without license): APPLICABLE - HIGH PRIORITY\n- Site contains numerous easements including Greenbelt Access & Use (0.31 ac), City of Austin Drainage (0.13 ac), wastewater, drainage, electric, and PUE easements. Facts.md notes the Greenbelt and Drainage easements aren't shown on the site plan, so I need to confirm licensing and ensure buildings don't encroach on these areas.\n\n**EL-2.17** (Private utilities in public ROW): May apply\n- Should verify utility routing doesn't cross into public right-of-way.\n\n**EL-2.18** (Abandoned utilities not removed): May apply\n- The existing demolished building requires checking the demolition plan for proper utility removal.\n\n**EL-2.19** (Public utilities not terminated): May apply\n- Any existing public utilities in the ROW need proper termination.\n\n**EL-2.20** (USTs not at adequate distance from easements): Not applicable\n- Facts.md confirms no registered Underground Storage Tanks on site.\n\n**EL-2.21** (Power pole relocation): May apply if poles relocated\n- The electrical plan should clarify whether poles are being relocated.\n\n**EL-2.22** (Transformer pad): HIGHLY APPLICABLE\n- Sheet 21 depicts transformer pads that need verification for proper clearances including 10 ft hot-stick side and 3 ft non-operator\n\n, 5 ft operator side clearances. Truck access must be within 6 ft of parking or traffic areas, a dedicated AE easement should exist, and the pad should be on customer property rather than in the ROW.\n\n**EL-2.23** (Tree well outlets): May apply if tree wells proposed\n- The landscape plan will indicate whether tree wells are included in the design.\n\n**EL-2.24** (Table B utilities in parking): Not applicable\n- Table B requirements only apply to nonresidential zoning, and this site is zoned MF-2 (residential).\n\nI should examine the electrical design plan more closely to verify transformer specifications and utility routing details, and review the landscape plan for any ROW tree-related issues.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2517,"cache_read_input_tokens":52380,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2517},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9a5665b-9006-428b-bc9b-c42e794b3bcd","uuid":"b64db3b5-078a-4a2f-acda-5d97a681c85d"}
