{"level":30,"time":1776954268771,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01FdW1g46hkLNQ7KtXhm4CVU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0129S9bEqrHJcFbXxyHaPo5d","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":15,"prompt":"Examine the biofiltration-detention pond plan and identify:\n1. The complete footprint and location of the detention pond relative to proposed buildings and utilities\n2. Are there any utility lines (electrical, water, wastewater, or storm drain) shown crossing through or under the pond footprint?\n3. What utilities are shown adjacent to or near the pond boundaries?\n4. Are there inlet/outlet structures and how are they positioned relative to utilities?\n5. Any markings indicating easement boundaries within or adjacent to the pond area?\n\nSpecifically, check whether any utilities appear to route underneath the proposed pond area."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2517,"cache_read_input_tokens":52380,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2517},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9a5665b-9006-428b-bc9b-c42e794b3bcd","uuid":"1e010ef0-1267-4fcf-8adf-ec9752341bd6"}
{"level":30,"time":1776954270082,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01PZPo2SGbQg17Qi4Qf9FiGA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see Austin Energy provided preliminary design requirements and a Bluebeam link for site comments. This indicates that Austin Energy is actively reviewing the project. \n\nNow, I need to systematically evaluate the 32 checklist items. Let me organize my approach:\n\n**Key Facts I've Gathered So Far:**\n1. Austin Energy completeness check is COMPLETE per City records\n2. Project is on preliminary electrical design (Sheet 21)\n3. The site plan includes water and wastewater utility connections to existing mains\n4. Austin Energy has provided preliminary design requirements\n5. City of Austin is serving water and wastewater (not uncertain)\n6. From the facts.md: Site is in West Bouldin Creek Watershed, Zone X flood, not in regulating plan area\n\n**What I Need to Verify:**\n1. ESPA (Electric Service Planning Application) - if new service required\n2. AEU (Austin Energy Utility) clearance - if it's documented\n3. Electric Service Availability Letter - only if uncertain which utility serves\n4. Site notes for AE service area\n5. Developer responsibility notes for conduit\n6. Four standard Austin Energy notes (exactly as required)\n7. Transformer/pull box approvals\n8. Guy anchor conflicts with driveways\n9. Preconstruction meeting note (if demolition)\n10. Electrical easements\n11. AutoCAD drawing submission to AE\n12. AE facility access documentation\n13-15. Moonlight tower requirements (need to check if applicable to downtown/central Austin location)\n16-22. Street lighting issues (spacing, conflicts, etc.)\n23. AULCC clearance - depends on linear footage of ROW work\n24-27. Gattan, telecom, dry utility, CIP clearances\n28-29. ROW utility coordination case closure\n29. Additional Review Acknowledgement table\n30-31. Addressing approval and street name reservation\n32. Transmission easement plat notes (only if transmission easement exists)\n\n\nThe project is located in the Valley View Road area and isn't subject to a regulating plan, which eliminates certain applicability concerns. Since it's outside the Great Streets boundary, downtown-specific requirements won't apply. I should examine the actual site plan sheets to verify what utility notes and electrical design elements are currently shown.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":641,"cache_read_input_tokens":58907,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":641},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"edb3a0f3-a37f-439a-848a-31f49210e3a7","uuid":"a1c3b244-feb7-41f3-86c8-fe747966766d"}
