{"level":30,"time":1776954290626,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine this electrical design plan and identify: 1) Are there ANY overhead electrical utilities shown (poles, overhead lines, overhead service drops, transmission lines)? 2) Are there ONLY underground electrical utilities shown? 3) What specific electrical infrastructure is depicted (transformers, pull boxes, meters, underground conduit routing)? 4) Are there any clearance dimensions or envelope delineations shown? 5) Is there any reference to Austin Energy (AE) utility coordination or clearance requirements?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for Valley View Townhomes, here are the findings for your specific questions:\n\n**1) Are there ANY overhead electrical utilities shown (poles, overhead lines, overhead service drops, transmission lines)?**\n*   **Yes.** There is an existing overhead electrical line shown along the western (left) boundary of the property, parallel to the road. This line is explicitly marked with the line type **\"- OHE -\"** (OverHead Electric).\n\n**2) Are there ONLY underground electrical utilities shown?**\n*   **No.** While the proposed onsite routing within the property boundaries appears to be entirely underground, it is not the *only* utility shown because the existing overhead line (\"- OHE -\") is clearly depicted along the perimeter. The proposed onsite blue routing lines are explicitly labeled as **\"Underground Electric Line\"**.\n\n**3) What specific electrical infrastructure is depicted (transformers, pull boxes, meters, underground conduit routing)?**\nThe drawing uses bold blue lines and symbols to depict the electrical network. The following specific infrastructure components are explicitly labeled with text callouts:\n*   **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**: Multiple locations are shown with dashed rectangular footprints (e.g., near Bldg 1, Bldg 6, between Bldg 2 & 5).\n*   **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**: Multiple locations are depicted along the main routing paths (often at directional changes or junctions).\n*   **\"Electrical Meters\"**: Shown as arrays attached to or immediately adjacent to the buildings (labeled at Bldg 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, and 8).\n*   **\"Underground Electric Line\"**: Explicitly called out pointing to the main blue lines routing the electrical service throughout the site.\n\n**4) Are there any clearance dimensions or envelope delineations shown?**\n*   **No specific numeric dimensions are shown.** There are dashed rectangular outlines drawn around the \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations, which typically indicate the pad itself or a general easement/clearance area, but there are absolutely zero numeric clearance dimensions (e.g., \"10' clearance\") or specific regulatory envelopes (such as radial safety clearances around the \"- OHE -\" lines) delineated on this plan.\n\n**5) Is there any reference to Austin Energy (AE) utility coordination or clearance requirements?**\n*   **No.** A thorough review of the labels, title block, and notes (including the \"Utility Notes\" section in the bottom right and the \"Note\" in the bottom left) reveals no mention of \"Austin Energy\", \"AE\", or any specific AE design criteria or clearance requirements. The only municipal reference found is to \"COA\" (City of Austin) in the bottom left note regarding a Water Flow Mitigation Rule.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1408,"outputTokens":585,"totalTokens":3746,"reasoningTokens":1753},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine this electrical design plan and identify: 1) Are there ANY overhead electrical utilities shown (poles, overhead lines, overhead service drops, transmission lines)? 2) Are there ONLY underground electrical utilities shown? 3) What specific electrical infrastructure is depicted (transformers, pull boxes, meters, underground conduit routing)? 4) Are there any clearance dimensions or envelope delineations shown? 5) Is there any reference to Austin Energy (AE) utility coordination or clearance requirements?"}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-HQG6huWNaujGyWCZZ80dcULa","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-lan