ical network. The following specific infrastructure components are explicitly labeled with text callouts:\n*   **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**: Multiple locations are shown with dashed rectangular footprints (e.g., near Bldg 1, Bldg 6, between Bldg 2 & 5).\n*   **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**: Multiple locations are depicted along the main routing paths (often at directional changes or junctions).\n*   **\"Electrical Meters\"**: Shown as arrays attached to or immediately adjacent to the buildings (labeled at Bldg 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, and 8).\n*   **\"Underground Electric Line\"**: Explicitly called out pointing to the main blue lines routing the electrical service throughout the site.\n\n**4) Are there any clearance dimensions or envelope delineations shown?**\n*   **No specific numeric dimensions are shown.** There are dashed rectangular outlines drawn around the \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations, which typically indicate the pad itself or a general easement/clearance area, but there are absolutely zero numeric clearance dimensions (e.g., \"10' clearance\") or specific regulatory envelopes (such as radial safety clearances around the \"- OHE -\" lines) delineated on this plan.\n\n**5) Is there any reference to Austin Energy (AE) utility coordination or clearance requirements?**\n*   **No.** A thorough review of the labels, title block, and notes (including the \"Utility Notes\" section in the bottom right and the \"Note\" in the bottom left) reveals no mention of \"Austin Energy\", \"AE\", or any specific AE design criteria or clearance requirements. The only municipal reference found is to \"COA\" (City of Austin) in the bottom left note regarding a Water Flow Mitigation Rule.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1408,"outputTokens":585,"totalTokens":3746,"reasoningTokens":1753},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,