ted on the western boundary (Pad 1 and Pad 2) are enclosed by dashed rectangular linework. A leader line pointing to the dashed box around Pad 2 (south-west) is labeled **\"Vault Easement\"**. Based on the identical visual convention, Pad 1 is also located within a \"Vault Easement.\"\n*   The two internally located transformer pads (Pad 3 and Pad 4) do not have any visible dashed linework or labels indicating they are encumbered by a specific utility or vault easement on this sheet.\n\n**3. Routing of Underground Electric Lines**\nThe underground electric lines are denoted by a dashed line with an embedded \"E\" (**— E —**) and are labeled in one instance on the left side as **\"Underground Electric Line\"**.\n*   **General Routing:** The main line enters the site from the west (near Valley View Road) and splits to run generally north and south along the western perimeter of the internal drive aisle, connecting to Pad 1 and Pad 2.\n*   **Routing to Internal Pads:** Branches from this main western line cross the paved internal drive aisles/parking areas to reach the internal transformers (Pad 3 and Pad 4). \n    *   The line to Pad 3 branches off near Unit 202, crosses the drive aisle eastward, routes between Bldg. 2 and Bldg. 8, crosses another internal drive aisle, and connects to the pad.\n    *   The line to Pad 4 branches off from the line near Pad 2, crosses the western drive aisle eastward, routes between Bldg. 8 and Bldg. 7, and connects to the pad.\n*   **Prohibited Areas:** The underground electric lines (— E —) are clearly shown routing directly across internal paved drive aisles/parking areas in multiple locations to distribute power throughout the site. There are no ponds or water quality features clearly labeled on this specific sheet that the lines cross.\n\n**4. Clearance Zones or Setback Requirements**\nThere are no dimensions, hashed areas, radius lines, or text annotations marked on this plan indicating clearance zones, working spaces, or specific setback requirements for any of the electrical transformer pads or electrical meters.\n\n**5. Annotations Regarding Austin Energy**\nA review of the general text, \"Note\", and \"Utility Notes\" on this sheet reveals **no annotations** regarding Austin Energy (AE) coordination, specific truck access requirements for the transformer locations, or Austin Energy specific easements. (Note: The \"Utility Notes\" reference \"City of Austin\" details for water/wastewater, but do not mention electrical utility coordination).","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1437,"outputTokens":821,"totalTokens":4461,"reasoningTokens":2203},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe 