{"level":30,"time":1776954306255,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01H8YPxFqgg4HqoLEjqbs6SV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The blocks.md for Sheet 3 is only 46 lines. Let me use the vision tool to look directly at Sheet 3 to see what the electrical transmission notes, Austin Energy requirements, and other electrical information says.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":249,"cache_read_input_tokens":54921,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":249},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e121e67-5008-4f73-b228-82e438cca3a3","uuid":"6a8a9bc1-8c0b-4515-b6ac-80d9ab745d6a"}
{"level":30,"time":1776954306701,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":3,"prompt":"Examine Sheet 3 (General Notes) and provide a comprehensive list of all notes visible related to:\n1. Austin Energy service area notes\n2. Developer responsibility notes for conduit and electrical infrastructure\n3. The four standard Austin Energy notes (tree pruning, easement access, erosion control, clearance maintenance)\n4. Any notes about moonlight towers or preconstruction meetings\n5. Any transmission easement notes\nProvide the exact text of any Austin Energy-related notes found on this sheet. If any expected standard notes are missing or incomplete, note that explicitly.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 3 (General Notes) of the provided site plan, here is a comprehensive breakdown of all notes related to Austin Energy (AE), categorized by your specific requests. \n\nPlease note: The document contains a numbered list titled **\"Electric Notes\"**, and strangely, an exact unnumbered duplicate of these five notes appears immediately below the \"Fire Department\" section.\n\n### 1. Austin Energy Service Area Notes\n**Status:** **Missing**\nThere is no specific note on this sheet explicitly stating, \"This project is located within the Austin Energy service area\" (or similar standard phrasing). However, the applicability is strongly implied by the extensive list of AE requirements.\n\n### 2. Developer Responsibility Notes for Conduit and Electrical Infrastructure\n**Status:** **Incomplete / Missing**\nThere are no notes explicitly detailing the developer's responsibility for installing conduit or electrical infrastructure per Austin Energy Design Criteria. The only note regarding financial responsibility for electrical infrastructure is limited to the *relocation* of existing facilities:\n*   **Electric Notes #5:** \"Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\"\n\n### 3. The Four Standard Austin Energy Notes\n**Status:** **Present**\nAll four standard notes are present under the heading **\"Electric Notes\"** in the middle column (numbered 1 through 4), with an additional fifth note. (As mentioned, this exact block of text is also repeated without numbers directly below the \"Fire Department\" section).\n\nHere is the exact transcription of the standard notes:\n\n*   **Tree Pruning (Note 1):** \"Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n*   **Easement Access (Note 2):** \"The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n*   **Erosion Control / Initial Pruning (Note 3):** \"The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\"\n*   **Clearance Maintenance (Note 4):** \"The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\"\n\n### 4. Notes about Moonlight Towers or Preconstruction Meetings\n**Status:** Moonlight Towers (**Missing**), Preconstruction Meetings (**Present**)\n*   There are absolutely **no notes** regarding Moonlight Towers on this sheet.\n*   Preconstruction meetings are explicitly addressed under the transmission notes.\n\n**Exact transcription regarding preconstruction meetings:**\n*   **Electric Transmission Notes #3:** \"A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (at 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n\n### 5. Transmission Easement Notes\n**Status:** **Present**\nA dedicated section titled **\"Electric Transmission Notes\"** is located at the top of the middle column, containing 16 specific items. \n\nHere is the exact transcription of the entire section:\n\n> **Electric Transmission Notes**\n> 1. No parking is permitted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\n> 2. **Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.** Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a meeting.\n> 3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (at 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\n> 4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\n> 5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n> 6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\n> 7. For safety reasons, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\n> 8. 24 hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\n> 9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\n> 10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n> 11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structure/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be nominal curbing.\n> 12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\n> 13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\n> 14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures.\n> 15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.\n> 16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n>     - any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.\n>     - any structure of any kind in such proximity to transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\n>     - any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1423,"outputTokens":1702,"totalTokens":5918,"reasoningTokens":2793},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 3237656]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf t