{"level":30,"time":1776954328380,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015LuENtisrTiASoacJ1J8o6","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful review of the \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for Valley View Townhomes, here are the detailed observations corresponding to your questions:\n\n**1) Are there any overhead electrical conductors, poles, or lines visible on this sheet?**\nYes, there are overhead electrical lines indicated on the plan. \n*   Along the western (left) property boundary, there is a dashed line labeled with **\"- OHE -\"** (Overhead Electric). \n*   Similarly, along the southern (bottom) property boundary, there is another dashed line labeled with **\"- OHE -\"**.\n\n**2) Are there underground electrical lines shown?**\nYes, the proposed electrical design for the site relies heavily on underground lines. These are represented by solid blue lines throughout the property. \n*   There are specific labels pointing to these blue lines that read **\"Underground Electric Line\"** (e.g., one on the left side near Building 2, and another in the middle near Building 4).\n\n**3) What electrical infrastructure is present (transformers, pull boxes, meters)?**\nThe plan shows a network of electrical infrastructure utilizing the following specific components:\n*   **Transformers:** There are four rectangular pads denoted with standard symbol hatching, each labeled exactly as **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**. They are located:\n    *   Near the northwest corner of Building 2.\n    *   Near the southwest corner of Building 8.\n    *   Between Buildings 5 and 6 on the eastern side.\n    *   South of Building 6 near the eastern edge.\n*   **Pull Boxes:** There are multiple blue circular symbols with an 'E' inside, labeled exactly as **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**. These are placed at junction points or bends in the underground lines (e.g., at the northwest property corner, between Buildings 3 & 4, southeast of Building 7, and near the western tie-in point).\n*   **Meters:** Banks of meters are shown attached or adjacent to every building. They are represented by small clustered squares and are labeled exactly as **\"Electrical Meters\"**. For example, they are located on the west sides of Buildings 1 & 2, north sides of Buildings 3 & 4, east sides of Buildings 5 & 6, and south sides of Buildings 7 & 8.\n\n**4) Are there any clearance dimensions or zone markings shown around electrical equipment?**\nNo. While the pads, pull boxes, and meters are clearly drawn to a rough scale, there are no dashed boundary lines, hatched \"keep-out\" zones, or specific clearance dimension texts (e.g., \"10' minimum clearance\") marked around any of the transformers, pull boxes, or meters on this specific plan sheet.\n\n**5) Are there any overhead transmission structures or transmission easements marked on the plan?**\nNo. There are standard overhead distribution lines marked \"- OHE -\" and various standard utility easements (e.g., \"5' P.U.E.\", \"10' P.U.E.\", \"10' Drainage Easement\"), but there are no specific labels indicating high-voltage overhead \"transmission\" towers, structures, or dedicated transmission-level easements.\n\n**6) What is the routing of electrical lines relative to buildings and utilities?**\n*   **Origin:** The primary underground electrical feed appears to tie into the existing overhead line (\"- OHE -\") on the western property boundary, transitioning underground near a utility pole.\n*   **Pathing Relative to Buildings:** The blue \"Underground Electric Line\" routes form a perimeter loop around the main clusters of buildings. The lines generally run parallel to the outer facades of the buildings rather than cutting underneath them. For example, a line runs completely along the northern edge outside Buildings 1, 3, and 4; another runs along the southern edge outside Buildings 8 and 7; and another runs along the eastern edge near Buildings 5 and 6.\n*   **Pathing Relative to Utilities:** The electrical lines frequently cross other utility lines (labeled 'W' for Water, 'WW' for Wastewater, and 'SD' for Storm Drain). Most of these crossings occur in the alleyways, driveways, or outer easement areas. The plan shows the electrical lines crossing these other utilities roughly perpendicularly to reach the various transformer pads and pull boxes distributed around the site."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51587e83-ba72-4647-83cb-6d408affd332","uuid":"c172ec6f-3aec-4a65-ba45-ba41386c18ca","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful review of the \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for Valley View Townhomes, here are the detailed observations corresponding to your questions:\n\n**1) Are there any overhead electrical conductors, poles, or lines visible on this sheet?**\nYes, there are overhead electrical lines indicated on the plan. \n*   Along the western (left) property boundary, there is a dashed line labeled with **\"- OHE -\"** (Overhead Electric). \n*   Similarly, along the southern (bottom) property boundary, there is another dashed line labeled with **\"- OHE -\"**.\n\n**2) Are there underground electrical lines shown?**\nYes, the proposed electrical design for the site relies heavily on underground lines. These are represented by solid blue lines throughout the property. \n*   There are specific labels pointing to these blue lines that read **\"Underground Electric Line\"** (e.g., one on the left side near Building 2, and another in the middle near Building 4).\n\n**3) What electrical infrastructure is present (transformers, pull boxes, meters)?**\nThe plan shows a network of electrical infrastructure utilizing the following specific components:\n*   **Transformers:** There are four rectangular pads denoted with standard symbol hatching, each labeled exactly as **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**. They are located:\n    *   Near the northwest corner of Building 2.\n    *   Near the southwest corner of Building 8.\n    *   Between Buildings 5 and 6 on the eastern side.\n    *   South of Building 6 near the eastern edge.\n*   **Pull Boxes:** There are multiple blue circular symbols with an 'E' inside, labeled exactly as **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**. These are placed at junction points or bends in the underground lines (e.g., at the northwest property corner, between Buildings 3 & 4, southeast of Building 7, and near the western tie-in point).\n*   **Meters:** Banks of meters are shown attached or adjacent to every building. They are represented by small clustered squares and are labeled exactly as **\"Electrical Meters\"**. For example, they are located on the west sides of Buildings 1 & 2, north sides of Buildings 3 & 4, east sides of Buildings 5 & 6, and south sides of Buildings 7 & 8.\n\n**4) Are there any clearance dimensions or zone markings shown around electrical equipment?**\nNo. While the pads, pull boxes, and meters are clearly drawn to a rough scale, there are no dashed boundary lines, hatched \"keep-out\" zones, or specific clearance dimension texts (e.g., \"10' minimum clearance\") marked around any of the transformers, pull boxes, or meters on this specific plan sheet.\n\n**5) Are there any overhead transmission structures or transmission easements marked on the plan?**\nNo. There are standard overhead distribution lines marked \"- OHE -\" and various standard utility easements (e.g., \"5' P.U.E.\", \"10' P.U.E.\", \"10' Drainage Easement\"), but there are no specific labels indicating high-voltage overhead \"transmission\" towers, structures, or dedicated transmission-level easements.\n\n**6) What is the routing of electrical lines relative to buildings and utilities?**\n*   **Origin:** The primary underground electrical feed appears to tie into the existing overhead line (\"- OHE -\") on the western property boundary, transitioning underground near a utility pole.\n*   **Pathing Relative to Buildings:** The blue \"Underground Electric Line\" routes form a perimeter loop around the main clusters of buildings. The lines generally run parallel to the outer facades of the buildings rather than cutting underneath them. For example, a line runs completely along the northern edge outside Buildings 1, 3, and 4; another runs along the southern edge outside Buildings 8 and 7; and another runs along the eastern edge near Buildings 5 and 6.\n*   **Pathing Relative to Utilities:** The electrical lines frequently cross other utility lines (labeled 'W' for Water, 'WW' for Wastewater, and 'SD' for Storm Drain). Most of these crossings occur in the alleyways, driveways, or outer easement areas. The plan shows the electrical lines crossing these other utilities roughly perpendicularly to reach the various transformer pads and pull boxes distributed around the site."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1776954329516,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":3,"prompt":"Please examine Sheet 3 (General Notes) and identify ALL notes related to Austin Energy, electric utilities, or developer responsibilities for electrical infrastructure. Specifically, look for:\n\n1. The four required Standard Austin Energy Notes about (a) AE tree pruning rights, (b) owner/developer obligation to provide easements, (c) owner responsibility for erosion control near overhead lines, (d) owner responsibility for NESC clearances\n2. Any note stating the site is within the Austin Energy service area\n3. Any note about developer responsibility for designing/constructing conduit and related infrastructure to AE standards\n4. Any preconstruction meeting requirements\n5. Any transmission easement notes\n\nList the exact text of any notes found. If any expected notes are missing, clearly state that.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 3 (General Notes), here is the requested information regarding Austin Energy, electric utilities, and developer responsibilities:\n\n### 1. Standard Austin Energy Notes\nThe four required notes are present under the **\"Electric Notes\"** section in the middle-left column. (Note: These exact same notes are also duplicated in an unnumbered paragraph block directly below the \"Fire Department\" section in the middle column).\n\n*   **(a) AE tree pruning rights:**\n    > \"1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n*   **(b) Owner/developer obligation to provide easements:**\n    > \"2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n*   **(c) Owner responsibility for erosion control near overhead lines:**\n    > \"3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\"\n*   **(d) Owner responsibility for NESC clearances:**\n    > \"4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\"\n\n*(Note 5 under \"Electric Notes\" also states: \"5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\")*\n\n### 2. Note Stating the Site is within the Austin Energy Service Area\n**Missing.** There is no note on this sheet explicitly stating that the site is within the Austin Energy service area.\n\n### 3. Developer Responsibility for Designing/Constructing Conduit/Infrastructure to AE Standards\n**Missing.** There is no note on this sheet explicitly stating the developer's responsibility for designing or constructing conduit and related infrastructure to Austin Energy standards.\n\n### 4. Preconstruction Meeting Requirements\nFound under the **\"Electric Transmission Notes\"** section (middle column, top):\n\n> \"3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry ([text unclear, appears to be: 512 505-7151]) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n\n### 5. Transmission Easement Notes\nAn entire section titled **\"Electric Transmission Notes\"** is present at the top of the middle column. The exact text is as follows:\n\n> 1. No parking is permitted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\n> 2. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a meeting.\n> 3. *[See pre-construction meeting note quoted above in Section 4]*\n> 4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\n> 5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n> 6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\n> 7. Retaining walls, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\n> 8. 24 Hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\n> 9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\n> 10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning of electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n> 11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/powerlines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be rollover curbing.\n> 12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\n> 13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\n> 14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures.\n> 15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.\n> 16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n>     - any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.\n>     - any structure of any kind in such proximity to transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\n>     - any structures, including but not limited to: fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1466,"outputTokens":1475,"totalTokens":6466,"reasoningTokens":3525},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 3237656]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please examine Sheet 3 (General Notes) and identify ALL notes related to Austin Energy, electric utilities, or developer responsibilities for electrical infrastructure. Specifically, look for:\n\n1. The four required Standard Austin Energy Notes about (a) AE tree pruning rights, (b) owner/developer obligation to provide easements, (c) owner responsibility for erosion control near overhead lines, (d) owner responsibility for NESC clearances\n2. Any note stating the site is within the Austin Energy service area\n3. Any note about developer responsibility for designing/constructing conduit and related infrastructure to AE standards\n4. Any preconstruction meeting requirements\n5. Any transmission easement notes\n\nList the exact text of any notes found. If any expected notes are missing, clearly state that."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-n0VGozRlt0SGGamy3mVGeMjN","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 14:25:29 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::skjpn-1776954255456-e5483cf2fdb2"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 3 (General Notes), here is the requested information regarding Austin Energy, electric utilities, and developer responsibilities:\n\n### 1. Standard Austin Energy Notes\nThe four required notes are present under the **\"Electric Notes\"** section in the middle-left column. (Note: These exact same notes are also duplicated in an unnumbered paragraph block directly below the \"Fire Department\" section in the middle column).\n\n*   **(a) AE tree pruning rights:**\n    > \"1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n*   **(b) Owner/developer obligation to provide easements:**\n    > \"2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n*   **(c) Owner responsibility for erosion control near overhead lines:**\n    > \"3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\"\n*   **(d) Owner responsibility for NESC clearances:**\n    > \"4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\"\n\n*(Note 5 under \"Electric Notes\" also states: \"5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\")*\n\n### 2. Note Stating the Site is within the Austin Energy Service Area\n**Missing.** There is no note on this sheet explicitly stating that the site is within the Austin Energy service area.\n\n### 3. Developer Responsibility for Designing/Constructing Conduit/Infrastructure to AE Standards\n**Missing.** There is no note on this sheet explicitly stating the developer's responsibility for designing or constructing conduit and related infrastructure to Austin Energy standards.\n\n### 4. Preconstruction Meeting Requirements\nFound under the **\"Electric Transmission Notes\"** section (middle column, top):\n\n> \"3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry ([text unclear, appears to be: 512 505-7151]) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n\n### 5. Transmission Easement Notes\nAn entire section titled **\"Electric Transmission Notes\"** is present at the top of the middle column. The exact text is as follows:\n\n> 1. No parking is permitted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\n> 2. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a meeting.\n> 3. *[See pre-construction meeting note quoted above in Section 4]*\n> 4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\n> 5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n> 6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\n> 7. Retaining walls, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\n> 8. 24 Hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\n> 9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\n> 10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning of electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n> 11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/powerlines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be rollover curbing.\n> 12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\n> 13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\n> 14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures.\n> 15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.\n> 16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n>     - any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.\n>     - any structure of any kind in such proximity to transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\n>     - any structures, including but not limited to: fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1466,"outputTokens":1475,"totalTokens":6466,"reasoningTokens":3525},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","cred