nt of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a meeting.\n> 3. *[See pre-construction meeting note quoted above in Section 4]*\n> 4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\n> 5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n> 6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\n> 7. Retaining walls, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\n> 8. 24 Hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\n> 9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\n> 10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning of electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n> 11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/powerlines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be rollover curbing.\n> 12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\n> 13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\n> 14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures.\n> 15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.\n> 16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n>     - any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.\n>     - any structure of any kind in such proximity to transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\n>     - any structures, including but not limited to: fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1776954332582,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine this electrical site plan and provide the following information:\n1. Are there any transformer pads shown on the plan? If so, what is their location relative to buildings and are they labeled with dimensions or easement boundaries?\n2. How are underground electrical lines routed across the site? Do they cross under any buildings, parking areas, or near utility equipment?\n3. Are there any AE (Austin Energy) easements shown or noted on this electrical plan? Are they marked with boundary lines?\n4. Are there any utility lines routed in or around the detention pond area (NE corner)?\n5. What is the scale of this drawing and confirm the title/sheet number at the bottom?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided Preliminary Electrical Design Plan, here is the information requested:\n\n**1. Are there any transformer pads shown on the plan? If so, what is their location relative to buildings and are they labeled with dimensions or easement boundaries?**\n*   **Yes**, there are four transformer pads clearly shown and labeled as **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**.\n*   **Locations relative to buildings**:\n    *   One is located just west of **Bldg. 2** (near Unit 201).\n    *   One is located east of **Bldg. 4** and west of **Bldg. 5**.\n    *   One is located east of **Bldg. 7** and west of **Bldg. 6**.\n    *   One is located west of **Bldg. 8** (near Unit 801).\n*   **Dimensions/Easements**: None of the pads have specific numerical dimensions (e.g., 10'x10') explicitly written on them. They are depicted with a dashed square boundary around them. The pad near Bldg. 8 has an adjacent label pointing to a **\"Vault Easement\"**, but the other three pads do not have specific easement labels attached directly to their dashed boundaries.\n\n**2. How are underground electrical lines routed across the site? Do they cross under any buildings, parking areas, or near utility equipment?**\n*   **Routing**: The primary electrical routing is depicted by the solid blue lines. They originate from an **\"Underground Electric Line\"** on the far west side of the site (near the street/sidewalk easement), run eastward across the site, and branch off to various **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** locations, transformer pads, and finally to **\"Electrical Meters\"** attached to the buildings.\n*   **Under Buildings**: **No**. The electrical lines route around the perimeters of the building footprints and do not cross underneath them.\n*   **Under Parking/Drive Areas**: **Yes**. The lines frequently cross the central drive aisles and paved spaces located between the building blocks (e.g., the large central aisle running east-west between buildings 1/3 and 2/4/7/8).\n*   **Near Utility Equipment**: **Yes**, they connect directly to all major electrical utility equipment, including pull boxes, transformer pads, and building meters.\n\n**3. Are there any AE (Austin Energy) easements shown or noted on this electrical plan? Are they marked with boundary lines?**\n*   There are **no explicit labels specifically reading \"AE Easement\" or \"Austin Energy Easement\"** visible on this sheet.\n*   There are, however, several standard utility easements marked with dashed boundary lines, including:\n    *   **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement\"** running along the southern property boundary.\n    *   **\"Vault Easement\"** near the transformer pad for Bldg. 8.\n    *   Various **\"P.U.E.\"** (Public Utility Easement) notations, such as a **\"5' P.U.E.\"** near the northern boundary.\n\n**4. Are there any utility lines routed in or around the detention pond area (NE corner)?**\n*   In the northeast corner (north and east of **Bldg. 5**), there is an area enclosed by a **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"** with dropping contour lines (663 to 659), which is typical for a detention or drainage area.\n*   **Yes**, utility lines are routed *around* this area. Specifically, a blue electrical line runs north-south along the immediate eastern exterior wall of Bldg. 5 to service the **\"Electrical Meters\"** for those units. The lines appear to stay close to the building footprint and do not route directly through the center of the recessed drainage/retaining wall area. There are also storm drain (**\"- SD -\"**) lines routed in the vicinity just outside this corner.\n\n**5. What is the scale of this drawing and confirm the title/sheet number at the bottom?**\n*   **Scale**: The scale bar in the top right corner indicates **\"Scale 1\\\" = 20'\"**.\n*   **Title**: The title block in the bottom right corner labels the document as **\"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\"** for **\"Valley View Townhomes\"**.\n*   **Sheet Number**: The bottom right corner clearly states **\"Sheet: 21 of 39\"**.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1452,"outputTokens":955,"totalTokens":4642,"reasoningTokens":2235},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine this electrical site plan and provide the following information:\n1. Are there any transformer pads shown on the plan? If so, what is their location relative to buildings and are they labeled with dimensions or easement boundaries?\n2. How are underground electrical lines routed across the site? Do they cross under any buildings, parking areas, or near utility equipment?\n3. Are there any AE (Austin Energy) easements shown or noted on this electrical plan? Are they marked with boundary lines?\n4. Are there any utility lines routed in or around the detention pond area (NE corner)?\n5. What is the scale of this drawing and confirm the title/sheet number at the bottom?"}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-hWS98isHPTMAeQC5rCUcCd72","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 1