{"level":30,"time":1776954335651,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine this electrical design plan and identify: 1) Whether there are any overhead electric conductors, service drops, poles, or transmission lines shown on the site. 2) The locations of all underground electric infrastructure (conduits, transformers, pull boxes, meters). 3) Whether any utility lines cross or pass through the site. 4) Any AE (Austin Energy) easements or equipment locations marked. 5) Whether clearance dimensions are shown from any buildings or structures to underground electrical conduit. Describe the routing of underground electrical lines and their proximity to buildings and other utilities.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet SP-2025-0126C), here are the details regarding your requested criteria:\n\n**1) Overhead Electric Infrastructure**\n*   **Overhead Lines:** Yes, overhead electric lines are shown off-site. On the far left (western) edge of the drawing, outside the main bold property boundary line (along what appears to be a street right-of-way), there is a dashed line repeatedly labeled exactly as \"**OHE**\".\n*   **Service Drops, Poles, Transmission Lines:** There are no obvious pole symbols explicitly labeled, nor are there any overhead service drops routing *into* the site. The electrical service enters the site underground. There are no overhead lines shown within the site's property boundary.\n\n**2) Locations of Underground Electric Infrastructure**\nUnderground electrical infrastructure is denoted by solid blue lines and blue callout boxes.\n*   **Underground Line Entry:** An \"**Underground Electric Line**\" enters the property from the west (mid-way down the western boundary) and connects immediately to an \"**Electrical Pull Box**\".\n*   **Electrical Transformer Pads:** There are two main transformer locations shown:\n    1.  One \"**Electrical Transformer Pad**\" is located on the western side of the site, situated between the property line and the gap between Bldg. 1 and Bldg. 2.\n    2.  A second \"**Electrical Transformer Pad**\" is located in the southwestern quadrant of the site, west of Bldg. 8.\n*   **Electrical Pull Boxes:** Several pull boxes are identified throughout the routing loop:\n    *   Near the western entry point.\n    *   Northwest corner (north of the northern transformer).\n    *   Northeast area (north of Bldg. 3).\n    *   East area (between Bldg. 3 and Bldg. 5).\n    *   Southwest area (south of the entry pull box, leading to the southern transformer).\n    *   Southeast area (south of Bldg. 7).\n    *   East area (south of Bldg. 6).\n*   **Electrical Meters:** Meter locations are called out with boxes pointing directly to the building footprints. Exactly transcribed labels \"**Electrical Meters**\" point to locations on:\n    *   Bldg. 1 (west side)\n    *   Bldg. 2 (west side)\n    *   Bldg. 3 (north side)\n    *   Bldg. 5 (west side)\n    *   Bldg. 6 (south side)\n    *   Bldg. 7 (south side)\n    *   Bldg. 8 (west side)\n\n**3) Utility Lines Crossing or Passing Through the Site**\n*   Various utility lines route extensively *through* the site to serve the proposed buildings, including lines labeled \"**W**\" (Water), \"**WW**\" (Wastewater), and \"**SD**\" (Storm Drain). These lines weave between all the building footprints.\n*   There are no obvious major third-party utility transmission corridors shown crossing through the property without serving it.\n\n**4) AE (Austin Energy) Easements or Equipment Locations**\n*   There are no explicit markings, labels, or callouts that use the specific abbreviation \"AE\" or the words \"Austin Energy\" on any equipment or easements within this drawing.\n*   There are general easements noted off-site to the south (e.g., transcribed exactly: \"**Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 \\ Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.**\" and \"**5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 885 D.R.T.C.Tx.**\"), but no specific utility provider is named on the plan graphics.\n\n**5) Clearance Dimensions & Routing Description**\n*   **Clearance Dimensions:** There are **no clearance dimensions** explicitly shown indicating the required offset distance from the buildings or structures to the underground electrical conduit.\n*   **Routing Description & Proximity:** The underground electrical system (blue line) branches into a north and south loop from the initial western entry point.\n    *   *Proximity to Buildings:* The conduits run very close to the building footprints, running parallel to the exterior walls to reach the meter banks. For example, the line runs tightly along the north exterior wall of Bldg. 1 and Bldg. 3, and along the south exterior wall of Bldg. 8 and Bldg. 7.\n    *   *Proximity to Utilities:* The electrical lines cross and run parallel to other utilities frequently. For example, the electrical line running east along the north side of Bldg. 1 and Bldg. 3 runs parallel and in very close proximity to a Water (\"W\") line. The electrical line routing south of Bldg. 7 crosses perpendicularly over Wastewater (\"WW\") and Storm Drain (\"SD\") lines.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1429,"outputTokens":1061,"totalTokens":5085,"reasoningTokens":2595},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine this electrical design plan and identify: 1) Whether there are any overhead electric conductors, service drops, poles, or transmission lines shown on the site. 2) The locations of all underground electric infrastructure (conduits, transformers, pull boxes, meters). 3) Whether any utility lines cross or pass through the site. 4) Any AE (Austin Energy) easements or equipment locations marked. 5) Whether clearance dimensions are shown from any buildings or structures to underground electrical conduit. Describe the routing of underground electrical lines and their proximity to buildings and other utilities."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-HKQpsbvVhkhs5eX3th5k49M2","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming