{"level":30,"time":1776954337502,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":1,"prompt":"Please examine Sheet 1 (Cover Sheet) and identify:\n\n1. Is there an \"Additional Review Acknowledgement\" table that lists external approvals/permits (TxDOT, railroad, gas company, TCEQ, water districts, easement acquisition, county approval, Planning and Development Review Department approvals, Austin Energy approvals, AULCC clearance, etc.)?\n2. If present, what external reviews/approvals are listed as completed, pending, or N/A?\n3. Is there any indication of Austin Energy approval or clearance?\n4. Are there any notes about street lighting or traffic signal coordination?\n\nPlease provide exact text or note if the table is missing.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (1)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776954340081,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Please analyze the site plan and identify: (1) The routing of underground utility lines relative to the proposed detention/biofiltration pond shown in the northeast corner. (2) The location of any overhead utility lines or electric poles (existing or proposed) and their proximity to buildings. (3) The existence and location of utility easements shown on the site plan (including electric, water, wastewater, drainage easements). (4) Identify any parking areas and whether utilities are routed through or under parking spaces. (5) Note the presence of any street trees in the right-of-way along Valley View Road frontage.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here is the information requested:\n\n**1. Routing of underground utility lines relative to the proposed detention/biofiltration pond (northeast corner)**\n*   The \"Detention/Biofiltration Pond\" is located in the northeast corner of the site, bounded by a \"Concrete Retaining Wall\" and a \"Pond Perimeter Fence.\"\n*   A Storm Drain line (labeled **\"- SD -\"**) routes from the interior of the site (originating from an inlet/manhole between Bldg. 3 and Bldg. 4) heading northeast toward the pond area. It terminates at a square structure located just outside the southwestern corner of the pond's retaining wall.\n*   Another Storm Drain line (labeled **\"- SD -\"**) runs east-west along the northern property boundary line, passing just north of the pond perimeter fence.\n*   Water (**\"- W -\"**) and Wastewater (**\"- WW -\"**) lines are routed longitudinally down the central north-south drive aisle of the property and do not appear to route toward or interact with the northeast detention pond area.\n\n**2. Location of overhead utility lines or electric poles and their proximity to buildings**\n*   **Western Boundary (Valley View Road):** An overhead line (labeled **\"- OHE -\"**) runs north-south along the western property boundary. Pole symbols are visible, including one labeled **\"Exist. Guy Pole\"** near the northwest corner driveway entrance and another labeled **\"AT&T Pole\"** nearby. These lines run parallel to Building 1 and Building 8, separated by the sidewalk and driveway areas.\n*   **Southern Boundary:** An overhead line (labeled **\"- OHE -\"**) runs east-west closely tracking the southern property line, situated behind a proposed retaining wall. Several circular symbols designated simply as **\"Pole\"** are spaced along this line. This line runs in close proximity to the southern facades of Building 8, Building 7, and the unit labeled 804.\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** An overhead line (labeled **\"- OHE -\"**) runs north-south along the eastern property line. It passes adjacent to Building 5 and Building 6.\n*   *Note:* Based on the linework, the overhead lines appear to run along the perimeter property boundaries and do not cross directly over proposed building footprints.\n\n**3. Existence and location of utility easements**\nThe site plan explicitly labels several utility easements across the property. Note that some document numbers are partially illegible due to resolution.\n*   **Wastewater:** Located in the northwest corner near the street connection. Labeled exactly as: **\"Wastewater Easement Doc# [unclear]\"**. Another pointing to a large vault area is also labeled **\"Wastewater Easement Doc# [unclear]\"**.\n*   **Combined Utilities:** Located in the southwest area between the driveway and Building 8. Labeled exactly as: **\"15' Exclusive Water, Wastewater, and Electric Line Vault Easement Doc# [unclear]\"**.\n*   **Drainage:**\n    *   Northeast corner, east of the pond: Labeled exactly as **\"25' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n    *   Eastern boundary, near Building 5: Labeled exactly as **\"25' Drainage Easement Doc# 2010021137 O.P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n    *   Southeast corner: Labeled exactly as **\"25' Drainage Easement Doc# [unclear]\"**.\n*   **Electric:** Located on the eastern boundary near Building 6. Labeled exactly as **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   **Public Utility Easement (P.U.E.):** Located along the northern boundary line. Labeled exactly as **\"5' P.U.E. Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   *(While not explicitly utilities, multiple **\"Sidewalk Easement Doc# [unclear]\"** labels exist along the western Valley View Rd frontage).*\n\n**4. Parking areas and whether utilities are routed through or under parking spaces**\n*   **Location of Parking:** As noted in the \"Parking Data\" table, there are \"40 Surface / 28 Garage\" spaces. The surface parking spaces are distributed along the central interior north-south drive aisles (between Buildings 1/8 and 2/5, and between 2/5 and 3/4).\n*   **Utility Routing in Parking Areas:** Major underground utility mains (Water labeled **\"- W -\"** and Wastewater labeled **\"- WW -\"**) run longitudinally straight down the center of the interior drive aisles. Based on the drawing, these main lines appear to run beneath the driving lane rather than directly underneath the marked surface parking stalls, though they run immediately adjacent to the parking bays. A Storm Drain line (**\"- SD -\"**) crosses the drive aisle perpendicularly between Buildings 2/5 and 3/4.\n\n**5. Presence of any street trees in the right-of-way along Valley View Road frontage**\n*   Tree symbols (circular graphics) are present along the western property frontage adjacent to Valley View Road, located between the proposed \"Concrete Sidewalk\" and the buildings.\n*   There is a specific callout near the northwest transformer pad pointing to a square graphic that reads exactly: **\"Tree Well need to look up approp. detail\"**.\n*   However, specific details regarding the trees are not provided on this specific sheet. A \"Tree List\" table located in the bottom left corner states exactly: **\"Refer to landscape plan sheet 20 for the tree list.\"**","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1434,"outputTokens":1261,"totalTokens":5113,"reasoningTokens":2418},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please analyze the site plan and identify: (1) The routing of underground utility lines relative to the proposed detention/biofiltration pond shown in the northeast corner. (2) The location of any overhead uti