{"level":30,"time":1776954353686,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011frrvZmnU6j4Lx4TKmQzKJ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Electric Review\n     2→\n     3→*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n     4→\n     5→Electric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n     6→\n     7→See Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\n     8→Link: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\n     9→Applicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n    10→\n    11→Site Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\n    12→Austin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n    13→* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n    14→* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n    15→* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n    16→* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n    17→* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n    18→* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n    19→* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n    20→* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n    21→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7a2037a-f555-4152-8bdc-44008e269230","uuid":"224027ad-b134-4a19-9e35-a19e21ba6200","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md","content":"# Electric Review\n\n*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n\nElectric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n\nSee Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\nLink: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\nApplicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n\nSite Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\nAustin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776954355550,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":1,"prompt":"Please examine Sheet 1 (Cover Sheet) and identify:\n\n1. Is there an \"Additional Review Acknowledgement\" table that lists external approvals/permits (TxDOT, railroad, gas company, TCEQ, water districts, easement acquisition, county approval, Planning and Development Review Department approvals, Austin Energy approvals, AULCC clearance, etc.)?\n2. If present, what external reviews/approvals are listed as completed, pending, or N/A?\n3. Is there any indication of Austin Energy approval or clearance?\n4. Are there any notes about street lighting or traffic signal coordination?\n\nPlease provide exact text or note if the table is missing.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful examination of Sheet 1 (Cover Sheet), here are the findings regarding your requests:\n\n**1 & 2. Additional Review Acknowledgement Table / External Reviews Status**\nThere is **no** \"Additional Review Acknowledgement\" table on this cover sheet. Consequently, there is no list indicating completed, pending, or N/A statuses for external approvals such as TxDOT, railroad, gas company, TCEQ, water districts, etc.\n\n**3. Austin Energy Approval or Clearance**\nThere is **no indication** of Austin Energy approval or clearance on this sheet. The \"Reviewed By:\" section on the right side of the page provides signature lines only for the following departments:\n*   Development Services Department\n*   City of Austin Fire Department\n*   Austin Water\n\n**4. Street Lighting or Traffic Signal Coordination Notes**\nThere are **no notes** specifically mentioning street lighting or traffic signal coordination. \n\n*(Note: There is a related \"Traffic Control Plan Note\" regarding temporary traffic control during construction, but it does not specify permanent traffic signals or street lighting. For completeness, it reads exactly as follows:)*\n> **Traffic Control Plan Note:**\n> This note is being placed on the plan set in the absence of a temporary traffic control plan (TCP) with the full understanding that an engineered TCP shall be reviewed and approved by the Right of Way Management Division. Furthermore, a TCP shall be submitted to TCPReview@austintexas.gov for review a minimum of 6 weeks prior to the start of construction. The applicant/project representative further recognizes that a TCP review fee is required for the initial review and all re-reviews, as prescribed by the most current version of the City's fee ordinance.\n> \n> The following must be taken into consideration:\n> - Refer to the 'Mobility Guidelines' for developing traffic control strategies\n>   http://www.austintexas.gov/page/mobility-guidelines\n> - TCPs shall not be approved without an approved site plan, site plan exemption, or general permit.\n> - A traffic control plan is not a permit.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1449,"outputTokens":435,"totalTokens":3294,"reasoningTokens":1410},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2370268]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to 