{"level":30,"time":1776954356309,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01PTB4V3auGY1gxB7jmY55hp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! Now I have detailed information from the vision analysis. Let me summarize the key findings:\n\n**Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21):**\n1. Four transformer pads identified:\n   - Pads 1 and 2 on western boundary (with \"Vault Easement\" labels)\n   - Pads 3 and 4 internally located (no easement shown)\n2. No Austin Energy coordination, truck access requirements, or AE-specific easement annotations\n3. NO clearance zones or setback requirements marked\n4. Underground electric lines routing across drive aisles to reach pads\n\n**Site Plan (Sheet 9):**\n1. Storm drain lines approaching the pond area (northeast corner)\n2. Multiple overhead electric lines (— OHE —) along property boundaries\n3. Multiple utility easements shown (drainage, water, wastewater, electric)\n4. Surface parking spaces in central drive aisles\n5. Tree wells mentioned but details referenced to landscape sheet\n\nNow let me check if this site is subject to Table B connectivity measures by checking whether it has >3 acres and nonresidential zoning, or has surface parking between building and principal street. Based on facts.md:\n- Zoning: MF-2 (residential)\n- Site area: 2.16 acres (less than 3 acres)\n- This site is NOT subject to Table B requirements - Table B only applies to nonresidential zones with 3+ acres, or surface parking between building and principal street\n\nKey deficiency patterns I need to check for:\n1. **EL-2.1 through EL-2.8:** Utility undergrounding requirements - NOT APPLICABLE because:\n   - Not a CTC (Valley View is local street, not listed)\n   - Not within Subchapter E Urban Roadway boundary\n   - Not in Plaza Saltillo TOD\n   - Not in NBG district\n   - MF-2 zoning (residential)\n\n2. **EL-2.2:** Hill Country Roadway Corridor - Need to check if within 1,000 feet of Loop 360, RM 620, RM 2222, RM 2244, or Southwest Parkway\n\n3. **EL-2.9:** 10-foot overhead utility zone - Only applies if overhead utilities remain on CTC, Urban Roadway, Plaza Saltillo TOD, or NBG sites. Since this site doesn't qualify under those categories, this doesn't apply.\n\n4. **EL-2.10:** Utilities routed under ponds - YES, the storm drain line appears to route near the detention pond area, but I need to verify if it's actually UNDER the pond or just adjacent\n\n5. **EL-2.11 & EL-2.12:** Austin Water in planting zones - Should review the landscape plan to confirm any ROW planting zones\n\n6. **EL-2.13:** Transformers in parkland - Need to determine if transformer pads fall within parkland boundaries (the site is in a parkland deficient area, which differs from having actual dedicated parkland on-site)\n\n7. **EL-2.14:** Light rail coordination - Should verify proximity to light rail\n\n8. **EL-2.15:** Easement encroaching into ROW - Need to cross-reference the plat and easements against ROW boundaries\n\n9. **EL-2.16:** Items within easement not licensed - Should check whether structures, paving, or landscaping exist within easements without proper licensing\n\n10. **EL-2.17:** Private utilities in public ROW - Need to verify if any private utilities appear in the ROW. **EL-2.18 & EL-2.19:** Abandoned and public utilities - Should review demolition plans to confirm removal. **EL-2.20:** Underground storage tanks are confirmed as absent per facts.md. **EL-2.21:** Power pole relocation - Need to check if poles are being moved. **EL-2.22:** Transformer pad clearances and easement - No clearance requirements or AE easement annotations on Sheet 21; need to verify ownership status. **EL-2.23:** Tree wells with electrical outlets - Should review landscape plan. **EL-2.24:** Utilities in parking - MF-2 zoning is residential, so this requirement doesn't apply.\n\nNow checking Hill Country Roadway status and reviewing additional details.\n\nThe site is actually on Valley View Road, not Hill Country Roadway. Looking at the documents, the main concerns are: Sheet 21 lacks Austin Energy easements and clearances for transformer pads, no truck access or AE coordination requirements are shown, and while vision analysis labels mention \"Vault Easement,\" there's no reference to AE easements. Need to examine the demolition plan more closely for abandoned utility removal and continue checking for other potential violations.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3110,"cache_read_input_tokens":56799,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3110},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5916cd46-093b-4cec-ae5c-02d81ed2e2c9","uuid":"855032e4-cc81-4ab0-9249-e3294687de0c"}
