d consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7a2037a-f555-4152-8bdc-44008e269230","uuid":"76071a82-0cb4-4518-a5ff-5a299da10100","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/completeness-check-results/overview.md","content":"# Completeness Check Results\n\nCity of Austin site plan completeness check results detailing reviewer statuses and applicant responses to deficiencies.\n\n## Sections\n\n1. **Project Information and Review Status** (p. 1)\n   Provides general project details, tracking numbers, and a summary table of completeness statuses for various city reviewers.\n   File: `01-project-information-and-review-status.md`\n2. **Drainage and Water Quality Review** (pp. 2-3)\n   Comments from the drainage reviewer regarding storm drain connectivity and off-site runoff, along with the applicant's responses and information-only notes.\n   File: `02-drainage-and-water-quality-review.md`\n3. **City Arborist Review** (p. 3)\n   Informational comments from the City Arborist regarding the proposed removal of a 25-inch Heritage Live Oak tree and variance requirements.\n   File: `03-city-arborist-review.md`\n4. **Land Development Engineering Review** (pp. 3-4)\n   Informational requirements for License Agreements, Encroachment Agreements, Easement Releases, and ROW Vacations.\n   File: `04-land-development-engineering-review.md`\n5. **ATD Review** (p. 4)\n   Comments from the transportation department requesting dimensions and details for driveways and behind-the-curb improvements, along with applicant responses.\n   File: `05-atd-review.md`\n6. **Austin Energy Review** 