{"level":30,"time":1776954388286,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01J8wiH6A7RXENCGPaPPbc9m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013RMpGjkeLodm4nr9pqMj9t","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":552,"cache_read_input_tokens":63953,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":552},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7a2037a-f555-4152-8bdc-44008e269230","uuid":"f24884cd-da83-45df-9426-490822a446d4"}
{"level":30,"time":1776954388301,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013RMpGjkeLodm4nr9pqMj9t","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Transportation & Public Works (TPW-TDS) Review\n     2→\n     3→*Details requirements related to parking, street impact fees, right-of-way, driveways, and trash collection.*\n     4→\n     5→TPW-TDS Review – Suzy Riley (512) 974-4073 - suzanne.riley@austintexas.gov\n     6→\n     7→GENERAL COMMENTS\n     8→Please show the property line on the site plan.\n     9→U1: Comment cleared.\n    10→\n    11→SIF COMMENTS \n    12→TPW 1: Comment Status: Cleared\n    13→* U0: Please add the following note to the coversheet: Development of structures that require a building permit within this Site Plan, or revisions thereof, are required to comply with the City of Austin Street Impact Fee Ordinances, as applicable, and must be paid upon completion of the building permit plan review for each building. \n    14→Reference: LDC 25-6-662\n    15→* U0: Comment cleared.\n    16→\n    17→TPW 2: Comment Status: Pending\n    18→* U0: FYI: The Building Permits for this site are required to comply with the City’s Street Impact Fee. The fee was adopted by City Council in December 2020 and is applicable to all Building Permits submitted on or after June 22, 2022. (For more information: https://www.austintexas.gov/department/street-impact-fee). Please complete a copy of the SIF worksheet: https://atd.knack.com/development-services#customer-portal/services/street-impact-fee-worksheet/ This development may be eligible for SIF offsets if off-site transportation mitigations are included with the site plan. Please inform this reviewer if you would like these options pursued.\n    19→* Comment remains. Continue to work with area engineer, Mustafa Wali (Mustafa.Wali@austintexas.gov) to complete.\n    20→\n    21→PARKING\n    22→TPW 3: Comment Status: Cleared\n    23→* U0: Include a table showing the proposed land uses, the floor area in square feet for each land use, the parking ratio, the number of parking spaces required by type, and the number of parking spaces proposed by type (standard, compact, handicapped, short-term and long-term bicycle, loading, etc.). The amount required per Appendix A is necessary for the calculation of required accessible parking and long and short-term bike parking.\n    24→Reference: LDC 25-6-472, Appendix A.\n    25→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    26→\n    27→TPW 4: Comment Status: Cleared\n    28→* U0: All parking must be provided in accordance with design and construction standards of the TCM. Show dimensions for garage parking within townhomes. Reference: TCM Table 9-1, Table 9-2, and Table 9-3.\n    29→* U1: Comment cleared. \n    30→\n    31→TPW 5: Comment Status: Cleared\n    32→* U0: Traffic control signs and marking used in parking areas, except for structured parking garages, must conform to the latest edition of the Texas Manual for Uniform Traffic Control Devices (TMUTCD). Reference: TCM, 9.3.2.T.\n    33→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    34→\n    35→TPW 6: Comment Status: Cleared\n    36→* U0: Approval of the Transportation & Public Works Department (TPW) is required in order to place parking within the right-of-way. Is the intention to keep the existing on-street parking indicated on the site plan?\n    37→Reference: TCM, 2.7.1.3.G.\n    38→U1: Comment cleared. \n    39→\n    40→TPW 7: Comment Status: Cleared\n    41→* U0: Where on-street parking is desired without adequate right-of-way, a dedication of right-of-way shall be required. Please confirm the current ROW can accommodate on-street parking, refer to Level 1 cross-section - TCM, Figure 2-15. Reference: TCM, 9.2.0.A.\n    42→\n    43→[Figure: Diagram of a Level 1 58' ROW street cross-section showing parallel parking, sidewalks, and street trees]\n    44→\n    45→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    46→\n    47→TPW 8: Comment Status: Cleared\n    48→* U0: Parallel parking shall be the default configuration of all on-street parking. Back-in angled parking must be approved by the City Transportation Engineer or applicable Director. Head-in angled parking is prohibited as an on-street parking type. \n    49→Reference: TCM, 9.2.1.\n    50→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    51→\n    52→TPW 9: Comment Status: Cleared\n    53→* U0: On-street parallel parking stalls width shall be measured from the edge of the traveled way to the face of curb. The combination of travel and parking stall next to one another shall be no less than 18 ft. In areas adjacent to transit routes, the minimum shall be 19 ft. Parking is assumed to be 8 ft in width. Dimension the stall width and the width of lane on the site plan. Reference: TCM 9.2.2.A.\n    54→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    55→\n    56→TPW 10: Comment Status: Cleared\n    57→* U0: Individual on-street parallel parking stall lengths shall be 20 ft in length. Dimension the parking stall length on the site plan.\n    58→Reference: TCM 9.2.2.C.\n    59→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    60→\n    61→TPW 11: Comment Status: Cleared\n    62→* U0: A minimum 3 ft buffer shall be provided between the edge of parallel on-street parking and a bike lane to ensure that opening car doors will not encroach on the protected bike lane. Dimension this buffer on the site plan. \n    63→Reference: TCM 9.2.3.2.A.\n    64→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    65→\n    66→TPW 12: Comment Status: Cleared\n    67→* U0: A 1.5 ft offset from the curbside of an on-street parking stall shall be provided to all obstructions such as parking meters, poles, trees, etc. Show all obstructions on the site plan and dimension the offset.\n    68→Reference: TCM 9.2.3.1.A.\n    69→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    70→\n    71→TPW 13: Comment Status: Cleared\n    72→* U0: On-street parking is prohibited within 15 ft of either side of fire hydrants. Dimension the distance between the on-street parking and the fire hydrant. \n    73→Reference: TCM 9.2.3.1.B. TCM Figure 9-2.\n    74→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    75→\n    76→BICYCLE PARKING \n    77→TPW 14: Comment Status: Cleared\n    78→* U0: Identify the location of bicycle parking on the site plan, note the number of short-term and long-term spaces to be provided, show the direct unobstructed path connecting bicycle parking to the development entrance, and show a detail of the bicycle rack(s) (City of Austin standard detail #710S-1 or S-2, and 710S-6C, approved 2012). The minimum bicycle parking requirement is as follows: two spaces for Commercial Uses, five spaces for Multifamily Residential Use, and one space for Industrial, Civic, and Agricultural Uses, or 10 percent of the proposed motor vehicle parking spaces, whichever is greater. \n    79→Reference: LDC 25-6-477, Appendix A. TCM, 9.8.1.\n    80→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    81→\n    82→TPW 15: Comment Status: Cleared\n    83→* U0: Short and long-term bicycle parking ratios must be provided in accordance with the TCM. Reference TCM Table 9-6 for the ratio of short-term and long-term bicycle parking spaces by land use. Residential land use requires 30% to 50% short-term bicycle parking and 50% to 70% long-term bicycle parking. Can assume long-term bike parking will be provided within individual garages. Please include this in the parking table. Reference: TCM, 9.8.0.\n    84→* Comment cleared. \n    85→\n    86→TPW 16: Comment Status: Cleared\n    87→* U0: U-rack shall be used for short-term bicycle parking. \n    88→Reference: TCM, 9.8.5.A.\n    89→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    90→\n    91→TPW 17: Comment Status: Cleared\n    92→* U0: Bicycle parking must be located in a well-lit area. \n    93→Reference: TCM 9.8.1.I.\n    94→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    95→\n    96→TPW 18: Comment Status: Pending\n    97→* U0: Provide enough space between bike rack locations to adequately accommodate a bicycle locked in every spot. One “U” rack provides two bicycle parking spots. Dimension the bicycle parking spaces on the site plan. The standard required bicycle space is 2 feet wide, 6 feet long, and 3 feet 4 inches tall. If larger styles of bicycles such as cargo or electric bicycles are anticipated, the design shall accommodate the footprint of these bicycles as the design bicycle (up to 3 ft wide by 10 ft long).\n    98→Reference: TCM Figure 9-14. and/or TCM, 9.8.1.\n    99→* U1: Comment remains. Please include COA standard detail 710S-6C.\n   100→\n   101→FRONTAGE REQUIREMENTS\n   102→TPW 19: Comment Status: Pending\n   103→* U0: The ASMP identifies Valley View Rd as a Level 1 street with 58-foor cross section. Back of curb infrastructure must be designed in accordance with the Transportation Criteria Manual and includes: A 7’ tree and furniture (planting) zone, measured from the back of curb is required. This is to be followed by a 5’ minimum clear zone (sidewalk) and a min. 2’ buffer zone between the building/property line. TCM 2.8.2.2\n   104→\n   105→[Figure: Cross-section diagram showing 7' tree and furniture zone and 5' sidewalk]\n   106→\n   107→* U1: Comment remains. Waiver request approved, please pay waiver fee. Please ensure sidewalk meets TCM 4.1.3, “Meandering paths should avoid sharp turns or transitions and gradually transition no more than 1 ft. off path per 5 ft. of sidewalk length and maintain a straight section no less than the width of the sidewalk between transitions.”\n   108→\n   109→TPW 20: Comment Status: Pending\n   110→* U0: A sidewalk easement is required if the public sidewalk enters onto private property. Provide an additional two feet within the easement for maintenance purposes. (Determine if the sidewalk easement requires maintenance (i.e. “with maintenance”). Otherwise add 2-additional feet). \n   111→Reference: TCM, 4.1.1, 4.1.2.\n   112→* U1: Comment remains. Pending resolution of sidewalk location. When resolved, please submit draft sidewalk easement directly to this reviewer for routing through city legal. \n   113→\n   114→DRIVEWAYS\n   115→TPW 21: Comment Status: Cleared\n   116→* U0: Driveways depicted on site plan do not match the required Type II driveway as the sidewalk crosses within the flare. Please revise.\n   117→* U1: Comment cleared.\n   118→\n   119→TPW 22: Comment Status: Cleared\n   120→* U0: All sidewalk and bicycle lane crossings of driveways shall maintain the elevation of the sidewalk and bicycle lane in a raised crossing. \n   121→Reference: TCM, 7.5.2.1.C\n   122→* U1: Comment cleared.\n   123→\n   124→TPW 23: Comment Status: Pending\n   125→* U0: Maximum number of driveways permitted on a street with 231 feet frontage is 1. Please revise. \n   126→Reference: TCM, Table 7-4\n   127→* U1: Comment remains. Pending review by area engineers. Response will be sent via email.\n   128→\n   129→THROAT LENGTH\n   130→TPW 24: Comment Status: Cleared\n   131→* U0: For multifamily or commercial sites with <25 parking spaces, minimum throat storage length is 25’ measured from property boundary to the first interruption point. For multifamily or commercial sites with 25-100 parking spaces, minimum throat storage length is 25’ or 40’ min. If left turns are permitted. Please provide total number of parking spaces to establish required throat length.\n   132→Reference: TCM, Table 9-5\n   133→* U1: Comment cleared.\n   134→\n   135→MISCELLANEOUS\n   136→TPW 25: Comment Status: Pending\n   137→* U0: Trash dumpsters must be located to provide adequate access and maneuverability for service vehicles. Show the dumpster.\n   138→Reference: LDC 25-2-1067(c); TCM, 9.3.0.2\n   139→* U1: Comment remains. Please confirm the collection point for the individual trash cans. Will these be collected at each unit or will there be a central collection point for the roll-out bins. Please identify this collection point on the site plan. Trash bins cannot be left within the ROW.\n   140→\n   141→TPW 26: Comment Status: Cleared\n   142→* U0: If roll-out bins are being proposed, then add the following notes to site plan sheet: \n   143→* Trash containers shall not be left at curb side unattended. Signs must be posted on the building or at a location that is publicly visible indicating that trash containers may not be left at curbside. The sign shall indicate the City of Austin’s Code enforcement phone number for the public to report violations. \n   144→* A restrictive covenant may be required for enforcement purposes. \n   145→Reference: TCM, 9.4.2.\n   146→* U1: Comment cleared.\n   147→\n   148→TPW 27: Comment Status: Pending\n   149→* U0: Service commitment from a commercial trash service must be provided indicating they can provide service. The letter should address the minimum clearance requirement for the service vehicles. \n   150→* U1: Comment remains.\n   151→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7a2037a-f555-4152-8bdc-44008e269230","uuid":"e3c50b90-aab0-4f6b-a021-5318f137dedf","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md","content":"# Transportation & Public Works (TPW-TDS) Review\n\n*Details requirements related to parking, street impact fees, right-of-way, driveways, and trash collection.*\n\nTPW-TDS Review – Suzy Riley (512) 974-4073 - suzanne.riley@austintexas.gov\n\nGENERAL COMMENTS\nPlease show the property line on the site plan.\nU1: Comment cleared.\n\nSIF COMMENTS \nTPW 1: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Please add the following note to the coversheet: Development of structures that require a building permit within this Site Plan, or revisions thereof, are required to comply with the City of Austin Street Impact Fee Ordinances, as applicable, and must be paid upon completion of the building permit plan review for each building. \nReference: LDC 25-6-662\n* U0: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 2: Comment Status: Pending\n* U0: FYI: The Building Permits for this site are required to comply with the City’s Street Impact Fee. The fee was adopted by City Council in December 2020 and is applicable to all Building Permits submitted on or after June 22, 2022. (For more information: https://www.austintexas.gov/department/street-impact-fee). Please complete a copy of the SIF worksheet: https://atd.knack.com/development-services#customer-portal/services/street-impact-fee-worksheet/ This development may be eligible for SIF offsets if off-site transportation mitigations are included with the site plan. Please inform this reviewer if you would like these options pursued.\n* Comment remains. Continue to work with area engineer, Mustafa Wali (Mustafa.Wali@austintexas.gov) to complete.\n\nPARKING\nTPW 3: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Include a table showing the proposed land uses, the floor area in square feet for each land use, the parking ratio, the number of parking spaces required by type, and the number of parking spaces proposed by type (standard, compact, handicapped, short-term and long-term bicycle, loading, etc.). The amount required per Appendix A is necessary for the calculation of required accessible parking and long and short-term bike parking.\nReference: LDC 25-6-472, Appendix A.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 4: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: All parking must be provided in accordance with design and construction standards of the TCM. Show dimensions for garage parking within townhomes. Reference: TCM Table 9-1, Table 9-2, and Table 9-3.\n* U1: Comment cleared. \n\nTPW 5: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Traffic control signs and marking used in parking areas, except for structured parking garages, must conform to the latest edition of the Texas Manual for Uniform Traffic Control Devices (TMUTCD). Reference: TCM, 9.3.2.T.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 6: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Approval of the Transportation & Public Works Department (TPW) is required in order to place parking within the right-of-way. Is the intention to keep the existing on-street parking indicated on the site plan?\nReference: TCM, 2.7.1.3.G.\nU1: Comment cleared. \n\nTPW 7: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Where on-street parking is desired without adequate right-of-way, a dedication of right-of-way shall be required. Please confirm the current ROW can accommodate on-street parking, refer to Level 1 cross-section - TCM, Figure 2-15. Reference: TCM, 9.2.0.A.\n\n[Figure: Diagram of a Level 1 58' ROW street cross-section showing parallel parking, sidewalks, and street trees]\n\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 8: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Parallel parking shall be the default configuration of all on-street parking. Back-in angled parking must be approved by the City Transportation Engineer or applicable Director. Head-in angled parking is prohibited as an on-street parking type. \nReference: TCM, 9.2.1.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 9: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: On-street parallel parking stalls width shall be measured from the edge of the traveled way to the face of curb. The combination of travel and parking stall next to one another shall be no less than 18 ft. In areas adjacent to transit routes, the minimum shall be 19 ft. Parking is assumed to be 8 ft in width. Dimension the stall width and the width of lane on the site plan. Reference: TCM 9.2.2.A.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 10: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Individual on-street parallel parking stall lengths shall be 20 ft in length. Dimension the parking stall length on the site plan.\nReference: TCM 9.2.2.C.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 11: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: A minimum 3 ft buffer shall be provided between the edge of parallel on-street parking and a bike lane to ensure that opening car doors will not encroach on the protected bike lane. Dimension this buffer on the site plan. \nReference: TCM 9.2.3.2.A.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 12: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: A 1.5 ft offset from the curbside of an on-street parking stall shall be provided to all obstructions such as parking meters, poles, trees, etc. Show all obstructions on the site plan and dimension the offset.\nReference: TCM 9.2.3.1.A.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 13: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: On-street parking is prohibited within 15 ft of either side of fire hydrants. Dimension the distance between the on-street parking and the fire hydrant. \nReference: TCM 9.2.3.1.B. TCM Figure 9-2.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nBICYCLE PARKING \nTPW 14: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Identify the location of bicycle parking on the site plan, note the number of short-term and long-term spaces to be provided, show the direct unobstructed path connecting bicycle parking to the development entrance, and show a detail of the bicycle rack(s) (City of Austin standard detail #710S-1 or S-2, and 710S-6C, approved 2012). The minimum bicycle parking requirement is as follows: two spaces for Commercial Uses, five spaces for Multifamily Residential Use, and one space for Industrial, Civic, and Agricultural Uses, or 10 percent of the proposed motor vehicle parking spaces, whichever is greater. \nReference: LDC 25-6-477, Appendix A. TCM, 9.8.1.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 15: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Short and long-term bicycle parking ratios must be provided in accordance with the TCM. Reference TCM Table 9-6 for the ratio of short-term and long-term bicycle parking spaces by land use. Residential land use requires 30% to 50% short-term bicycle parking and 50% to 70% long-term bicycle parking. Can assume long-term bike parking will be provided within individual garages. Please include this in the parking table. Reference: TCM, 9.8.0.\n* Comment cleared. \n\nTPW 16: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: U-rack shall be used for short-term bicycle parking. \nReference: TCM, 9.8.5.A.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 17: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Bicycle parking must be located in a well-lit area. \nReference: TCM 9.8.1.I.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 18: Comment Status: Pending\n* U0: Provide enough space between bike rack locations to adequately accommodate a bicycle locked in every spot. One “U” rack provides two bicycle parking spots. Dimension the bicycle parking spaces on the site plan. The standard required bicycle space is 2 feet wide, 6 feet long, and 3 feet 4 inches tall. If larger styles of bicycles such as cargo or electric bicycles are anticipated, the design shall accommodate the footprint of these bicycles as the design bicycle (up to 3 ft wide by 10 ft long).\nReference: TCM Figure 9-14. and/or TCM, 9.8.1.\n* U1: Comment remains. Please include COA standard detail 710S-6C.\n\nFRONTAGE REQUIREMENTS\nTPW 19: Comment Status: Pending\n* U0: The ASMP identifies Valley View Rd as a Level 1 street with 58-foor cross section. Back of curb infrastructure must be designed in accordance with the Transportation Criteria Manual and includes: A 7’ tree and furniture (planting) zone, measured from the back of curb is required. This is to be followed by a 5’ minimum clear zone (sidewalk) and a min. 2’ buffer zone between the building/property line. TCM 2.8.2.2\n\n[Figure: Cross-section diagram showing 7' tree and furniture zone and 5' sidewalk]\n\n* U1: Comment remains. Waiver request approved, please pay waiver fee. Please ensure sidewalk meets TCM 4.1.3, “Meandering paths should avoid sharp turns or transitions and gradually transition no more than 1 ft. off path per 5 ft. of sidewalk length and maintain a straight section no less than the width of the sidewalk between transitions.”\n\nTPW 20: Comment Status: Pending\n* U0: A sidewalk easement is required if the public sidewalk enters onto private property. Provide an additional two feet within the easement for maintenance purposes. (Determine if the sidewalk easement requires maintenance (i.e. “with maintenance”). Otherwise add 2-additional feet). \nReference: TCM, 4.1.1, 4.1.2.\n* U1: Comment remains. Pending resolution of sidewalk location. When resolved, please submit draft sidewalk easement directly to this reviewer for routing through city legal. \n\nDRIVEWAYS\nTPW 21: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Driveways depicted on site plan do not match the required Type II driveway as the sidewalk crosses within the flare. Please revise.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 22: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: All sidewalk and bicycle lane crossings of driveways shall maintain the elevation of the sidewalk and bicycle lane in a raised crossing. \nReference: TCM, 7.5.2.1.C\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 23: Comment Status: Pending\n* U0: Maximum number of driveways permitted on a street with 231 feet frontage is 1. Please revise. \nReference: TCM, Table 7-4\n* U1: Comment remains. Pending review by area engineers. Response will be sent via email.\n\nTHROAT LENGTH\nTPW 24: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: For multifamily or commercial sites with <25 parking spaces, minimum throat storage length is 25’ measured from property boundary to the first interruption point. For multifamily or commercial sites with 25-100 parking spaces, minimum throat storage length is 25’ or 40’ min. If left turns are permitted. Please provide total number of parking spaces to establish required throat length.\nReference: TCM, Table 9-5\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nMISCELLANEOUS\nTPW 25: Comment Status: Pending\n* U0: Trash dumpsters must be located to provide adequate access and maneuverability for service vehicles. Show the dumpster.\nReference: LDC 25-2-1067(c); TCM, 9.3.0.2\n* U1: Comment remains. Please confirm the collection point for the individual trash cans. Will these be collected at each unit or will there be a central collection point for the roll-out bins. Please identify this collection point on the site plan. Trash bins cannot be left within the ROW.\n\nTPW 26: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: If roll-out bins are being proposed, then add the following notes to site plan sheet: \n* Trash containers shall not be left at curb side unattended. Signs must be posted on the building or at a location that is publicly visible indicating that trash containers may not be left at curbside. The sign shall indicate the City of Austin’s Code enforcement phone number for the public to report violations. \n* A restrictive covenant may be required for enforcement purposes. \nReference: TCM, 9.4.2.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 27: Comment Status: Pending\n* U0: Service commitment from a commercial trash service must be provided indicating they can provide service. The letter should address the minimum clearance requirement for the service vehicles. \n* U1: Comment remains.\n","numLines":151,"startLine":1,"totalLines":151}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776954388452,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan and identify:\n1. Are there any street trees shown in the public right-of-way along Valley View Road?\n2. If street trees exist, what are the planting zone boundaries and root barrier placements?\n3. Are there any utility planting zones or exclusion zones labeled?\n4. What is the location of Austin Water (AW) infrastructure (water mains, services) relative to the planting zones?\n5. Are there adequate Street Tree Utility Gaps (minimum 8 feet between planting zones)?\n6. Any tree wells proposed and their locations?\n7. Proximity of landscape/planting features to the detention pond\n\nLook for any potential conflicts between utilities and landscape features.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35 for \"VALLEY VIEW TOWNHOMES\"), here are the findings for your specific questions:\n\n**1. Are there any street trees shown in the public right-of-way along Valley View Road?**\nThere are no trees explicitly shown outside the property line in a delineated public right-of-way. However, there are three trees located along the western boundary next to \"Valley View Road\" within a shaded area designated by Key Note \"H-2\" (\"STREET YARD\"). These trees are labeled with the symbol \"SY\", which the Key Notes define as \"SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\". \n\n**2. If street trees exist, what are the planting zone boundaries and root barrier placements?**\nThe plan does not explicitly label, dimension, or visibly delineate specific \"planting zone boundaries\" or \"root barrier\" placements for any of the trees shown.\n\n**3. Are there any utility planting zones or exclusion zones labeled?**\nThere are no areas explicitly labeled as \"utility planting zones\" or \"exclusion zones\" on this specific sheet. \n\n**4. What is the location of Austin Water (AW) infrastructure (water mains, services) relative to the planting zones?**\nAustin Water infrastructure (such as water mains, meters, or services) is not visibly labeled or clearly indicated on this landscape plan sheet. (Note: Other utilities are visible, such as a line labeled \"SD\" running east-west between the buildings and a line labeled \"OHE\" along the southern boundary, but no clear water/wastewater lines are denoted).\n\n**5. Are there adequate Street Tree Utility Gaps (minimum 8 feet between planting zones)?**\nBecause neither Austin Water utility lines nor specific defined planting zone boundaries are shown on this landscape sheet, the presence of an 8-foot utility gap cannot be determined from this document alone.\n\n**6. Any tree wells proposed and their locations?**\nThere are no tree wells explicitly labeled, nor are there standard hardscape tree well symbols (like grates or isolated cutouts in pavement) indicated on this plan. The trees appear to be proposed within continuous landscape beds, street yards, or open spaces.\n\n**7. Proximity of landscape/planting features to the detention pond**\nIn the northeast section of the site, there are structures explicitly labeled \"SEDIMENTATION BASIN\" and \"FILTRATION BASIN\". Several proposed trees (including one labeled \"M\" and others with standard tree canopy symbols) and general landscape planting areas are located immediately adjacent to the exterior structural walls of these basins on their north, east, and south sides. A wooden privacy fence (Key Note \"H-6\") also runs in close proximity to the east of the filtration basin.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1457,"outputTokens":593,"totalTokens":5248,"reasoningTokens":3198},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the landscape plan and identify:\n1. Are there any street trees shown in the public right-of-way along Valley View Road?\n2. If street trees exist, what are the planting zone boundaries and root barrier placements?\n3. Are there any utility planting zones or exclusion zones labeled?\n4. What is the location of Austin Water (AW) infrastructure (water mains, services) relative to the planting zones?\n5. Are there adequate Street Tree Utility Gaps (minimum 8 feet between planting zones)?\n6. Any tree wells proposed and their locations?\n7. Proximity of landscape/planting features to the detention pond\n\nLook for any potential conflicts between utilities and landscape features."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-OortswAz53L8iRaDCd7jplaS","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 14:26:28 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::k9vsn-1776954321168-22eadde198f2"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35 for \"VALLEY VIEW TOWNHOMES\"), here are the findings for your specific questions:\n\n**1. Are there any street trees shown in the public right-of-way along Valley View Road?**\nThere are no trees explicitly shown outside the property line in a delineated public right-of-way. However, there are three trees located along the western boundary next to \"Valley View Road\" within a shaded area designated by Key Note \"H-2\" (\"STREET YARD\"). These trees are labeled with the symbol \"SY\", which the Key Notes define as \"SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\". \n\n**2. If street trees exist, what are the planting zone boundaries and root barrier placements?**\nThe plan does not explicitly label, dimension, or visibly delineate specific \"planting zone boundaries\" or \"root barrier\" placements for any of the trees shown.\n\n**3. Are there any utility planting zones or exclusion zones labeled?**\nThere are no areas explicitly labeled as \"utility planting zones\" or \"exclusion zones\" on this specific sheet. \n\n**4. What is the location of Austin Water (AW) infrastructure (water mains, services) relative to the planting zones?**\nAustin Water infrastructure (such as water mains, meters, or services) is not visibly labeled or clearly indicated on this landscape plan sheet. (Note: Other utilities are visible, such as a line labeled \"SD\" running east-west between the buildings and a line labeled \"OHE\" along the southern boundary, but no clear water/wastewater lines are denoted).\n\n**5. Are there adequate Street Tree Utility Gaps (minimum 8 feet between planting zones)?**\nBecause neither Austin Water utility lines nor specific defined planting zone boundaries are shown on this landscape sheet, the presence of an 8-foot utility gap cannot be determined from this document alone.\n\n**6. Any tree wells proposed and their locations?**\nThere are no tree wells explicitly labeled, nor are there standard hardscape tree well symbols (like grates or isolated cutouts in pavement) indicated on this plan. The trees appear to be proposed within continuous landscape beds, street yards, or open spaces.\n\n**7. Proximity of landscape/planting features to the detention pond**\nIn the northeast section of the site, there are structures explicitly labeled \"SEDIMENTATION BASIN\" and \"FILTRATION BASIN\". Several proposed trees (including one labeled \"M\" and others with standard tree canopy symbols) and general landscape planting areas are located immediately adjacent to the exterior structural walls of these basins on their north, east, and south sides. A wooden privacy fence (Key Note \"H-6\") also runs in close proximity to the east of the filtration b