{"level":30,"time":1776954396209,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QYpnw3ad5uAnN4XjnFVrA9","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Transportation & Public Works (TPW-TDS) Review\n     2→\n     3→*Details requirements related to parking, street impact fees, right-of-way, driveways, and trash collection.*\n     4→\n     5→TPW-TDS Review – Suzy Riley (512) 974-4073 - suzanne.riley@austintexas.gov\n     6→\n     7→GENERAL COMMENTS\n     8→Please show the property line on the site plan.\n     9→U1: Comment cleared.\n    10→\n    11→SIF COMMENTS \n    12→TPW 1: Comment Status: Cleared\n    13→* U0: Please add the following note to the coversheet: Development of structures that require a building permit within this Site Plan, or revisions thereof, are required to comply with the City of Austin Street Impact Fee Ordinances, as applicable, and must be paid upon completion of the building permit plan review for each building. \n    14→Reference: LDC 25-6-662\n    15→* U0: Comment cleared.\n    16→\n    17→TPW 2: Comment Status: Pending\n    18→* U0: FYI: The Building Permits for this site are required to comply with the City’s Street Impact Fee. The fee was adopted by City Council in December 2020 and is applicable to all Building Permits submitted on or after June 22, 2022. (For more information: https://www.austintexas.gov/department/street-impact-fee). Please complete a copy of the SIF worksheet: https://atd.knack.com/development-services#customer-portal/services/street-impact-fee-worksheet/ This development may be eligible for SIF offsets if off-site transportation mitigations are included with the site plan. Please inform this reviewer if you would like these options pursued.\n    19→* Comment remains. Continue to work with area engineer, Mustafa Wali (Mustafa.Wali@austintexas.gov) to complete.\n    20→\n    21→PARKING\n    22→TPW 3: Comment Status: Cleared\n    23→* U0: Include a table showing the proposed land uses, the floor area in square feet for each land use, the parking ratio, the number of parking spaces required by type, and the number of parking spaces proposed by type (standard, compact, handicapped, short-term and long-term bicycle, loading, etc.). The amount required per Appendix A is necessary for the calculation of required accessible parking and long and short-term bike parking.\n    24→Reference: LDC 25-6-472, Appendix A.\n    25→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    26→\n    27→TPW 4: Comment Status: Cleared\n    28→* U0: All parking must be provided in accordance with design and construction standards of the TCM. Show dimensions for garage parking within townhomes. Reference: TCM Table 9-1, Table 9-2, and Table 9-3.\n    29→* U1: Comment cleared. \n    30→\n    31→TPW 5: Comment Status: Cleared\n    32→* U0: Traffic control signs and marking used in parking areas, except for structured parking garages, must conform to the latest edition of the Texas Manual for Uniform Traffic Control Devices (TMUTCD). Reference: TCM, 9.3.2.T.\n    33→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    34→\n    35→TPW 6: Comment Status: Cleared\n    36→* U0: Approval of the Transportation & Public Works Department (TPW) is required in order to place parking within the right-of-way. Is the intention to keep the existing on-street parking indicated on the site plan?\n    37→Reference: TCM, 2.7.1.3.G.\n    38→U1: Comment cleared. \n    39→\n    40→TPW 7: Comment Status: Cleared\n    41→* U0: Where on-street parking is desired without adequate right-of-way, a dedication of right-of-way shall be required. Please confirm the current ROW can accommodate on-street parking, refer to Level 1 cross-section - TCM, Figure 2-15. Reference: TCM, 9.2.0.A.\n    42→\n    43→[Figure: Diagram of a Level 1 58' ROW street cross-section showing parallel parking, sidewalks, and street trees]\n    44→\n    45→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    46→\n    47→TPW 8: Comment Status: Cleared\n    48→* U0: Parallel parking shall be the default configuration of all on-street parking. Back-in angled parking must be approved by the City Transportation Engineer or applicable Director. Head-in angled parking is prohibited as an on-street parking type. \n    49→Reference: TCM, 9.2.1.\n    50→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    51→\n    52→TPW 9: Comment Status: Cleared\n    53→* U0: On-street parallel parking stalls width shall be measured from the edge of the traveled way to the face of curb. The combination of travel and parking stall next to one another shall be no less than 18 ft. In areas adjacent to transit routes, the minimum shall be 19 ft. Parking is assumed to be 8 ft in width. Dimension the stall width and the width of lane on the site plan. Reference: TCM 9.2.2.A.\n    54→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    55→\n    56→TPW 10: Comment Status: Cleared\n    57→* U0: Individual on-street parallel parking stall lengths shall be 20 ft in length. Dimension the parking stall length on the site plan.\n    58→Reference: TCM 9.2.2.C.\n    59→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    60→\n    61→TPW 11: Comment Status: Cleared\n    62→* U0: A minimum 3 ft buffer shall be provided between the edge of parallel on-street parking and a bike lane to ensure that opening car doors will not encroach on the protected bike lane. Dimension this buffer on the site plan. \n    63→Reference: TCM 9.2.3.2.A.\n    64→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    65→\n    66→TPW 12: Comment Status: Cleared\n    67→* U0: A 1.5 ft offset from the curbside of an on-street parking stall shall be provided to all obstructions such as parking meters, poles, trees, etc. Show all obstructions on the site plan and dimension the offset.\n    68→Reference: TCM 9.2.3.1.A.\n    69→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    70→\n    71→TPW 13: Comment Status: Cleared\n    72→* U0: On-street parking is prohibited within 15 ft of either side of fire hydrants. Dimension the distance between the on-street parking and the fire hydrant. \n    73→Reference: TCM 9.2.3.1.B. TCM Figure 9-2.\n    74→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    75→\n    76→BICYCLE PARKING \n    77→TPW 14: Comment Status: Cleared\n    78→* U0: Identify the location of bicycle parking on the site plan, note the number of short-term and long-term spaces to be provided, show the direct unobstructed path connecting bicycle parking to the development entrance, and show a detail of the bicycle rack(s) (City of Austin standard detail #710S-1 or S-2, and 710S-6C, approved 2012). The minimum bicycle parking requirement is as follows: two spaces for Commercial Uses, five spaces for Multifamily Residential Use, and one space for Industrial, Civic, and Agricultural Uses, or 10 percent of the proposed motor vehicle parking spaces, whichever is greater. \n    79→Reference: LDC 25-6-477, Appendix A. TCM, 9.8.1.\n    80→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    81→\n    82→TPW 15: Comment Status: Cleared\n    83→* U0: Short and long-term bicycle parking ratios must be provided in accordance with the TCM. Reference TCM Table 9-6 for the ratio of short-term and long-term bicycle parking spaces by land use. Residential land use requires 30% to 50% short-term bicycle parking and 50% to 70% long-term bicycle parking. Can assume long-term bike parking will be provided within individual garages. Please include this in the parking table. Reference: TCM, 9.8.0.\n    84→* Comment cleared. \n    85→\n    86→TPW 16: Comment Status: Cleared\n    87→* U0: U-rack shall be used for short-term bicycle parking. \n    88→Reference: TCM, 9.8.5.A.\n    89→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    90→\n    91→TPW 17: Comment Status: Cleared\n    92→* U0: Bicycle parking must be located in a well-lit area. \n    93→Reference: TCM 9.8.1.I.\n    94→* U1: Comment cleared.\n    95→\n    96→TPW 18: Comment Status: Pending\n    97→* U0: Provide enough space between bike rack locations to adequately accommodate a bicycle locked in every spot. One “U” rack provides two bicycle parking spots. Dimension the bicycle parking spaces on the site plan. The standard required bicycle space is 2 feet wide, 6 feet long, and 3 feet 4 inches tall. If larger styles of bicycles such as cargo or electric bicycles are anticipated, the design shall accommodate the footprint of these bicycles as the design bicycle (up to 3 ft wide by 10 ft long).\n    98→Reference: TCM Figure 9-14. and/or TCM, 9.8.1.\n    99→* U1: Comment remains. Please include COA standard detail 710S-6C.\n   100→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a7253b0-d093-45b5-84cb-fd14b5436b5c","uuid":"0b3481f6-c97c-4dd6-9bfc-aa7079cb199f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md","content":"# Transportation & Public Works (TPW-TDS) Review\n\n*Details requirements related to parking, street impact fees, right-of-way, driveways, and trash collection.*\n\nTPW-TDS Review – Suzy Riley (512) 974-4073 - suzanne.riley@austintexas.gov\n\nGENERAL COMMENTS\nPlease show the property line on the site plan.\nU1: Comment cleared.\n\nSIF COMMENTS \nTPW 1: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Please add the following note to the coversheet: Development of structures that require a building permit within this Site Plan, or revisions thereof, are required to comply with the City of Austin Street Impact Fee Ordinances, as applicable, and must be paid upon completion of the building permit plan review for each building. \nReference: LDC 25-6-662\n* U0: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 2: Comment Status: Pending\n* U0: FYI: The Building Permits for this site are required to comply with the City’s Street Impact Fee. The fee was adopted by City Council in December 2020 and is applicable to all Building Permits submitted on or after June 22, 2022. (For more information: https://www.austintexas.gov/department/street-impact-fee). Please complete a copy of the SIF worksheet: https://atd.knack.com/development-services#customer-portal/services/street-impact-fee-worksheet/ This development may be eligible for SIF offsets if off-site transportation mitigations are included with the site plan. Please inform this reviewer if you would like these options pursued.\n* Comment remains. Continue to work with area engineer, Mustafa Wali (Mustafa.Wali@austintexas.gov) to complete.\n\nPARKING\nTPW 3: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Include a table showing the proposed land uses, the floor area in square feet for each land use, the parking ratio, the number of parking spaces required by type, and the number of parking spaces proposed by type (standard, compact, handicapped, short-term and long-term bicycle, loading, etc.). The amount required per Appendix A is necessary for the calculation of required accessible parking and long and short-term bike parking.\nReference: LDC 25-6-472, Appendix A.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 4: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: All parking must be provided in accordance with design and construction standards of the TCM. Show dimensions for garage parking within townhomes. Reference: TCM Table 9-1, Table 9-2, and Table 9-3.\n* U1: Comment cleared. \n\nTPW 5: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Traffic control signs and marking used in parking areas, except for structured parking garages, must conform to the latest edition of the Texas Manual for Uniform Traffic Control Devices (TMUTCD). Reference: TCM, 9.3.2.T.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 6: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Approval of the Transportation & Public Works Department (TPW) is required in order to place parking within the right-of-way. Is the intention to keep the existing on-street parking indicated on the site plan?\nReference: TCM, 2.7.1.3.G.\nU1: Comment cleared. \n\nTPW 7: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Where on-street parking is desired without adequate right-of-way, a dedication of right-of-way shall be required. Please confirm the current ROW can accommodate on-street parking, refer to Level 1 cross-section - TCM, Figure 2-15. Reference: TCM, 9.2.0.A.\n\n[Figure: Diagram of a Level 1 58' ROW street cross-section showing parallel parking, sidewalks, and street trees]\n\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 8: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Parallel parking shall be the default configuration of all on-street parking. Back-in angled parking must be approved by the City Transportation Engineer or applicable Director. Head-in angled parking is prohibited as an on-street parking type. \nReference: TCM, 9.2.1.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 9: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: On-street parallel parking stalls width shall be measured from the edge of the traveled way to the face of curb. The combination of travel and parking stall next to one another shall be no less than 18 ft. In areas adjacent to transit routes, the minimum shall be 19 ft. Parking is assumed to be 8 ft in width. Dimension the stall width and the width of lane on the site plan. Reference: TCM 9.2.2.A.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 10: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Individual on-street parallel parking stall lengths shall be 20 ft in length. Dimension the parking stall length on the site plan.\nReference: TCM 9.2.2.C.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 11: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: A minimum 3 ft buffer shall be provided between the edge of parallel on-street parking and a bike lane to ensure that opening car doors will not encroach on the protected bike lane. Dimension this buffer on the site plan. \nReference: TCM 9.2.3.2.A.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 12: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: A 1.5 ft offset from the curbside of an on-street parking stall shall be provided to all obstructions such as parking meters, poles, trees, etc. Show all obstructions on the site plan and dimension the offset.\nReference: TCM 9.2.3.1.A.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 13: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: On-street parking is prohibited within 15 ft of either side of fire hydrants. Dimension the distance between the on-street parking and the fire hydrant. \nReference: TCM 9.2.3.1.B. TCM Figure 9-2.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nBICYCLE PARKING \nTPW 14: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Identify the location of bicycle parking on the site plan, note the number of short-term and long-term spaces to be provided, show the direct unobstructed path connecting bicycle parking to the development entrance, and show a detail of the bicycle rack(s) (City of Austin standard detail #710S-1 or S-2, and 710S-6C, approved 2012). The minimum bicycle parking requirement is as follows: two spaces for Commercial Uses, five spaces for Multifamily Residential Use, and one space for Industrial, Civic, and Agricultural Uses, or 10 percent of the proposed motor vehicle parking spaces, whichever is greater. \nReference: LDC 25-6-477, Appendix A. TCM, 9.8.1.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 15: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Short and long-term bicycle parking ratios must be provided in accordance with the TCM. Reference TCM Table 9-6 for the ratio of short-term and long-term bicycle parking spaces by land use. Residential land use requires 30% to 50% short-term bicycle parking and 50% to 70% long-term bicycle parking. Can assume long-term bike parking will be provided within individual garages. Please include this in the parking table. Reference: TCM, 9.8.0.\n* Comment cleared. \n\nTPW 16: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: U-rack shall be used for short-term bicycle parking. \nReference: TCM, 9.8.5.A.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 17: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Bicycle parking must be located in a well-lit area. \nReference: TCM 9.8.1.I.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 18: Comment Status: Pending\n* U0: Provide enough space between bike rack locations to adequately accommodate a bicycle locked in every spot. One “U” rack provides two bicycle parking spots. Dimension the bicycle parking spaces on the site plan. The standard required bicycle space is 2 feet wide, 6 feet long, and 3 feet 4 inches tall. If larger styles of bicycles such as cargo or electric bicycles are anticipated, the design shall accommodate the footprint of these bicycles as the design bicycle (up to 3 ft wide by 10 ft long).\nReference: TCM Figure 9-14. and/or TCM, 9.8.1.\n* U1: Comment remains. Please include COA standard detail 710S-6C.\n","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":151}}}
