{"level":30,"time":1776954403307,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine this landscape plan and provide the following information:\n1. Are there any trees shown in the street right-of-way (ROW) along Valley View Road or other public street frontages? If so, describe their locations.\n2. Are there any designated utility exclusion zones, root barriers, or planting zone boundaries marked on this plan?\n3. Are there any notes or labels indicating planting zones, utility gaps, or restrictions in the ROW?\n4. How are utilities (water, sewer, electric, storm drain) routed relative to landscaping areas?\n5. What is the scale of this drawing and confirm the sheet number?","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (31)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776954403307,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013wD22chP3LjKcqn9J4RzZ2","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here is the requested information:\n\n**1. Detention Pond Location**\n*   **Location:** Yes, the detention pond is located in the upper right portion of the drawing. Based on the North arrow (located above the Bleyl Engineering logo on the right side) which points straight up, this corresponds to the **Northeast corner** of the site.\n*   **Labels:** It is delineated by a dashed line rectangle and is specifically labeled as **\"Biofiltration / Detention Pond\"**. There is also an adjacent square labeled **\"Pond Perimeter Fence\"**.\n\n**2. Overall Site Layout**\n*   **Buildings:** The site consists of 8 multi-unit residential buildings (townhomes) labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8.\n    *   **North Row:** Bldg. 1, Bldg. 3, and Bldg. 5.\n    *   **Middle Row:** Bldg. 2, Bldg. 4, and Bldg. 6.\n    *   **South Row:** Bldg. 8 and Bldg. 7.\n*   **Main Circulation Route:** Access to the site is provided from the road on the left (West) side via two entrances labeled \"Construct Type II Driveway\". The main northern entrance leads into a continuous loop road that encircles the central buildings (Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 7) and a \"Common Open Space\" area.\n*   **Parking Areas:** There are no large, centralized parking lots. Parking is integrated directly into the units. The circulation loop road provides direct driveway access to individual unit garages. This layout is confirmed by the \"Parking Data\" table in the bottom right, which lists **\"Residential 10 Surface / 78 Garage\"**.\n\n**3. Utility Line Routings**\n*   **Visibility:** Yes, utility line routings are highly visible throughout the plan.\n*   **Types visible:**\n    *   **Water (\"- W -\"):** Lines run from the street entrance and follow the entirety of the inner circulation loop road.\n    *   **Wastewater (\"- WW -\"):** Lines run roughly parallel to the water lines, routing through the main circulation loop to service the buildings.\n    *   **Storm Drain (\"- SD -\"):** Lines are visible, particularly routing around the southern edge of the loop road toward the eastern edge and the detention pond area.\n*   **Crossing under parking:** Yes. Because the main water (\"- W -\") and wastewater (\"- WW -\") lines are routed directly underneath the main loop driveway, they inherently cross directly in front of and under the individual unit driveways/aprons that lead into the garages.\n\n**4. Easements**\nSeveral easements are distinctly marked and noted on the plan. Transcribing exactly as they appear:\n*   **Western/Left Edge (Near road access):**\n    *   **\"Wastewater Easement Doc#\"** (Text following \"Doc#\" is unclear/cut off).\n    *   **\"Sidewalk Easement Doc#\"** (Appears twice, near both driveway entrances; text following \"Doc#\" is unclear).\n*   **Northern Boundary:**\n    *   **\"5' P.U.E. Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   **Eastern/Right Boundary (Near pond and Bldg 5/6):**\n    *   **\"25' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** (Runs north-south along the property line).\n    *   **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n    *   **\"Existing Access & P.U. Easement Doc. 2010070237 O.P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   **Southern/Bottom Edge:**\n    *   **\"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg 14, Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n    *   **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement ~Vol. 5468, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n\n**5. Scale and Sheet Number**\n*   **Scale:** The graphic scale located in the lower right area of the drawing explicitly states: **Scale 1\" = 20'**.\n*   **Sheet Number:** Located in the bottom right corner title block, the sheet number is exactly: **Sheet: 9 of 39**. (The drawing number below it is SP-2025-0126C)."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b6f63193-ad83-4c2c-8030-773d2a7b74d6","uuid":"e1b12adc-6b9e-4e2f-a26b-14e36bee2bf8","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here is the requested information:\n\n**1. Detention Pond Location**\n*   **Location:** Yes, the detention pond is located in the upper right portion of the drawing. Based on the North arrow (located above the Bleyl Engineering logo on the right side) which points straight up, this corresponds to the **Northeast corner** of the site.\n*   **Labels:** It is delineated by a dashed line rectangle and is specifically labeled as **\"Biofiltration / Detention Pond\"**. There is also an adjacent square labeled **\"Pond Perimeter Fence\"**.\n\n**2. Overall Site Layout**\n*   **Buildings:** The site consists of 8 multi-unit residential buildings (townhomes) labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8.\n    *   **North Row:** Bldg. 1, Bldg. 3, and Bldg. 5.\n    *   **Middle Row:** Bldg. 2, Bldg. 4, and Bldg. 6.\n    *   **South Row:** Bldg. 8 and Bldg. 7.\n*   **Main Circulation Route:** Access to the site is provided from the road on the left (West) side via two entrances labeled \"Construct Type II Driveway\". The main northern entrance leads into a continuous loop road that encircles the central buildings (Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 7) and a \"Common Open Space\" area.\n*   **Parking Areas:** There are no large, centralized parking lots. Parking is integrated directly into the units. The circulation loop road provides direct driveway access to individual unit garages. This layout is confirmed by the \"Parking Data\" table in the bottom right, which lists **\"Residential 10 Surface / 78 Garage\"**.\n\n**3. Utility Line Routings**\n*   **Visibility:** Yes, utility line routings are highly visible throughout the plan.\n*   **Types visible:**\n    *   **Water (\"- W -\"):** Lines run from the stree