{"level":30,"time":1776954409233,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KUwYWBPahk9DbFThJThsKU","type":"tool_result","content":"   100→\n   101→FRONTAGE REQUIREMENTS\n   102→TPW 19: Comment Status: Pending\n   103→* U0: The ASMP identifies Valley View Rd as a Level 1 street with 58-foor cross section. Back of curb infrastructure must be designed in accordance with the Transportation Criteria Manual and includes: A 7’ tree and furniture (planting) zone, measured from the back of curb is required. This is to be followed by a 5’ minimum clear zone (sidewalk) and a min. 2’ buffer zone between the building/property line. TCM 2.8.2.2\n   104→\n   105→[Figure: Cross-section diagram showing 7' tree and furniture zone and 5' sidewalk]\n   106→\n   107→* U1: Comment remains. Waiver request approved, please pay waiver fee. Please ensure sidewalk meets TCM 4.1.3, “Meandering paths should avoid sharp turns or transitions and gradually transition no more than 1 ft. off path per 5 ft. of sidewalk length and maintain a straight section no less than the width of the sidewalk between transitions.”\n   108→\n   109→TPW 20: Comment Status: Pending\n   110→* U0: A sidewalk easement is required if the public sidewalk enters onto private property. Provide an additional two feet within the easement for maintenance purposes. (Determine if the sidewalk easement requires maintenance (i.e. “with maintenance”). Otherwise add 2-additional feet). \n   111→Reference: TCM, 4.1.1, 4.1.2.\n   112→* U1: Comment remains. Pending resolution of sidewalk location. When resolved, please submit draft sidewalk easement directly to this reviewer for routing through city legal. \n   113→\n   114→DRIVEWAYS\n   115→TPW 21: Comment Status: Cleared\n   116→* U0: Driveways depicted on site plan do not match the required Type II driveway as the sidewalk crosses within the flare. Please revise.\n   117→* U1: Comment cleared.\n   118→\n   119→TPW 22: Comment Status: Cleared\n   120→* U0: All sidewalk and bicycle lane crossings of driveways shall maintain the elevation of the sidewalk and bicycle lane in a raised crossing. \n   121→Reference: TCM, 7.5.2.1.C\n   122→* U1: Comment cleared.\n   123→\n   124→TPW 23: Comment Status: Pending\n   125→* U0: Maximum number of driveways permitted on a street with 231 feet frontage is 1. Please revise. \n   126→Reference: TCM, Table 7-4\n   127→* U1: Comment remains. Pending review by area engineers. Response will be sent via email.\n   128→\n   129→THROAT LENGTH\n   130→TPW 24: Comment Status: Cleared\n   131→* U0: For multifamily or commercial sites with <25 parking spaces, minimum throat storage length is 25’ measured from property boundary to the first interruption point. For multifamily or commercial sites with 25-100 parking spaces, minimum throat storage length is 25’ or 40’ min. If left turns are permitted. Please provide total number of parking spaces to establish required throat length.\n   132→Reference: TCM, Table 9-5\n   133→* U1: Comment cleared.\n   134→\n   135→MISCELLANEOUS\n   136→TPW 25: Comment Status: Pending\n   137→* U0: Trash dumpsters must be located to provide adequate access and maneuverability for service vehicles. Show the dumpster.\n   138→Reference: LDC 25-2-1067(c); TCM, 9.3.0.2\n   139→* U1: Comment remains. Please confirm the collection point for the individual trash cans. Will these be collected at each unit or will there be a central collection point for the roll-out bins. Please identify this collection point on the site plan. Trash bins cannot be left within the ROW.\n   140→\n   141→TPW 26: Comment Status: Cleared\n   142→* U0: If roll-out bins are being proposed, then add the following notes to site plan sheet: \n   143→* Trash containers shall not be left at curb side unattended. Signs must be posted on the building or at a location that is publicly visible indicating that trash containers may not be left at curbside. The sign shall indicate the City of Austin’s Code enforcement phone number for the public to report violations. \n   144→* A restrictive covenant may be required for enforcement purposes. \n   145→Reference: TCM, 9.4.2.\n   146→* U1: Comment cleared.\n   147→\n   148→TPW 27: Comment Status: Pending\n   149→* U0: Service commitment from a commercial trash service must be provided indicating they can provide service. The letter should address the minimum clearance requirement for the service vehicles. \n   150→* U1: Comment remains.\n   151→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a7253b0-d093-45b5-84cb-fd14b5436b5c","uuid":"c1851bde-cecc-446a-bbb5-b1a611d8ca2d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md","content":"\nFRONTAGE REQUIREMENTS\nTPW 19: Comment Status: Pending\n* U0: The ASMP identifies Valley View Rd as a Level 1 street with 58-foor cross section. Back of curb infrastructure must be designed in accordance with the Transportation Criteria Manual and includes: A 7’ tree and furniture (planting) zone, measured from the back of curb is required. This is to be followed by a 5’ minimum clear zone (sidewalk) and a min. 2’ buffer zone between the building/property line. TCM 2.8.2.2\n\n[Figure: Cross-section diagram showing 7' tree and furniture zone and 5' sidewalk]\n\n* U1: Comment remains. Waiver request approved, please pay waiver fee. Please ensure sidewalk meets TCM 4.1.3, “Meandering paths should avoid sharp turns or transitions and gradually transition no more than 1 ft. off path per 5 ft. of sidewalk length and maintain a straight section no less than the width of the sidewalk between transitions.”\n\nTPW 20: Comment Status: Pending\n* U0: A sidewalk easement is required if the public sidewalk enters onto private property. Provide an additional two feet within the easement for maintenance purposes. (Determine if the sidewalk easement requires maintenance (i.e. “with maintenance”). Otherwise add 2-additional feet). \nReference: TCM, 4.1.1, 4.1.2.\n* U1: Comment remains. Pending resolution of sidewalk location. When resolved, please submit draft sidewalk easement directly to this reviewer for routing through city legal. \n\nDRIVEWAYS\nTPW 21: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: Driveways depicted on site plan do not match the required Type II driveway as the sidewalk crosses within the flare. Please revise.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 22: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: All sidewalk and bicycle lane crossings of driveways shall maintain the elevation of the sidewalk and bicycle lane in a raised crossing. \nReference: TCM, 7.5.2.1.C\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 23: Comment Status: Pending\n* U0: Maximum number of driveways permitted on a street with 231 feet frontage is 1. Please revise. \nReference: TCM, Table 7-4\n* U1: Comment remains. Pending review by area engineers. Response will be sent via email.\n\nTHROAT LENGTH\nTPW 24: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: For multifamily or commercial sites with <25 parking spaces, minimum throat storage length is 25’ measured from property boundary to the first interruption point. For multifamily or commercial sites with 25-100 parking spaces, minimum throat storage length is 25’ or 40’ min. If left turns are permitted. Please provide total number of parking spaces to establish required throat length.\nReference: TCM, Table 9-5\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nMISCELLANEOUS\nTPW 25: Comment Status: Pending\n* U0: Trash dumpsters must be located to provide adequate access and maneuverability for service vehicles. Show the dumpster.\nReference: LDC 25-2-1067(c); TCM, 9.3.0.2\n* U1: Comment remains. Please confirm the collection point for the individual trash cans. Will these be collected at each unit or will there be a central collection point for the roll-out bins. Please identify this collection point on the site plan. Trash bins cannot be left within the ROW.\n\nTPW 26: Comment Status: Cleared\n* U0: If roll-out bins are being proposed, then add the following notes to site plan sheet: \n* Trash containers shall not be left at curb side unattended. Signs must be posted on the building or at a location that is publicly visible indicating that trash containers may not be left at curbside. The sign shall indicate the City of Austin’s Code enforcement phone number for the public to report violations. \n* A restrictive covenant may be required for enforcement purposes. \nReference: TCM, 9.4.2.\n* U1: Comment cleared.\n\nTPW 27: Comment Status: Pending\n* U0: Service commitment from a commercial trash service must be provided indicating they can provide service. The letter should address the minimum clearance requirement for the service vehicles. \n* U1: Comment remains.\n","numLines":52,"startLine":100,"totalLines":151}}}
