{"level":30,"time":1776954435174,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01USweqXompj95d6NG4efgDB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see from Sheet 9 that it has \"Block 2: drawing — Lighting Note & Figure 34\" which mentions \"all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5.\"\n\nHowever, I don't see any mention of street lights in the ROW. The lighting appears to be building exterior lighting. There's no mention of street light poles, street light coordination, or Great Streets lighting requirements.\n\nNow let me also verify whether the project is in the Great Streets boundary or within the DAPCZ to determine applicability of those items.\n\nThe project is at 3759 Valley View Road. Valley View Road doesn't seem to be in the downtown area or central Austin where Great Streets would apply based on the description in the grouping (bounded by MLK Blvd (N), Lady Bird Lake/Cesar Chavez (S), IH-35 (E), Lamar Blvd (W)).\n\nValley View Road is in South Austin, which is south of Lady Bird Lake, so it's outside the Great Streets boundary. Therefore, items EL-3.20 (Great Streets lighting labels) are likely N/A for this project.\n\nSimilarly, for moonlight towers (EL-3.13, EL-3.14, EL-3.15), the grouping notes that \"moonlight tower locations are not mapped in Bureau code files\" and recommends flagging for human verification if the project is in downtown or central Austin. Since Valley View Road is in South Austin, this is likely outside the moonlight tower area.\n\nLet me now compile my findings. Let me think about what's applicable and what's a deficiency:\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY:\n\n**What I found:**\n1. Sheet 3 has the FOUR Standard Austin Energy Notes (present and verbatim) ✓ - EL-3.6 PASS\n2. Sheet 3 has Transmission Easement Notes (comprehensive) ✓ - EL-3.32 PASS (with provisions)\n\n\n3. Sheet 3 includes preconstruction safety meeting note for transmission easement work ✓, but Sheet 8's preconstruction meeting note is for Environmental Inspector rather than Austin Energy ✗ - EL-3.9 FAIL. Additionally, Sheet 3 is missing the note stating the site is within AE service area ✗ - EL-3.4 FAIL, and missing the note about developer responsibility for conduit and infrastructure ✗ - EL-3.5 FAIL. The Cover Sheet also lacks the Additional Review Acknowledgement table ✗ - EL-3.29 FAIL.\n\nAustin Energy completeness check shows the review was marked complete, suggesting review occurred, but no ESPA or AEU clearance letters are visible. No approved addressing plan was found, and the project appears to fall outside Great Streets and Moonlight Tower areas. Critical documentation is missing: ESPA approval, AEU clearance letter, Electric Service Availability Letter, electrical transformer and pull box design approval from AE, final electrical easement coordination documents, georeferenced AutoCAD drawing, evidence of AE personnel access demonstration, and street-specific plan notes for point of service and voltage.\n\nSeveral additional items couldn't be verified: street light coordinates (none appear proposed), ROW utility coordination linear footage determination needed to establish AULCC applicability, AULCC clearance letter itself, Gattan and telecommunications clearances (unclear if applicable for private development), dry utility clearances, CIP clearance, ROW utility coordination case closure status, and addressing plan approval beyond potential AVL presence. Street name reservations for any private drives also lack documentation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2062,"cache_read_input_tokens":74889,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2062},"output_tokens":2,"service_ti