{"level":30,"time":1776954442857,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01PEBev78nKtRkhuGh2rQ411","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0192c9vBPMD6MR72Mhu1L1a3","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":2,"prompt":"Examine the plat sheet carefully and identify:\n1. All easement lines shown on the plat\n2. The specific easement labels/descriptions (e.g., \"5' Electric Easement\", \"10' Drainage Easement\", \"Wastewater Easement\", etc.)\n3. The boundaries and dimensions of each easement\n4. Whether the Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (Instrument 2010070731) is shown\n5. Whether the City of Austin Drainage Easement (Instrument 2011021137) is shown\n6. How the easements relate to Lot 1 boundaries\n7. Any notation about which easements are dedicated vs. private\n\nThis is critical for determining whether all recorded easements are properly depicted on the submitted site plan."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":300,"cache_read_input_tokens":65900,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":300},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9a5665b-9006-428b-bc9b-c42e794b3bcd","uuid":"f2d50b69-cc05-4efa-9a19-7c784962f33a"}
{"level":30,"time":1776954442859,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":2,"prompt":"Examine the plat sheet carefully and identify:\n1. All easement lines shown on the plat\n2. The specific easement labels/descriptions (e.g., \"5' Electric Easement\", \"10' Drainage Easement\", \"Wastewater Easement\", etc.)\n3. The boundaries and dimensions of each easement\n4. Whether the Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (Instrument 2010070731) is shown\n5. Whether the City of Austin Drainage Easement (Instrument 2011021137) is shown\n6. How the easements relate to Lot 1 boundaries\n7. Any notation about which easements are dedicated vs. private\n\nThis is critical for determining whether all recorded easements are properly depicted on the submitted site plan.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (2)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776954445117,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine this site plan for: 1) Any overhead electrical utilities shown (poles, overhead lines, transmission lines, transmission easements)? 2) Are there any labeled easements shown? 3) Where are the buildings positioned relative to any overhead utilities or easements? 4) Are there any clearance envelopes or height limit lines shown? 5) Is there any transmission easement boundary delineated? 6) What is shown on the western property boundary?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan, here are the findings corresponding to your questions:\n\n**1) Overhead electrical utilities shown:**\n*   There are overhead electric lines delineated by a dashed line type with the letters \"**--- OHE ---**\". \n*   One such \"**--- OHE ---**\" line runs along the southern (bottom) property boundary.\n*   Another \"**--- OHE ---**\" line is visible near the southeastern (bottom right) corner, crossing over the eastern property line.\n*   An \"**Existing Utility Pole**\" is labeled near the northwest (top left) corner of the site, adjacent to the street right-of-way.\n\n**2) Labeled easements shown:**\nThere are several labeled easements located around the perimeter of the property:\n*   **North side:** \"**5' P.U.E. Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.**\"\n*   **East side:** \n    *   \"**25' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.**\" (near the northeast corner)\n    *   \"**15' Drainage Easement Doc. 2010021137 O.P.R.T.C.Tx.**\" (adjacent to Building 5)\n    *   \"**15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.**\" (along the eastern boundary line)\n*   **South side / Southeast corner:** \"**5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.**\"\n*   **West side:**\n    *   \"**Wastewater Easement Doc#**\"\n    *   \"**Sidewalk Easement Doc#**\"\n    *   \"**15' Water and Wastewater Vault Easement Doc#**\"\n\n**3) Building positions relative to utilities or easements:**\n*   The buildings (labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8) are positioned centrally within the lot and appear to be purposefully set back to avoid encroaching on any of the labeled easements. \n*   For example, Buildings 5 and 6 are positioned just west of the eastern drainage easements. Buildings 1 and 8 are positioned east of the western sidewalk and wastewater easements. Buildings 3 and 4 are located south of the northern 5' P.U.E.\n*   No buildings are shown situated directly underneath the \"**--- OHE ---**\" lines running along the southern boundary.\n\n**4) Clearance envelopes or height limit lines:**\n*   There are **no** graphical clearance envelopes, safety arcs, or height limit lines delineated around the overhead utilities on this specific plan drawing. \n*   There is a \"**Building Height Table**\" provided in the lower right portion of the page that lists maximum allowable building heights (e.g., 40'), but this is a general zoning/site data table, not a spatial envelope drawn relative to the utility lines.\n\n**5) Transmission easement boundary delineated:**\n*   There are **no** easements specifically labeled as \"transmission\" easements on this document. The electrical-related easement is simply labeled \"**5' Elec. & Tele. Easement**\", and the lines are standard \"**OHE**\" (Overhead Electric).\n\n**6) What is shown on the western property boundary:**\nThe western property boundary (the left side of the drawing, fronting the road) contains several specific features and labels:\n*   Two separate entrances labeled \"**Construct Type II Driveway See Detail 433S-2**\".\n*   A \"**Concrete Sidewalk**\" running parallel to the street.\n*   Multiple easements as noted above: \"**Wastewater Easement Doc#**\", \"**Sidewalk Easement Doc#**\", and \"**15' Water and Wastewater Vault Easement Doc#**\".\n*   An \"**Existing Utility Pole**\" and \"**Wastewater Service Connection**\" near the northernmost driveway.\n*   A \"**Transformer Pad (Typ.)**\" positioned just inside the property line between the two driveways.\n*   A label pointing to a landscape feature stating: \"**Tree Well need to look up approp. detail**\".","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1401,"outputTokens":949,"totalTokens":4956,"reasoningTokens":2606},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine this site plan for: 1) Any overhead electrical utilities shown (poles, overhead lines, transmis