{"level":30,"time":1776954445461,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine this landscape plan and provide the following information:\n1. Are there any trees shown in the street right-of-way (ROW) along Valley View Road or other public street frontages? If so, describe their locations.\n2. Are there any designated utility exclusion zones, root barriers, or planting zone boundaries marked on this plan?\n3. Are there any notes or labels indicating planting zones, utility gaps, or restrictions in the ROW?\n4. How are utilities (water, sewer, electric, storm drain) routed relative to landscaping areas?\n5. What is the scale of this drawing and confirm the sheet number?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here is the information requested:\n\n**1. Are there any trees shown in the street right-of-way (ROW) along Valley View Road or other public street frontages? If so, describe their locations.**\nYes. Along the left side of the plan, parallel to \"Valley View Road\", there is a shaded strip designated by Key Note H-1 (\"PROPOSED PAVING\") and Key Note H-2 (\"STREET YARD\"). Within this area, between the road's edge of pavement and the building, there are several large tree symbols. Some of these trees are explicitly tagged with Key Note H-3 (\"STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\") and labels such as \"SY/M\".\n\n**2. Are there any designated utility exclusion zones, root barriers, or planting zone boundaries marked on this plan?**\nNo. Based on a review of the linework, symbols, and labels on this specific sheet, there are no features explicitly marked or labeled as \"utility exclusion zones,\" \"root barriers,\" or specific \"planting zone boundaries\" separating landscaping from utilities.\n\n**3. Are there any notes or labels indicating planting zones, utility gaps, or restrictions in the ROW?**\nNo. A review of the \"IRRIGATION NOTES\", \"NOTE\", \"KEY NOTES\", and the individual labels scattered across the plan does not reveal any text mentioning planting zones, utility gaps, or specific restrictions within the Right-of-Way.\n\n**4. How are utilities (water, sewer, electric, storm drain) routed relative to landscaping areas?**\nUtilities and landscaping areas frequently overlap on this plan. Notable routing includes:\n*   **Overhead Electric (OHE):** An \"OHE\" line runs continuously along the bottom (south) edge of the property line. This line passes directly through the drawn canopy symbols of at least seven trees planted along that southern boundary.\n*   **Storm Drain (SD):** A prominent \"SD\" line runs east-to-west through the center of the site (mostly under the building footprint). On the west side, it exits and runs underneath the shaded \"STREET YARD\" area (H-2) very close to the street yard landscaping trees (H-3) before meeting Valley View Road.\n*   **Water (W) and Electric (E):** Lines labeled \"W\" and \"E\" run generally through the central portions of the site, largely appearing to be routed under the building footprint or internal paved areas rather than through the primary perimeter planting beds.\n*   **Limit of Construction (LOC):** An \"LOC\" line surrounds the perimeter, and landscaping (trees and sod) is shown extending right up to this limit.\n\n**5. What is the scale of this drawing and confirm the sheet number?**\n*   **Scale:** Located above the bar scale in the bottom right, the text reads exactly: `SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")`\n*   **Sheet Number:** Located in the bottom right corner, the text reads exactly: `SHEET NO. 28 of 35`","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1442,"outputTokens":655,"totalTokens":4361,"reasoningTokens":2264},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":