{"level":30,"time":1776954454956,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Please examine Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) and identify:\n\n1. Are there any street light poles, light fixtures, or street lighting infrastructure shown on this sheet?\n2. Are there any labels or callouts indicating street lighting?\n3. Are there any utility boxes, transformers, pull boxes, or other electrical equipment shown? If so, describe their locations and what they are.\n4. Does the plan show underground electrical lines extending to or along the property frontage?\n5. Are there any conflicts noted between electrical infrastructure and other utilities (gas lines, storm drains, etc.)?\n6. Is there any information about lighting coordination with Austin Energy or other agencies?\n\nIf street lights are not shown on this sheet, note that explicitly.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan), here are the findings for your specific questions:\n\n1.  **Are there any street light poles, light fixtures, or street lighting infrastructure shown on this sheet?**\n    *   No. There are no street light poles, light fixtures, or specific street lighting infrastructure clearly shown or identifiable on this sheet.\n\n2.  **Are there any labels or callouts indicating street lighting?**\n    *   No. There are no labels or callouts for \"Street Light,\" \"SL,\" or any similar street lighting terminology anywhere on this plan.\n\n3.  **Are there any utility boxes, transformers, pull boxes, or other electrical equipment shown? If so, describe their locations and what they are.**\n    *   Yes, the plan shows numerous pieces of electrical equipment, indicated by blue squares and rectangles with leader lines to text callouts. They are distributed primarily around the perimeters of the proposed buildings (Bldg 1 through Bldg 8). The specific exact callouts found are:\n        *   **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**: Located in multiple areas, including west of Bldg 1, west of Bldg 8, east of Bldg 4, east of Bldg 6, east of Bldg 7, and near the southwestern property boundary.\n        *   **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**: Located west of Bldg 1, west of Bldg 2, west of Bldg 8, east of Bldg 4, and between Bldg 6 and Bldg 7.\n        *   **\"Electrical Meters\"**: Located on the north side of Bldg 1, north side of Bldg 3, east side of Bldg 4, west side of Bldg 8, south of Bldg 7, and between Bldg 1 and Bldg 2.\n\n4.  **Does the plan show underground electrical lines extending to or along the property frontage?**\n    *   Yes. There is a prominent, thick blue line running generally north-south along the western property frontage (Valley View Road). It is explicitly labeled with the callout **\"Underground Electric Line\"**. This line connects to the broader electrical network distributed throughout the site.\n\n5.  **Are there any conflicts noted between electrical infrastructure and other utilities (gas lines, storm drains, etc.)?**\n    *   No specific, identified conflicts are called out on the drawing at points where lines cross. However, the \"Utility Notes\" box in the bottom right corner contains general instructions regarding potential conflicts:\n        *   *\"2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\"*\n\n6.  **Is there any information about lighting coordination with Austin Energy or other agencies?**\n    *   No. There are no notes or information regarding lighting coordination with Austin Energy or any other specific agency on this sheet.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1467,"outputTokens":604,"totalTokens":4613,"reasoningTokens":2542},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please examine Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) and identify:\n\n1. Are there any street light poles, light fixtures, or street lighting infrastructure shown on this sheet?\n2. Are there any labels or callouts indicating street lighting?\n3. Are there any utility boxes, transformers, pull boxes, or other electrical equipment shown? If so, describe their locations and what they are.\n4. Does the plan show underground electrical lines extending to or along the property frontage?\n5. Are there any conflicts noted between electrical infrastructure and other utilities (gas lines, storm drains, etc.)?\n6. Is there any information about lighting coordination with Austin Energy or other agencies?\n\nIf street lights are not shown on this sheet, note that explicitly."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-4mFBttxQxoRaMjJV2Fk5Ut4C","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 14:27:34 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::rgfs8-1776954426359-15d1013a9171"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan), here are the findings for your specific questions:\n\n1.  **Are there any street light poles, light fixtures, or street lighting infrastructure shown on this sheet?**\n    *   No. There are no street light poles, light fixtures, or specific street lighting infrastructure clearly shown or identifiable on this sheet.\n\n2.  **Are there any labels or callouts indicating street lighting?**\n    *   No. There are no labels or callouts for \"Street Light,\" \"SL,\" or any similar street lighting terminology anywhere on this plan.\n\n3.  **Are there any utility boxes, transformers, pull boxes, or other electrical equipment shown? If so, describe their locations and what they are.**\n    *   Yes, the plan shows numerous pieces of electrical equipment, indicated by blue squares and rectangles with leader lines to text callouts. They are distributed primarily around the perimeters of the proposed buildings (Bldg 1 through Bldg 8). The specific exact callouts found are:\n        *   **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**: Located in multiple areas, including west of Bldg 1, west of Bldg 8, east of Bldg 4, east of Bldg 6, east of Bldg 7, and near the southwestern property boundary.\n        *   **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**: Located west of Bldg 1, west of Bldg 2, west of Bldg 8, east of Bldg 4, and between Bldg 6 and Bldg 7.\n        *   **\"Electrical Meters\"**: Located on the north side of Bldg 1, north side of Bldg 3, east side of Bldg 4, west side of Bldg 8, south of Bldg 7, and between Bldg 1 and Bldg 2.\n\n4.  **Does the plan show underground electrical lines extending to or along the property frontage?**\n    *   Yes. There is a prominent, thick blue line running generally north-south along the western property frontage (Valley View Road). It is explicitly labeled with the callout **\"Underground Electric Line\"**. This line connects to the broader electrical network distributed throughout the site.\n\n5.  **Are there any conflicts noted between electrical infrastructure and other utilities (gas lines, storm drains, etc.)?**\n    *   No specific, identified conflicts are called out on the drawing at points where lines cross. However, the \"Utility Notes\" box in the bottom right corner contains general instructions regarding potential conflicts:\n        *   *\"2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\"*\n\n6.  **Is there any information about lighting coordination with Austin Energy or other agencies?**\n 