ility (AEU) clearance or approval not obtained or not documented\"\n- Applicability: \"All sites served by Austin Energy\"\n\n\n- No AEU clearance letter appears in the documentation, suggesting this approval wasn't obtained or documented (FAIL)\n\nEL-3.3: \"Electric Service Availability Letter from Austin Energy not provided confirming that the point of service is within the Austin Energy service area; or for locations where the serving utility is uncertain, AE Public Involvement has not been contacted to obtain this letter\"\n- Applicability: \"Only when new electrical service is being obtained from Austin Energy and there is a question as to which electric utility serves the location\"\n- Austin Energy clearly serves this location within city limits with no utility uncertainty indicated, so this likely qualifies as N/A\n\nThe Austin Energy completeness check notation in the grouping notes indicates AE reviewed the submission, but this differs from ESPA approval. I need to flag EL-3.1 and EL-3.2 as deficiencies since I'm not seeing direct documentation of those approvals.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2383,"cache_read_input_tokens":76951,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2383},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7a2037a-f555-4152-8bdc-44008e269230","uuid":"6ba4e0e6-2e58-42e5-843f-4384f0413ef4"}
