tions, or distinctive linework indicating the presence of root barriers along the ROW or anywhere else on this plan.\n*   **Utility Exclusion Zones:** There are no designated or labeled \"utility exclusion zones\" marked near the ROW or elsewhere on the drawing.\n\n**3. Location and annotation of any tree wells that are proposed**\n*   **Tree Wells:** There are no explicit annotations or labels for \"tree wells\" (such as grated cutouts within continuous hardscape).\n*   **Landscape Islands:** Proposed trees located within the internal paved/parking areas are shown in curbed planting islands or peninsulas rather than confined wells. For example, a tree in the central drive aisle is labeled with \"PL\". The KEY NOTES identify this as \"PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 16 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\".\n*   The general \"NOTE:\" section provides construction details for these areas: *\"FINISHED ELEVATION FOR PARKING LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED PARKING LOT ELEVATION...\"*\n\n**4. Electrical outlets or service locations marked at tree wells or in street yard areas**\n*   A visual scan of the \"Street Yard\" planting zones (labeled H.2/H.3) and the internal parking lot islands reveals no symbols or text annotations indicating electrical outlets (e.g., weatherproof receptacles for landscape lighting) or electrical service connection points at these tree locations.\n*   An overhead electric line (labeled \"-OHE-\") runs along the bottom property boundary, but no specific drops or landscape electrical connections are detailed.\n\n**5. Austin Water (AW) infrastructure (mains, services) shown and their proximity to planting zones**\n*   **Water Mains:** A utility line annotated as \"-W-\" (standard for water main) runs vertically within the Valley View Road right-of-way on the left side of the drawing, parallel to the western property line (-LOC-).\n*   **Proximity to Planting Zones:** This \"-W-\" main is located in the ROW immediately adjacent to the property. The \"STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\" (H.3) zone and its proposed trees are located just inside the property line, placing this primary planting zone in close proximity to the water main.\n*   **Services crossing Planting Zones:** Near the bottom-left corner, a utility line (appearing to branch off the ROW mains) crosses the -LOC- into the site. This crossing passes directly through the shaded \"H.2\" / \"H.3\" street yard area, in very close proximity to a proposed tree cluster (annotated with tags including \"M\").\n*   **Documentation Requirement:** While not physical infrastructure, the \"IRRIGATION NOTES\" specifically mention Austin Water in item 4: *\"THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL PROVIDE A REPORT TO THE CITY ON A FORM PROVIDED BY AUSTIN WATER CERTIFYING COMPLIANCE WITH SUBSECTION 1 WHEN THE FINAL PLUMBING INSPECTIONS PERFORMED BY THE CITY.\"*","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1432,"outputTokens":904,"totalTokens":5895,"reasoningTokens":3559},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary docume