{"level":30,"time":1776954462136,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_013PCnneY3jG9x2FVboKWQVg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! I found something important. Block 9 \"Site Demolition Notes\" has 10 notes, but I notice:\n- None of the 10 notes mention transmission line safety requirements\n- No mention of 48-hour pre-construction safety meeting with Austin Energy\n- No mention of 10-foot barricades from transmission structures\n- No mention of warning signs under overhead facilities\n- No mention of prohibition on materials/spoils in transmission easement\n\nHowever, Sheet 3 Block 20 (Electric Transmission Notes) has 16 detailed notes about these requirements.\n\nThis is a DEFICIENCY: **EL-1.18** requires demolition plan to address required safety clearances from transmission lines, including:\n1. Pre-construction safety meeting ≥48 hours before work\n2. Barricades erected 10 ft from all transmission structures (including guys and anchors)\n3. Warning signs under overhead facilities\n4. Prohibition on materials or spoils storage within transmission easement\n\nThe demolition plan (Sheet 8) does NOT include these notes in its demolition plan sequence (Block 9). The requirements are mentioned in Sheet 3 (General Notes, Block 20), but not in the demolition plan notes themselves.\n\nNow let me check for other deficiencies. Let me look at the biofiltration pond plan to check SCM staging areas and maintenance access clearances.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1941,"cache_read_input_tokens":63839,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1941},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_mana