{"level":30,"time":1776954464009,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QYHDBfeuFUbBGLrBmFGRcn","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 5 — Erosion and Sedimentation Control Plan\n     2→\n     3→Site layout detailing erosion and sedimentation control measures.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the Erosion and Sedimentation Control Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project located in Austin, Texas. Its primary purpose is to detail the site's protective environmental measures during construction, illustrating the spatial layout of silt fences, mulch socks, inlet protections, and construction staging areas relative to proposed building footprints and existing topography.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values visible on this sheet:**\n    10→*   **Building 1:** 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50'\n    11→*   **Building 2:** 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    12→*   **Building 3:** 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    13→*   **Building 4:** 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    14→*   **Building 5:** 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.00'\n    15→*   **Building 6:** 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.00'\n    16→*   **Building 7:** 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.00'\n    17→*   **Building 8:** 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    18→*   **Benchmark 1:** Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88\n    19→*   **Benchmark 2:** Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88\n    20→*   **Topsoil Requirement:** Minimum 6 inches of topsoil over subgrade loosened to at least 2 inches depth.\n    21→*   **Idle Disturbed Area Limit:** Must be stabilized if not worked on for more than 14 days.\n    22→*   **Right-of-Way:** Valley View Road 60' R.O.W.\n    23→\n    24→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    25→\n    26→*   **Block 1: drawing — Site Plan & Erosion Controls**\n    27→    Contains the primary engineering drawing showing building layouts, topographies, and environmental control placements.\n    28→    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of proposed buildings, contour lines, utility routings, and the exact placement of erosion controls like silt fences, mulch socks, and tree protection fencing. *READ* for specific spot elevations and building square footages.\n    29→\n    30→*   **Block 5: notes — Legend**\n    31→    Provides the visual key for line types and symbols used on the main drawing.\n    32→    *READ the block content for* the definitions of line types denoting Limits of Construction, Silt Fences, Filter Dikes, Mulch Socks, Inlet Protections, and Tree Removals/Protection.\n    33→\n    34→*   **Block 6: notes — Erosion Notes**\n    35→    Contains mandatory environmental compliance instructions and contractor responsibilities.\n    36→    *READ the block content for* specific stabilization timelines (14-day rule), dust control mandates, and daily clean-up requirements per Austin City Rules.\n    37→\n    38→*   **Block 2: notes — Decompaction and Topsoil Requirements**\n    39→    Details soil preparation standards for revegetated areas.\n    40→    *READ the block content for* specifications on subgrade discing/scarifying depths and required topsoil thickness (6 inches).\n    41→\n    42→*   **Block 3: notes — Benchmarks**\n    43→    Lists the primary elevation reference points for the site.\n    44→    *READ the block content for* exact benchmark elevations and physical descriptions (Mag Nails). \n    45→\n    46→*   **Block 4: notes — Legal Description**\n    47→    Provides the formal property identification.\n    48→    *READ the block content for* the subdivision name, lot number, and recording volume/page in Travis County.\n    49→\n    50→*   **Block 7: notes — Tree List Reference**\n    51→    A brief directive note.\n    52→    *READ the block content for* the cross-reference pointing to Sheet 30 for the complete tree list.\n    53→\n    54→*   **Blocks 8, 9, 10, 11, 12: various — Administrative & Boilerplate**\n    55→    Contains the title block, project location (3759 Valley View Road), engineering firm details (Bleyl Engineering), Texas 811 dig warning, sheet index (Sheet 5 of 39), and the engineer's signed/dated professional seal (Jason K. Rodgers).\n    56→    *READ the block content for* general project metadata, sheet numbering, and contact/firm information.\n    57→\n    58→---\n    59→\n    60→- `block-6.md` — notes: This block provides specific erosion control notes that must be followed during construction, refere\n    61→\n    62→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    63→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"401e6f81-2db8-4fbd-be98-34356fe0baff","uuid":"e439996c-dd41-4455-b530-f51248487269","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-05/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 5 — Erosion and Sedimentation Control Plan\n\nSite layout detailing erosion and sedimentation control measures.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Erosion and Sedimentation Control Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project located in Austin, Texas. Its primary purpose is to detail the site's protective environmental measures during construction, illustrating the spatial layout of silt fences, mulch socks, inlet protections, and construction staging areas relative to proposed building footprints and existing topography.\n\n**Key values visible on this sheet:**\n*   **Building 1:** 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50'\n*   **Building 2:** 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n*   **Building 3:** 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n*   **Building 4:** 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n*   **Building 5:** 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.00'\n*   **Building 6:** 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.00'\n*   **Building 7:** 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.00'\n*   **Building 8:** 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n*   **Benchmark 1:** Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88\n*   **Benchmark 2:** Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88\n*   **Topsoil Requirement:** Minimum 6 inches of topsoil over subgrade loosened to at least 2 inches depth.\n*   **Idle Disturbed Area Limit:** Must be stabilized if not worked on for more than 14 days.\n*   **Right-of-Way:** Valley View Road 60' R.O.W.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 1: drawing — Site Plan & Erosion Controls**\n    Contains the primary engineering drawing showing building layouts, topographies, and environmental control placements.\n    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of proposed buildings, contour lines, utility routings, and the exact placement of erosion controls like silt fences, mulch socks, and tree protection fencing. *READ* for specific spot elevations and building square footages.\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Legend**\n    Provides the visual key for line types and symbols used on the main drawing.\n    *READ the block content for* the definitions of line types denoting Limits of Construction, Silt Fences, Filter Dikes, Mulch Socks, Inlet Protections, and Tree Removals/Protection.\n\n*   **Block 6: notes — Erosion Notes**\n    Contains mandatory environmental compliance instructions and contractor responsibilities.\n    *READ the block content for* specific stabilization timelines (14-day rule), dust control mandates, and daily clean-up requirements per Austin City Rules.\n\n*   **Block 2: notes — Decompaction and Topsoil Requirements**\n    Details soil preparation standards for revegetated areas.\n    *READ the block content for* specifications on subgrade discing/scarifying depths and required topsoil thickness (6 inches).\n\n*   **Block 3: notes — Benchmarks**\n    Lists the primary elevation reference points for the site.\n    *READ the block content for* exact benchmark elevations and physical descriptions (Mag Nails). \n\n*   **Block 4: notes — Legal Description**\n    Provides the formal property identification.\n    *READ the block content for* the subdivision name, lot number, and recording volume/page in Travis County.\n\n*   **Block 7: notes — Tree List Reference**\n    A brief directive note.\n    *READ the block content for* the cross-reference pointing to Sheet 30 for the complete tree list.\n\n*   **Blocks 8, 9, 10, 11, 12: various — Administrative & Boilerplate**\n    Contains the title block, project location (3759 Valley View Road), engineering firm details (Bleyl Engineering), Texas 811 dig warning, sheet index (Sheet 5 of 39), and the engineer's signed/dated professional seal (Jason K. Rodgers).\n    *READ the block content for* general project metadata, sheet numbering, and contact/firm information.\n\n---\n\n- `block-6.md` — notes: This block provides specific erosion control notes that must be followed during construction, refere\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":63,"startLine":1,"totalLines":63}}}
