{"level":30,"time":1776954470052,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01JpNdBKA6SVZ2dZFbF9RmhH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now let me check if there's any \"staging and construction management plan\" mentioned. From the EL-1 grouping description, checklist items EL-1.22, EL-1.23, EL-1.24, EL-1.25 all reference staging areas, maintenance access drives, and construction access points.\n\nLooking at the sheet guide for Sheet 5, it mentions \"construction staging areas\" but doesn't provide details on clearances. Let me check the blocks for Sheet 5 to see if there's any staging area detail.\n\nAlso, from the facts and earlier notes:\n- The site has a biofiltration/detention pond (privately maintained)\n- Combined storage volume appears to be 6,388 cf (from Sheet 15), which is LESS than 5,000 cu ft? Let me check.\n\nActually, looking at Sheet 15 guide:\n- Maximum Ponding Depth above Sand Bed: 3.65 ft\n- Filtration Pond Area Provided: 831 sf\n\nThis appears to be a single pond for Unit 501. The facts mention \"Stacked biofiltration / detention pond (privately maintained)\" suggesting it might be one combined pond.\n\nFrom the DCM exemption in the grouping notes:\n\"SCM staging area and maintenance access drive clearance requirements exempt when combined pond volume ≤5,000 cu ft AND ponding depth ≤3 ft\"\n\nIf the combined volume is 6,388 cu ft and depth is 3.65 ft, then BOTH thresholds are exceeded, so the 14-ft clearance requirements (EL-1.22, EL-1.23) DO APPLY.\n\nLet me read the blocks for Sheet 5 and 15 to check if these clearances are shown.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3703,"cache_read_input_tokens":65780,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"e