outhern property line of **LOT 1**. The boundary it runs parallel to is dimensioned as `361.42'`.\n*   **\"20' Drainage Easement (Existing)\"**: This is shown as a 20-foot wide strip running horizontally along the northern property line of **LOT 2**. The boundary it runs parallel to is dimensioned as `284.92'`.\n*   **\"10' Wastewater Line Easement\"**: This is a 10-foot wide strip running roughly east-west through the middle/lower section of **LOT 2**. It enters from the western boundary of Lot 2 and exits through the eastern boundary at Clawson Road. It contains specific metes and bounds notation, including a segment labeled `151.00'`.\n\n**4. Whether the Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (Instrument 2010070731) is shown**\nThis instrument is **not shown** on the plat. Please note that this plat was surveyed and recorded in 1975, so any instruments recorded in 2010 would not appear on this historical document.\n\n**5. Whether the City of Austin Drainage Easement (Instrument 2011021137) is shown**\nThis instrument is **not shown** on the plat. Similar to the item above, a 2011 instrument cannot appear on a 1975 plat.\n\n**6. How the easements relate to Lot 1 boundaries**\nOnly one of the depicted easements is located on Lot 1:\n*   The **\"Exist. 5' Elec. Ease.\"** runs exactly parallel to and just inside the southern boundary line of Lot 1 (which abuts O.R. Rogers' property).\n*   The other two easements (\"20' Drainage Easement (Existing)\" and \"10' Wastewater Line Easement\") are located entirely within the boundaries of **LOT 2** and do not cross into Lot 1.\n\n**7. Any notation about which easements are dedicated vs. private**\nIn the upper right quadrant under the owner's dedication heading (**\"KNOW ALL MEN BY THESE PRESENTS\"**), the document contains the following specific notation dedicating the easements to the public:\n> *\"...and I do hereby dedicate to the public all streets and easements as shown hereon.\"*\n\nAdditionally, the labels for the electric