{"level":30,"time":1776954500179,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01DHQnw3Aai7Huuq8WnXLh55","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect. So there's no ESPA approval or Austin Energy sign-off documented on the electrical plan sheet. The plan is labeled \"Preliminary\" which suggests it hasn't been finalized with AE approval.\n\nHowever, I need to be careful about EL-3.1 and EL-3.2. Let me re-read their applicability:\n\nEL-3.1: \"Electric Service Planning Application (ESPA) not submitted to Austin Energy for review and approval, or ESPA approval not documented in the plan set\"\n- Applicability: \"Only when new or modified electrical service is required. Check: project scope for new construction or electrical service upgrades\"\n- NEW ELECTRICAL SERVICE IS BEING PROVIDED (39 units with building service)\n- ESPA approval is NOT documented in the plan set\n\nThis is a FAIL.\n\nEL-3.2: \"Austin Energy Utility (AEU) clearance or approval not obtained or not documented\"\n- Applicability: \"All sites served by Austin Energy. Check: submittal package for AEU clearance letter\"\n- Site IS served by Austin Energy\n- AEU clearance letter is NOT in the submittal package (I haven't found it)\n\nHowever, the master comment report says \"AE completeness check complete\" which could mean:\na) Austin Energy has reviewed the submission and found it complete (meaning no deficiencies from AE's perspective), OR\nb) Simply that Austin Energy has completed their review/checklist process\n\nThis is ambiguous. A \"completeness check complete\" is different from issuing a clearance letter. The grouping document notes that \"Successful AULCC coordination results in an AULCC Completeness Letter (clearance letter) that must be on file before the ROW Review can be marked Approved.\"\n\nSo a \"completeness check\" by Austin Energy is not the same as an AEU \"clearance letter.\"\n\n\nI should flag both EL-3.1 and EL-3.2 as deficiencies. The ESPA approval isn't documented in the plan set, and while Austin Energy completed a completeness check, that's distinct from providing the formal clearance letter required by EL-3.2. The \"Reviewer Convention\" citation indicates this follows standard practice rather than a specific code requirement. clearance. Since Austin Energy's completeness check doesn't explicitly confirm no conflicts with the project, I should mark this as not-verifiable rather than assuming it satisfies the requirement.\n\nFor the ESPA approval, the documentation is clearly missing from the plan set, so that's a definite fail. I'll document both findings now.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1630,"cache_read_input_tokens":79334,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1630},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7a2037a-f555-4152-8bdc-44008e269230","uuid":"9465ed2d-a44f-4a07-a409-15280ac4f52a"}
