area**:\nThere are no overhead utilities, power lines (such as standard \"OHE\" lines seen elsewhere on the drawing), overhead structures, or tree canopies shown encroaching directly over the dashed rectangle marking the \"Staging and Storage Area\". It appears to be an open area. There is a \"Tree Protection (Typ.)\" zone labeled just to the northeast of it, but it does not overlap the staging rectangle.\n\n4) **Location of the \"Maintenance Access Drive\"**:\nA specifically labeled \"Maintenance Access Drive\" is not found on this plan. There are, however, two access points labeled \"Stabilized Construction Entrance\" located on the western boundary—one at the northwest corner and one at the southwest corner. \n\n5) **Clearance dimensions on the maintenance access drive**:\nNot applicable, as a \"Maintenance Access Drive\" is not explicitly labeled or dimensioned on this specific sheet.\n\n6) **Overall layout showing staging areas relative to buildings and utilities**:\n*   **Location**: The \"Staging and Storage Area\" is located on the western perimeter of the development.\n*   **Relative to Buildings**: It is situated directly west of \"Bldg. 2\", north of \"Bldg. 8\", and south of the northern \"Stabilized Construction Entrance\".\n*   **Relative to Utilities**: It is adjacent to the western property boundary, where underground water lines (labeled \"8\" W.L.\") are routed. A sanitary sewer manhole (\"Wastewater MH\") is located further to the northwest near the entrance. Overhead electric lines (labeled \"OHE\") are shown running along the southern and eastern boundaries of the overall site plan, but they are far removed from this western staging area."}]}
