{"level":30,"time":1776954519118,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0136L98YygBLGcdRhqby2siV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the site. Let me work through the checklist items systematically:\n\n## APPLICABILITY ANALYSIS:\n\n**Site Facts:**\n- Address: 3759 Valley View Road\n- Zoning: MF-2 (Multi-Family)\n- No Regulating Plan (not Plaza Saltillo TOD, NBG, Hill Country Corridor)\n- Valley View Road: LOCAL STREET (not CTC or Urban Roadway per Subchapter E)\n- Utilities: Underground electrical lines proposed; water/wastewater lines proposed; detention pond in NE corner\n- Multiple recorded easements, including TWO (2010070731 and 2011021137) NOT depicted on submitted plans\n\n## CHECKLIST ITEM EVALUATION:\n\n**EL-2.1** — Utility lines not placed underground from building to property line on CTC or Urban Roadway\n- **Status: N/A** — Site fronts Valley View Road, which is a LOCAL STREET, not a CTC or Urban Roadway per Subchapter E § 2.2.2.B.3. This requirement does not apply.\n\n**EL-2.2** — All on-site utility lines not underground in Hill Country Roadway Corridor\n- **Status: N/A** — Site is on Valley View Road in South Austin. Hill Country corridors (Loop 360, RM 620, RM 2222, RM 2244, Southwest Parkway) are not in the immediate vicinity. No evidence site is within 1,000 feet of any Hill Country Roadway.\n\n**EL-2.3** — Utility lines in ROW not placed underground or relocated to rear on CTC\n- **Status: N/A** — Site does not front a CTC per Subchapter E.\n\n**EL-2.4** — Utility lines in ROW not placed underground or relocated on Urban Roadway\n\n\n- **Status: N/A** — Valley View Road is a local street, not an Urban Roadway per Subchapter E.\n\n**EL-2.5 through EL-2.7** — Utilities not underground on Plaza Saltillo TOD streets (Core Transit Corridor, Pedestrian Priority Street, Local Street)\n- **Status: N/A** — No regulating plan applies to this site, so these requirements are inapplicable.\n\n**EL-2.8** —\n\nUtilities not underground within NBG Zoning District\n- **Status: N/A** — The site is zoned MF-2, falling outside the NBG district.\n\n**EL-2.9** — Building portion within 10-foot radius of energized overhead conductor\n- **Status: PASS** — An existing overhead electric line runs along Valley View Road in the public right-of-way, but doesn't extend over any buildings. All proposed structures are positioned well away from the Valley View Road property line, and electrical service is routed underground from Valley View Road into the site, eliminating any conflict with energized conductors.\n\n**EL-2.10** — Utilities routed underneath detention or retention pond\n- **Status: PASS** — The Biofiltration-Detention Pond Plan confirms no site utilities cross through or beneath the pond.\n\nOnly internal drainage pipes exist within the pond structure.\n\n**EL-2.11** — Austin Water mains/services within designated ROW planting zone\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE** — The Landscape Plan shows three street yard trees along Valley View Road but doesn't explicitly mark planting zone boundaries or root barriers. Without dimensional details, I can't confirm whether Austin Water infrastructure complies with planting zone requirements.\n\n**EL-2.12** — Utility exclusion planting zone contains Austin Water infrastructure\n- **Status: N/A** — No utility exclusion planting zones are explicitly delineated on the landscape plan.\n\n**EL-2.13** — Transformers/utility boxes within parkland boundaries\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE** — Facts.md confirms a Parkland Deficient Area exists but doesn't specify parkland boundary locations. The electrical plan shows four transformer pads on customer property inside the property line, yet without precise parkland boundary data, I cannot definitively determine whether transformers fall within parkland limits. City verification of parkland mapping is needed.\n\n**EL-2.14** — New utilities routed through/adjacent to light rail corridor without UROP consultation or Downtown Rail Corridor Permit\n- **Status: N/A** — The site has no proximity to any light rail guideway alignment or Project Connect corridors.\n\n**EL-2.15** — Utility easement boundary encroaches into proposed public ROW\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE** — Multiple easements are documented in Facts.md (recorded 2010-2011), but the plat only shows 1975 easements. The Greenbelt Access and Drainage easements from 2010-2011 don't appear on the plat, so I cannot verify whether they encroach into the proposed ROW without seeing their actual boundaries overlaid on the improvements.\n\n**EL-2.16** — Items placed within utility easement without License Agreement\n- **Status: FAIL** — Facts.md explicitly notes the Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (2010070731) is not depicted on the site plan and must be added before approval, designating a 0.31 ac no-build zone in the NE interior.  The City of Austin Drainage Easement (2011021137) covering 0.13 ac in the NE corner is also missing from the site plan, along with several other GIS-confirmed easements. Four transformer pads are shown but lack documentation of dedicated Austin Energy easements, required License Agreements under UCM § 1.10.10.3, or City Manager licenses per § 14-11-41. Sheet 9 notes \"Additional electric easements may be required at a later date,\" confirming the AE easement documentation is incomplete—a critical deficiency since utility infrastructure is depicted without corresponding easement encumbrances or licenses.\n\n**EL-2.17** — Private utilities located in public ROW not relocated to private property or easement\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE** — Sheets 19-20 show utility tap connections, but without precise ROW boundary mapping overlaid on the utility plans, I cannot determine if private utilities remain in the public ROW. The documented connections appear to reference public utilities rather than private utilities proposed to stay in the ROW.\n\n**EL-2.18** — Abandoned utilities creating clearance conflicts not removed\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE** — The existing building was demolished in June 2022 under permit 2022-096813. Facts.md notes this, but the site plan\n\n's Tree Removal & Demolition Plan (Sheet 8) does not show specific details about abandoned utility lines or demolition of old electrical infrastructure, making it impossible to verify whether conflicting abandoned utilities were actually removed.\n\n**EL-2.19** — Public/franchise utilities in ROW not terminated at property line\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE** — Precise ROW mapping is needed to confirm proper termination. Sheet 19 documents a tap to the existing public water line, but actual abandonment or termination of old service connections is not documented in the materials reviewed.\n\n**EL-2.20** — Underground storage tanks not at adequate distance from utility easements\n- **Status: N/A** — No underground storage tanks are registered on the site per Facts.md.\n\n**EL-2.21** — Power pole relocation not coordinated with Austin Energy\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE** — Poles exist in the public ROW along Valley View Road, but no pole relocation documentation or coordination letters with Austin Energy are evident on the electrical plan. Sheet 9 references \"Additional electric easements may be required\" without any supporting Austin Energy coordination letters in the supplementary documents.\n\n**EL-2.22** — Transformer pad not sized per AE Design specs, clearances not met, not accessible, or lacks AE easement\n- **Status: FAIL** — Multiple critical issues identified. The Site Plan Release Notes on Sheet 9 state that \"Additional electric easements may be required at a later date,\" indicating transformers lack a dedicated AE easement. Vision analysis identifies four transformer pads in landscape and courtyard areas, but clearance measurements to buildings are not documented, the required 10-foot clearance from buildings is not explicitly verified, and 6-foot parking proximity requirements are not confirmed.\n\nPad dimensions lack AE Design specification documentation, with Sheet 21 showing only transformer symbols without dimensions or design approval. Additionally, no AE License Agreement is provided, consistent with deficiencies noted in EL-2.16.\n\n**EL-2.23** — Tree wells without electrical outlet for seasonal lighting\n- **Status: N/A** — The landscape plan (Sheet 31) contains no explicitly labeled tree wells or standard hardscape tree well symbols. Trees are shown within continuous landscape beds and open spaces rather than isolated wells.\n\n**EL-2.24** — Electric/telecom utility lines routed through parking\n- **Status: N/A** — Table B requirements apply only to nonresidential zoning districts (NO, P, LO, GO, CR, LR, GR, W/LO, CS, CS-1, CH, IP, MI, R&D) or specific residential surface parking conditions. The MF-2 zoning designation does not trigger these applicability thresholds.\n\n## SUMMARY OF FINDINGS:\n\n**Pass (Not reported):**\n- EL-2.1 through EL-2.8 (n/a)\n- EL-2.9 (pass)\n- EL-2.\n\n10 (pass)\n- EL-2.12, EL-2.14, EL-2.20, EL-2.23, EL-2.24 (n/a)\n\n**Not-Verifiable (Report):**\n- EL-2.11 — Cannot verify AW planting zone compliance due to missing dimensional planting zone data\n- EL-2.13 — Cannot verify transformer placement relative to parkland without parkland boundary information\n- EL-2.15 — Cannot verify easement or ROW encroachment without critical easement depictions\n- EL-2.17 — Cannot verify private utility locations in ROW without ROW boundary mapping\n- EL-2.18 — Cannot verify abandoned utility status without demolition detail review\n- EL-2.19 — Cannot verify public utility termination without ROW mapping or termination documentation\n- EL-2.21 — Cannot verify pole relocation coordination; no AE letters provided and relocation necessity unclear\n\n**Fail (Report):**\n- EL-2.16 — Utilities in easements lack License Agreements; AE easements undocumented and no licenses provided\n- EL-2.22 — Transformer pad missing AE easement documentation, clearance details, design specifications, and license agreement","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1576,"cache_read_input_tokens":67327,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1576},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9a5665b-9006-428b-bc9b-c42e794b3bcd","uuid":"7868ac94-8c75-431c-a2e1-c96f47535879"}
