-3.18, EL-3.20 through EL-3.22 (N/A) - Street lighting not included in scope\n- EL-3.19 (N/A) - Electrical plans adequately cover required areas\n- EL-3.23 (N/A) - AUL\n\nCC applicability hinges on ROW utility linear footage, but I don't see clear evidence of utility pole relocation or 300+ linear feet of ROW work. EL-3.24 through EL-3.27 (N/A) - No conflicts identified with Gattan, telecom, dry utilities, or CIP; internal utilities serve private development. ROW utility coordination case may not trigger if AULCC threshold isn't met. EL-3.30 (N/A) - No new public street names evident; private roads use unit numbers rather than street names per the address plan. EL-3.31 (NOT-VERIFIABLE) - I need to verify this further since I cannot locate evidence of approved addressing in the materials provided.\n\nEL-3.32 passes - transmission easement notes are thorough and documented. Looking back at EL-3.31 more carefully: the requirement applies when new addresses are created, and this project does create 39 new unit addresses. The standard requires an approved addressing plan separate from an Address Validation Letter, but I only see the AVL in the record, not a distinct approved plan. This appears to be a deficiency that should be flagged.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1963,"cache_read_input_tokens":80964,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1963},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7a2037a-f555-4152-8bdc-44008e269230","uuid":"b4578d36-7f2a-4602-86f7-fcbb9db9e144"}
