{"level":30,"time":1776954539861,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":15,"prompt":"Please analyze the biofiltration-detention pond plan and identify: (1) The exact location and boundary of the detention/biofiltration pond footprint. (2) Identify any utility lines (electric, water, wastewater, storm drain) shown on or crossing under the pond area. (3) Identify the location of any utility easements within or adjacent to the pond area. (4) Show the routing of any underground utility lines relative to the pond perimeter. (5) Check for any annotations about utility coordination or clearances related to the pond.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Biofiltration-Detention Pond Plan & Calculations\" document, here are the findings addressing your specific requests:\n\n**(1) Exact location and boundary of the detention/biofiltration pond footprint:**\n*   **Location:** The pond is located in the upper portion of the plan, situated immediately to the north of the building footprint labeled **\"Unit 501\"**.\n*   **Boundary:** The footprint is explicitly bounded on the north, east, west, and partially on the south by structures labeled **\"Concrete Structural Retaining Wall w/ Fall Protection Railing (By Others)\"**.\n*   **Internal Layout:** The pond footprint is divided into two primary sections:\n    *   A **\"Sedimentation\"** chamber on the western side.\n    *   A filtration area on the eastern side containing **\"Top of Biofiltration Media FL = 672.00\"**.\n    *   These two sections are separated by a internal **\"Rock Flow Spreader 6\"-12\" (H) x 3'(W) 3-8\" Dia. Rock\"**.\n\n**(2) Utility lines (electric, water, wastewater, storm drain) shown on or crossing under the pond area:**\n*   **Storm Drain (-SD-):**\n    *   A storm drain line physically penetrates the western retaining wall, labeled: **\"24\\\" Pipe Through Pond Wall FL IN 24\\\" 672.34\"**.\n    *   Internal to the biofiltration area (underneath), there is a network of storm drain underdrains labeled **\"6\\\" Perforated PVC @ 1.27%\"** and **\"6\\\" Perforated PVC @ 1.00%\"**, connecting to a **\"Cleanout FL 6\\\" 669.75\"**.\n    *   An outfall pipe exits through the eastern retaining wall, labeled: **\"6\\\" PVC Raised Outlet Pipe See Detail 1.6.7.C-3 FL IN 6\\\" 669.31\"** discharging to a pipe labeled **\"- SD -\"**.\n*   **Electric (-E-):** An underground electric line is shown, but it does *not* cross under the pond. It is located just outside the pond's western boundary.\n*   **Wastewater (-WW-):** An underground wastewater line is shown, but it does *not* cross under the pond. It is located outside the pond's southern boundary.\n*   **Water (-W-):** No water lines are visible crossing under or into the pond footprint in this view.\n\n**(3) Location of any utility easements within or adjacent to the pond area:**\n*   Based on this specific plan sheet, there are **no explicitly labeled utility easements** (e.g., standard \"10' P.U.E.\" or \"Drainage Easement\" dashed boundaries) visible within or immediately crossing the pond's footprint. There is an **\"8' Wide Maintenance Ramp 4:1 Max Slope\"** adjacent to the west wall, providing access, but this is not labeled as a utility easement.\n\n**(4) Routing of any underground utility lines relative to the pond perimeter:**\n*   **Electric (-E-):** Routes generally north-south, running parallel to and just outside the western perimeter retaining wall, adjacent to the maintenance ramp.\n*   **Wastewater (-WW-):** Routes diagonally (roughly southwest to northeast) immediately south of the pond's southern retaining wall, passing close to the corner of \"Unit 501\".\n*   **Storm Drain (-SD-) (External):** In addition to the lines penetrating the east and west walls, there is a separate storm drain line labeled **\"- SD -\"** routing east-west, running parallel to and just outside the northern perimeter retaining wall.\n\n**(5) Annotations about utility coordination or clearances related to the pond:**\n*   There are no specific dimensional clearance annotations (e.g., \"maintain 5' clearance from wall\") attached to the utilities near the pond.\n*   However, there is a general utility coordination annotation located in the standard notes block in the bottom right corner of the document. It reads exactly as follows:\n    > \"The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\"","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1419,"outputTokens":957,"totalTokens":5589,"reasoningTokens":3213},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2119648]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Jus