{"level":30,"time":1776954546822,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F35Ws43jDFSqBywQ1FHLJF","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 19 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: diagram — A legend explaining the symbols and line types used in the site plan diagram for various utilities.\n     4→\n     5→### Legend\n     6→| Symbol | Description |\n     7→| :--- | :--- |\n     8→| W | Existing Water Line |\n     9→| W | Proposed Water Line |\n    10→| [Solid Square Symbol] | Single Water Service |\n    11→| [Split Square Symbol] | Double Water Service |\n    12→| WW | Existing Wastewater Line |\n    13→| WW | Proposed Wastewater Line |\n    14→| [Dashed Line] | Wastewater Service |\n    15→| RW | Existing Reclaimed Water Line |\n    16→| RW | Proposed Reclaimed Water Line |\n    17→| E | Proposed Underground Electric |\n    18→| SD | Proposed Storm Drain |\n    19→| [FH Symbol] | Fire Hydrant |\n    20→| [Valve Symbol] | Gate Valve |\n    21→| [AARV Symbol] | AARV |\n    22→| [T Symbol] | Transformer Pad |\n    23→\n    24→## Block 2: drawing — The main diagram showing the layout of the townhomes, including buildings, units, utility lines (water, wastewater, electric, storm drain), fire hydrants, cleanouts, and other site features. It includes numerous annotations and specific measurements for the utility infrastructure.\n    25→\n    26→[Detailed diagram showing the layout of multiple buildings labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8, each containing multiple units. The diagram includes extensive utility routing with lines for water (W), wastewater (WW), and storm drain (SD). There are numerous callouts for specific components like '6\" Cleanout Traffic Bearing', 'Air Spade Trench', 'Duplex Grinder Pump Lift Station', 'Fire Demand Meter', and 'PVC Wastewater Service Line'. Topographic lines and elevations are also visible. Various easements and setbacks are marked. The layout is bounded by 'Valley View Road' to the west.]\n    27→\n    28→## Block 3: notes — A note indicating the requirement for a pressure reducing valve for lots/structures with high water pressure.\n    29→\n    30→### PRV Note\n    31→Lots/Structure with 65 psi or greater require a pressure reducing valve, set at 65 psi, to be installed on the property owner's side of the right of way.\n    32→\n    33→## Block 4: notes — A brief note directing the reader to the landscape plan sheet for the tree list.\n    34→\n    35→### Tree List\n    36→Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n    37→\n    38→## Block 5: notes — A table listing the Drainage Fixture Units (DFU's) for each building, broken down by building type (e.g., 4Plex, 5Plex, 6Plex).\n    39→\n    40→### Drainage Fixture Unit Table\n    41→| Building # | Building Type | DFU's |\n    42→| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n    43→| 1 | 4Plex | 136 |\n    44→| 2 | 6Plex | 204 |\n    45→| 3 | 5Plex | 170 |\n    46→| 4 | 5Plex | 170 |\n    47→| 5 | 4Plex | 136 |\n    48→| 6 | 4Plex | 136 |\n    49→| 7 | 5Plex | 170 |\n    50→| 8 | 6Plex | 204 |\n    51→\n    52→## Block 6: notes\n    53→\n    54→## Block 7: notes — A note detailing the requirements for restraining joints on water line components.\n    55→\n    56→### Restrained Joints for all Water Line Bends, Tees, Gate Valves & Ends\n    57→All horizontal and vertical water line bends, tee's, gate valves and dead end's shall be restrained to the water main using factory restrained joint pipe as approved in SPL WW-27F, or, mechanical joint restraint devices as approved in SPL WW-27A.\n    58→\n    59→## Block 8: notes — The legal description of the property.\n    60→\n    61→### Legal Description\n    62→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    63→\n    64→## Block 9: notes — A disclaimer regarding the accuracy of existing utility locations shown on the plans, requiring the contractor to field verify.\n    65→\n    66→The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n    67→\n    68→## Block 11: table — The logo and contact information for Bleyl Engineering, the firm responsible for the planning, design, and management of the project.\n    69→\n    70→### Bleyl Engineering\n    71→Planning • Design • Management\n    72→7701 San Felipe Blvd., Suite 200, Austin TX 78729\n    73→Texas Firm Registration No. F-678\n    74→Tel. 512-454-2400\n    75→www.bleylengineering.com\n    76→\n    77→Austin | Bryan | Conroe | Houston\n    78→\n    79→## Block 12: table — A note regarding the requirements for private fire hydrants, including compliance with the Austin Fire Code and annual maintenance.\n    80→\n    81→### City of Austin - Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division\n    82→(512) 972-1060\n    83→This project has private hydrants located within the property. The property owner is required to comply with Austin Fire Code. Failure to comply may result in civil and/or criminal remedies available to the City. The performance of this obligation shall always rest with the owner or record. Fire hydrants on private property are required to serviced, maintained and flowed annually, using a contractor registered with the City to provide this service. This project includes __1__ private hydrants.\n    84→\n    85→## Block 14: text_block — Information about the benchmarks used for the project, including elevation and location details.\n    86→\n    87→### Benchmarks\n    88→B.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    89→Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    90→\n    91→B.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    92→Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    93→\n    94→## Block 16: text_block — A list of utility notes instructing the contractor to verify existing utility locations, notify the engineer of conflicts, and specifying pipe materials for private domestic water and wastewater branches.\n    95→\n    96→### Utility Notes\n    97→1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n    98→2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n    99→3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tubing. See Detail 520-AW-01B\n   100→4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the buildings are to be 6\" PVC @ 2.0% min. See Detail 520-AW-01C\n   101→\n   102→## Block 17: text_block — A disclaimer regarding the verification of data and calculations, stating the engineer's responsibility.\n   103→\n   104→Release of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n   105→\n   106→## Block 19: text_block\n   107→\n   108→## Block 20: text_block — A general note stating that the project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule and requires inspection by a geologist for trenches deeper than 5 feet.\n   109→\n   110→### Note\n   111→This project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM) provision that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\n   112→\n   113→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"401e6f81-2db8-4fbd-be98-34356fe0baff","uuid":"f7837625-586c-4c17-a9cf-a5133ef15473","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-19/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 19 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — A legend explaining the symbols and line types used in the site plan diagram for various utilities.\n\n### Legend\n| Symbol | Description |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| W | Existing Water Line |\n| W | Proposed Water Line |\n| [Solid Square Symbol] | Single Water Service |\n| [Split Square Symbol] | Double Water Service |\n| WW | Existing Wastewater Line |\n| WW | Proposed Wastewater Line |\n| [Dashed Line] | Wastewater Service |\n| RW | Existing Reclaimed Water Line |\n| RW | Proposed Reclaimed Water Line |\n| E | Proposed Underground Electric |\n| SD | Proposed Storm Drain |\n| [FH Symbol] | Fire Hydrant |\n| [Valve Symbol] | Gate Valve |\n| [AARV Symbol] | AARV |\n| [T Symbol] | Transformer Pad |\n\n## Block 2: drawing — The main diagram showing the layout of the townhomes, including buildings, units, utility lines (water, wastewater, electric, storm drain), fire hydrants, cleanouts, and other site features. It includes numerous annotations and specific measurements for the utility infrastructure.\n\n[Detailed diagram showing the layout of multiple buildings labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8, each containing multiple units. The diagram includes extensive utility routing with lines for water (W), wastewater (WW), and storm drain (SD). There are numerous callouts for specific components like '6\" Cleanout Traffic Bearing', 'Air Spade Trench', 'Duplex Grinder Pump Lift Station', 'Fire Demand Meter', and 'PVC Wastewater Service Line'. Topographic lines and elevations are also visible. Various easements and setbacks are marked. The layout is bounded by 'Valley View Road' to the west.]\n\n## Block 3: notes — A note indicating the requirement for a pressure reducing valve for lots/structures with high water pressure.\n\n### PRV Note\nLots/Structure with 65 psi or greater require a pressure reducing valve, set at 65 psi, to be installed on the property owner's side of the right of way.\n\n## Block 4: notes — A brief note directing the reader to the landscape plan sheet for the tree list.\n\n### Tree List\nRefer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n\n## Block 5: notes — A table listing the Drainage Fixture Units (DFU's) for each building, broken down by building type (e.g., 4Plex, 5Plex, 6Plex).\n\n### Drainage Fixture Unit Table\n| Building # | Building Type | DFU's |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 1 | 4Plex | 136 |\n| 2 | 6Plex | 204 |\n| 3 | 5Plex | 170 |\n| 4 | 5Plex | 170 |\n| 5 | 4Plex | 136 |\n| 6 | 4Plex | 136 |\n| 7 | 5Plex | 170 |\n| 8 | 6Plex | 204 |\n\n## Block 6: notes\n\n## Block 7: notes — A note detailing the requirements for restraining joints on water line components.\n\n### Restrained Joints for all Water Line Bends, Tees, Gate Valves & Ends\nAll horizontal and vertical water line bends, tee's, gate valves and dead end's shall be restrained to the water main using factory restrained joint pipe as approved in SPL WW-27F, or, mechanical joint restraint devices as approved in SPL WW-27A.\n\n## Block 8: notes — The legal description of the property.\n\n### Legal Description\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n## Block 9: notes — A disclaimer regarding the accuracy of existing utility locations shown on the plans, requiring the contractor to field verify.\n\nThe location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n\n## Block 11: table — The logo and contact information for Bleyl Engineering, the firm responsible for the planning, design, and management of the project.\n\n### Bleyl Engineering\nPlanning • Design • Management\n7701 San Felipe Blvd., Suite 200, Austin TX 78729\nTexas Firm Registration No. F-678\nTel. 512-454-2400\nwww.bleylengineering.com\n\nAustin | Bryan | Conroe | Houston\n\n## Block 12: table — A note regarding the requirements for private fire hydrants, including compliance with the Austin Fire Code and annual maintenance.\n\n### City of Austin - Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division\n(512) 972-1060\nThis project has private hydrants located within the property. The property owner is required to comply with Austin Fire Code. Failure to comply may result in civil and/or criminal remedies available to the City. The performance of this obligation shall always rest with the owner or record. Fire hydrants on private property are required to serviced, maintained and flowed annually, using a contractor registered with the City to provide this service. This project includes __1__ private hydrants.\n\n## Block 14: text_block — Information about the benchmarks used for the project, including elevation and location details.\n\n### Benchmarks\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n## Block 16: text_block — A list of utility notes instructing the contractor to verify existing utility locations, notify the engineer of conflicts, and specifying pipe materials for private domestic water and wastewater branches.\n\n### Utility Notes\n1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tubing. See Detail 520-AW-01B\n4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the buildings are to be 6\" PVC @ 2.0% min. See Detail 520-AW-01C\n\n## Block 17: text_block — A disclaimer regarding the verification of data and calculations, stating the engineer's responsibility.\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n\n## Block 19: text_block\n\n## Block 20: text_block — A general note stating that the project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule and requires inspection by a geologist for trenches deeper than 5 feet.\n\n### Note\nThis project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM) provision that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\n\n","numLines":113,"startLine":1,"totalLines":113}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776954548859,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01LxFxR13MugnwrosX2d3U3E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've successfully returned the structured output with the 13 findings (7 fail + 6 not-verifiable) that I identified from the EL-3 grouping review. The evaluation is complete. \n\nItems marked as PASS or N/A were excluded from the output as required:\n- PASS items: EL-3.2, EL-3.6, EL-3.19 (and others like EL-3.8, EL-3.9, EL-3.13, EL-3.14, EL-3.15, EL-3.16, EL-3.17, EL-3.18, EL-3.20, EL-3.21, EL-3.22, EL-3.27, EL-3.30, EL-3.32)\n- N/A items: EL-3.3, EL-3.8, EL-3.9, EL-3.13, EL-3.14, EL-3.15, EL-3.16, EL-3.17, EL-3.18, EL-3.20, EL-3.21, EL-3.22, EL-3.30 (some are both N/A and not-verifiable, but I made determination calls)\n\nActually, looking back at my analysis, I may have been inconsistent on some items. Let me verify my logic:\n\n- EL-3.30: I marked as Not-Verifiable, but if no new streets/drive names are proposed, it should be N/A. The instructions say this applies \"Only when new streets or private drives are proposed.\" Without clear evidence of NEW proposed street/drive names (beyond Valley View Road which is existing), this should arguably be N/A. But I marked Not-Verifiable because I couldn't determine from the documents if there were new drive names. This seems reasonable - if unclear, Not-Verifiable is appropriate.\n\n\n- EL-3.32: I need to double-check this one. The vision analysis found 16 Electric Transmission Notes on Sheet 3, which should cover most of the AEDC 1.16.0(8) requirements. But I need to confirm all eight required items are actually present and that they appear on the plat sheet itself (Sheet 2), not just the transmission sheet. The required notes include AE tree pruning rights and additional easements, among others.\n\nLooking at what the vision analysis identified: tree pruning language appears in Note 3, easement/access provisions are mentioned, erosion control and tree protection show up in Note 3, clearance maintenance is in Note 4, NESC compliance restrictions are in Item 16, and 24-hour AE access requirements are documented. I should verify the remaining items (road capacity and construction notice requirements) are also present to confirm full compliance. The requirement calls for \"48-hour notice to AE before construction or grading within a transmission easement\" per AEDC 1.16.0(8)(viii), but Sheet 3 only states \"Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading\" without specifying the 48-hour timeframe. The sheet does reference contacting Andrew Perez to schedule a meeting, which suggests advance coordination but lacks the explicit notice period. Since I need to verify whether these notes actually appear on the plat sheet itself, and given the language discrepancy, EL-3.32 could potentially be flagged as not-verifiable or fail depending on what's documented. I'm reconsidering whether to include it in my assessment. 3, I can't verify that all eight required notes appear on the actual plat sheet itself, or whether the specific 48-hour language is included.\n\nI need to mark EL-3.32 as not-verifiable since the notes' presence on a general sheet doesn't necessarily fulfill the requirement for them to be on the plat sheet specifically.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7018,"cache_read_input_tokens":72808,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7018},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a7253b0-d093-45b5-84cb-fd14b5436b5c","uuid":"6f0be870-cd83-4c2a-9148-ac0c