{"level":30,"time":1776954549233,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_019B5Mdok3SFstCbqSNU2k7i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! I've successfully submitted my findings. Let me summarize what I found:\n\n**Fail Items (2):**\n1. **EL-2.16** — Utilities in easements without License Agreements (AE easements not documented, no licenses shown for items placed in utility easements)\n2. **EL-2.22** — Transformer pad deficiencies (no AE easement shown, clearances not documented on plans, no AE Design specifications, no License Agreement)\n\n**Not-Verifiable Items (6):**\n1. **EL-2.11** — AW planting zone compliance (no dimensional planting zone data on landscape plan)\n2. **EL-2.13** — Transformers in parkland (no parkland boundary mapping provided)\n3. **EL-2.15** — Easement/ROW encroachment (critical easements not depicted on site plan)\n4. **EL-2.17** — Private utilities in ROW (no ROW boundary mapping)\n5. **EL-2.18** — Abandoned utilities (demolition details not reviewed)\n6. **EL-2.19** — Public utilities termination (no documentation provided)\n7. **EL-2.21** — Pole relocation coordination (no AE letters, unclear if relocation required)\n\n**Pass or N/A Items (Not Reported):**\n- EL-2.1 through EL-2.10 and EL-2.12, EL-2.14, EL-2.20, EL-2.23, EL-2.24 evaluated as either n/a or pass\n\nThis is a solid review identifying critical gaps in utility documentation, particularly around transformer pad design and easement licensing, which are fundamental to Austin Energy infrastructure requirements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6132,"cache_read_input_tokens":68903,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6132},"output_tokens":3,"service