here any drainage easements, wastewater easements, electric easements, or public utility easements shown?**\nYes, all four types of easements are shown and explicitly labeled on this plat:\n*   **Drainage:** Labeled as `26' Drainage Easement (Existing)` in Lot 2.\n*   **Wastewater:** Labeled as `10' Wastewater Line Easement` in Lot 2.\n*   **Electric:** Labeled as `Exist. 5' Elec. Ease.` (Lot 1) and `5' Elec. Ease.` (Lot 2).\n*   **Public Utility:** Labeled as `5' P.U.E. (Exist.)` (Lot 1).\n\n**3. Are there any easements labeled as \"Greenbelt Access,\" \"Drainage,\" or similar in the NE corner of Lot 1?**\n**No.** There are no easements labeled \"Greenbelt Access\" or \"Drainage\" in the northeast corner of Lot 1. The only easement located in that immediate area is the `5' P.U.E. (Exist.)` running along the northern boundary. The drainage easement is located entirely within Lot 2.\n\n**4. What is the scale and confirm the sheet number?**\n*   **Scale:** Under the \"LEGEND\" section at the bottom center, it is listed as `Scale 1\" = 100 Feet`.\n*   **Sheet Number:** In the title block in the bottom right corner, it is listed exactly as `Sheet: 2 of 39`.\n\n**5. What date was this plat recorded and what is the plat reference number?**\n*   **Recording Date:** According to the \"FILED FOR RECORD\" section on the middle-left side of the document, the plat was \"...duly recorded on the `11` day of `Dec` A.D. `1975` at `2:15` o'clock `P.` M.\"\n*   **Plat Reference Number:** The top header of the document reads `TRAVIS COUNTY PLAT VOLUME 73 PAGE 76`. The recording stamp text also confirms it was recorded \"...in Book `73`, Page `76`\".","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1428,"outputTokens":781,"totalTokens":5048,"reasoningTokens":2839},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1618032]"},{"type":"text