{"level":30,"time":1776954591843,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01GyLrmtkbRKRzGMsLA73ztp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"From this grep search, I see references to \"field verify locations of utility crossings\" but no specific mention of:\n- Clearances at utility crossings\n- Separation dimensions\n- Crossing methods (trenchless vs open-cut)\n- Joint trench agreements\n\nThe only crossing-related details I found are for water service taps and sewer cleanouts, not electrical-to-other-utility crossings.\n\nBased on my comprehensive review, here are the deficiencies I've identified:\n\n1. **EL-1.18** - Demolition plan sequence notes do not address required safety clearances from transmission lines\n   - Status: FAIL\n   - Deficiency: Sheet 8 Block 9 (Site Demolition Notes) has 10 notes but lacks the 4 required transmission safety clearance items\n   - Missing: Pre-construction safety meeting ≥48 hrs, barricades 10 ft, warning signs, prohibition on materials in easement\n   - Code: UCM 1.14.9\n\n2. **EL-1.21** - Plans do not include a requirement for field verification of all utility separations and clearances during construction and prior to final acceptance\n   - Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE or FAIL\n   - The plans mention \"field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction\" but don't explicitly state \"during construction and prior to final acceptance\"\n   - This is incomplete/ambiguous\n   - Code: Reviewer Convention\n\n3. **EL-1.22** - SCM staging area vertical clearance from existing and proposed vegetation and all other objects not demonstrated at minimum 14 ft\n   - Status: FAIL\n   - Deficiency: Sheet 5 shows \"Staging and Storage Area\" but NO 14-ft vertical clearance dimension is labeled\n   - The pond is 6,388 cf (>5,000 cf) and 3.65 ft depth (>3 ft), so exemption doesn't apply\n   - Code: DCM 1.2.4.E.2.e\n\n4. **EL-1.23** - Maintenance access drive vertical clearance from existing and proposed vegetation and all other objects not demonstrated at minimum 14 ft\n   - Status: FAIL\n   - Deficiency: Sheet 15 shows \"8' Wide Concrete Maintenance Path\" and \"8' Wide Maintenance Ramp\" but NO 14-ft vertical clearance dimension is labeled\n   - The pond exceeds exemption thresholds\n   - Code: DCM 1.2.4.E.1.e.ii\n\n5. **EL-1.26** - Overhead electrical clear ance zones not graphically delineated on plans\n   - Status: FAIL\n   - Deficiency: OHE lines appear on the site plan perimeter without any clearance envelope graphics. Missing graphical representation of the 7.5-ft horizontal sky-to-ground boundary and 15-ft radial zone from overhead conductors. No transmission clearance analysis or AE-provided envelope documented.\n   - Code: UCM 1.10.3; UCM 1.14.3.1\n\n6. **EL-1.27** - Horizontal dashed height limit lines not shown on plans\n   - Status: FAIL\n   - Deficiency: Height limit line annotations delineating overhead conductor clearance envelope boundaries are absent from the plans.\n   - Code: UCM 1.10.3\n\n7. **EL-1.28** - Sloped or stepped dashed height limit lines not shown on plans\n   - Status: FAIL (or N/A if the site doesn't have significant grade changes)\n   - Deficiency: Sloped and stepped height limit lines are not shown for non-uniform grade conditions. Since the site has topography variations, this requirement applies.\n   - Code: UCM 1.10.3\n\nI should also verify a few additional items: utility crossings and clearances under EL-1.9/EL-1.10, staging and spoils placement within the transmission easement per EL-1.25, and whether EL-1.1 regarding overhead utility zones applies (likely N/A since Valley View Road is a local street, not a CTC/Urban Roadway). For EL-1.25 specifically, the transmission notes on Sheet 3 Block 20 explicitly prohibit aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging, or spoils areas within 20 feet of transmission wires, so I need to verify compliance with this setback requirement. in the findings. The applicability of EL-1.1 needs clarification—since Valley View Road is classified as a Local Street rather than a Core Transit Corridor or Urban Roadway, this requirement doesn't apply. For the other electrical standards, EL-1.2 and EL-1.3 are triggered by the overhead distribution lines visible along the perimeter, while EL-1.6 would only be relevant if customer service equipment like transformers are positioned near poles (though these appear to be underground installations). EL-1.7 similarly depends on whether overhead service drops exist, which the plans suggest are underground. I need to continue evaluating which remaining items are actually applicable to this project.\n\nSince demolition is proposed, EL-1.18 becomes relevant. The key question is whether transmission safety clearance notes appearing in the general notes on Sheet 3 satisfy the requirement, or if they must be specifically included in the demolition plan notes on Sheet 8. The standard explicitly references \"demolition plan sequence notes,\" not general notes, so the absence of these safety requirements from the dedicated demolition notes section constitutes a deficiency. My assessment identifies seven items as deficiencies: EL-1.18 for missing transmission safety notes in the demolition sequence, EL-1.22 and EL-1.23 for undemonstrated clearances in staging and maintenance areas, EL-1.26 through EL-1.28 for missing delineation of clearance zones and height limit lines, with EL-1.21 possibly incomplete pending field verification.\n\nFor the remaining items like EL-1.9, EL-1.10, and EL-1.12, I need to determine whether crossing details with clearance dimensions are actually shown on the plans. Without explicit crossing detail sheets or dimensional information visible, these would likely fall into the \"not-verifiable\" category rather than definitive failures, since I cannot confirm whether the required information is present or absent from the available documentation. losure specifications not found). The key distinction is whether the plans themselves must contain this information versus whether it needs to exist somewhere in the project documentation. For items like crossing methods that directly affect construction sequencing, the absence from utility plans represents a clear gap. For specifications and agreements that might exist in separate documents, I can only mark them not-verifiable if I haven't seen evidence of them. I'll consolidate around the deficiencies I can definitively identify from what's been provided.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3702,"cache_read_input_tokens":83116,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3702},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"401e6f81-2db8-4fbd-be98-34356fe0baff","uuid":"80f8a5ce-530d-46f8-9170-b8806b0ee66b"}
{"level":30,"time":1776954593419,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_013NE4xWDxWQgQYEMhdqTV4u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Key finding for SCM clearance items:\n- **Staging and Storage Area IS shown** but NO clearance dimensions or height limit lines are indicated\n- **NO maintenance access drives are labeled** on the erosion control plan\n- **NO vertical clearance notations anywhere**\n\nThis is important because:\n- EL-1.22 requires SCM staging area to demonstrate 14-ft vertical clearance (Sheet 5 doesn't show this)\n- EL-1.23 requires maintenance access drive to demonstrate 14-ft vertical clearance (Sheet 5 doesn't have labeled maintenance access drives)\n\nNow let me compile my findings and evaluate each checklist item. Let me create a structured evaluation.\n\n## EVALUATION OF EACH CHECKLIST ITEM:\n\nLet me go through each item:\n\n**EL-1.1** - Building or structure located within 10-ft radius of overhead conductors, or overhead utility zone not graphically delineated\n- **Applicability:** Only when overhead utilities present AND site fronts CTC or Urban Roadway\n- **Facts:** Site is on Valley View Road (LOCAL STREET, not CTC or Urban Roadway) per facts.md\n- **Status:** N/A - The LDC overhead utility zone (10-ft radius) requirement only applies to CTCs and Urban Roadways. Valley View Road is classified as ASMP Level 1 (Local Street)\n\n**EL-1.2** - Customer facilities not maintaining 7-ft 6-in horizontal clearance from AE overhead conductors\n- **Applicability:** Only when overhead electric distribution present\n- **Facts:** Overhead electric line shown on Sheet 21 and Sheet 9\n- **Evidence:** \n  - Proposed transformer pads shown on electrical plan (Sheet 21)\n  - Building locations shown on Site Plan (Sheet 9)\n  - NO horizontal clearance dimensions shown from overhead conductor to transformers or buildings\n- **Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE - Clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to transformer pads and buildings are not shown on the plans. \n\nWithout specific measurements, I can't confirm compliance. The plans should display these dimensions, which suggests this likely fails the requirement. I need to determine if the transformer pads qualify as customer facilities—the definition covers any customer-side structure including tanks and vaults, so customer-provided transformers would fall under this. The electrical plans don't clarify whether these are utility or customer-owned, so I'll treat them as customer-provided for this analysis.\n\n**EL-1.\n\n3** shows the same issue as EL-1.2—no radius dimensions are marked on the drawings, making verification impossible. For **EL-1.4**, the vault requirement only applies if a vault sits near overhead lines. Sheet 20 references a meter vault, but I need to confirm its proximity to the overhead line. The plans lack vault clearance dimensions and there's no AE approval documentation in the file. **EL-1.5** requires clearance measurements from the pole centerline rather than the conductor itself, but since no clearance dimensions appear anywhere on the plans, this can't be verified either.\n\n**EL-1.6** addresses customer service entrance facilities needing 10-ft clearance from AE poles. Meters are shown on Sheet 21, but horizontal clearance dimensions from poles are missing. **EL-1.7** only applies when overhead service drops cross truck traffic areas—the plans show all proposed service as underground, so this doesn't apply. **EL-1.8** involves utilities crossing Texas Gas lines without proper 2-ft clearance or coordination, but no TGS lines appear on the plans. **EL-1.9** requires checking if wastewater and water utilities crossing the site intersect with AE underground conduit, which would need 12-inch clearance at perpendicular crossings—this needs closer examination of the specific crossing locations shown on Sheets 19-21. **EL-1.10** concerns non-AE utilities in joint trenches, which would only be relevant if utilities run parallel to AE conduit.\n\nFor **EL-1.11**, the water tap at Valley View Road is in the ROW and needs verification that it maintains proper spacing from existing facilities. **EL-1.12** addresses whether crossing methods are documented for the water and wastewater utilities shown on Sheets 19-20, which requires confirmation that the plans specify how these utilities cross over or under each other.\n\n**EL-1.13** checks if encasement specs are provided where utilities bore under roads or structures. **EL-1.14** only applies if large-diameter wastewater lines with cleanouts are proposed—need to verify the service line size to determine applicability. **EL-1.15** examines whether storm drain access points on Sheet 12 are positioned too close to overhead utility poles.\n\n**EL-1.16** requires checking if non-electrical utilities run parallel within electrical easements shown across the sheets. **EL-1.17** doesn't apply since the project involves underground development with no new poles. **EL-1.18** flags that the demolition plan on Sheet 8 lacks transmission line safety protocols, specifically missing the 48-hour notification requirement.\n\nThe demolition notes also omit barricading requirements (10-ft from structures), warning signage, and restrictions on storing spoils within transmission easements—all four components are absent. **EL-1.19** requires a 25-ft access corridor with 16-ft vertical clearance adjacent to transmission ROW; Sheet 5 erosion control plans don't show this labeled corridor with dimensions, making it unverifiable or non-compliant. **EL-1.20** appears to address another demolition plan deficiency that needs examination. The biofiltration-detention pond exceeds the 5,000 cubic foot threshold with a water quality volume of 6,388 cubic feet, requiring a 14-foot vertical clearance demonstration for the staging area. Sheet 5 shows the staging area location but lacks any clearance dimension or label. The maintenance access drive also needs this clearance verification for the residential townhome development SCM, and no such dimension is provided on the plans.\n\nFor the work zone access driveway, no height clearance dimensions appear anywhere on the construction documents, making it impossible to verify the required 18-foot clearance below overhead utilities. The staging and spoils area shown on Sheet 5 is not located within a transmission easement based on the vision tool analysis.\n\nRegarding overhead clearance zones, the plans completely lack the required 7.5-foot horizontal and 15-foot radius delineations around the overhead line visible on Sheets 21 and 9—no transmission clearance envelope from the utility company is shown either. Similarly, dashed height limit lines are absent from all plan sheets. For sloped terrain areas where overhead utilities exist, stepped or sloped height limit lines should be graphically indicated but are not present.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":759,"cache_read_input_tokens":67115,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":759},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e121e67-5008-4f73-b228-82e438cca3a3","uuid":"688e58f9-c4df-4d12-834f-0eb35e241bbb"}
