{"level":30,"time":1776954593465,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015wJ1jGfMUHUwhPT69rqjsF","type":"tool_result","content":"    30→## Block 6: notes — This block contains 'Utility Notes' detailing contractor responsibilities regarding existing utilities and specific requirements for private domestic water and wastewater branches. Below the notes are disclaimers about the application not verifying all data and the reliance on record information for existing utilities.\n    31→\n    32→**Utility Notes**\n    33→1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n    34→2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n    35→3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tube per Detail 520-AW-01B\n    36→4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the building are to be 6\" PVC service connections per Detail 520-AW-01C\n    37→\n    38→Release of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n    39→\n    40→The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n    41→\n    42→## Block 7: notes — A small block containing text that references another sheet for profile information.\n    43→\n    44→See Sht. 19\n    45→for Profile\n    46→\n    47→## Block 11: text_block — A block providing the legal description of the property, identifying it as Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision.\n    48→\n    49→**Legal Description**\n    50→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    51→\n    52→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e121e67-5008-4f73-b228-82e438cca3a3","uuid":"fccc31fc-d094-4dc3-a1bc-c4f217ecabde","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/blocks.md","content":"## Block 6: notes — This block contains 'Utility Notes' detailing contractor responsibilities regarding existing utilities and specific requirements for private domestic water and wastewater branches. Below the notes are disclaimers about the application not verifying all data and the reliance on record information for existing utilities.\n\n**Utility Notes**\n1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tube per Detail 520-AW-01B\n4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the building are to be 6\" PVC service connections per Detail 520-AW-01C\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n\nThe location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n\n## Block 7: notes — A small block containing text that references another sheet for profile information.\n\nSee Sht. 19\nfor Profile\n\n## Block 11: text_block — A block providing the legal description of the property, identifying it as Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision.\n\n**Legal Description**\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n","numLines":23,"startLine":30,"totalLines":52}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776954593512,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":12,"prompt":"This is the Storm Sewer Plan. Please examine and describe: 1) Where are the storm drain manholes located on this plan? List each by location relative to buildings. 2) Are there any Austin Energy utility poles marked on this plan? If so, where are they located? 3) What is the horizontal distance between each storm drain manhole and any nearby Austin Energy poles? Are these distances marked or dimensioned? 4) Are there any dimensions or clearances marked between storm drain structures and overhead electric poles? 5) What is the minimum clearance you can observe between any manhole and any pole? Please be specific about locations and use cardinal directions and building references.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided Storm Sewer Plan, here are the answers to your questions:\n\n**1) Where are the storm drain manholes located on this plan? List each by location relative to buildings.**\nThere are three specific structures explicitly labeled as \"SD Manhole\" on this plan. They are located as follows:\n*   **Central Manhole:** Labeled \"SD Manhole / Rim: 681.71\", located centrally between Bldg. 3 (to its north) and Bldg. 4 (to its south).\n*   **East-Central Manhole:** Labeled \"SD Manhole / Rim: 683.76\", located directly north of Bldg. 7 and east of Bldg. 4.\n*   **Southern Manhole:** Labeled \"SD Manhole / Rim: 681.02\", located near the southern property line, directly south of Bldg. 4. \n\n*(Note: There is also an \"Existing Wastewater MH\" in the northwest corner and a \"4'x4' Junction Box\" north of Bldg 5, but these are not storm drain manholes).*\n\n**2) Are there any Austin Energy utility poles marked on this plan? If so, where are they located?**\nThere are **no** utility poles explicitly labeled as \"Austin Energy\" on this plan. \n*   There is one pole labeled explicitly as an \"**AT&T Pole**\" in the northwest corner near the existing wastewater easement.\n*   There is an overhead electric line labeled \"**OHE**\" running along the southern property boundary, which has small circular symbols indicating utility poles along its path (e.g., near the southeast corner and near the southwestern guardrail), but they do not denote ownership by Austin Energy.\n\n**3) What is the horizontal distance between each storm drain manhole and any nearby Austin Energy poles? Are these distances marked or dimensioned?**\nBecause there are no explicitly labeled Austin Energy poles, this cannot be definitively answered. Furthermore, looking at the generic OHE poles and the storm drain manholes, **there are no horizontal distances marked or dimensioned** between any manhole and any utility pole on this plan.\n\n**4) Are there any dimensions or clearances marked between storm drain structures and overhead electric poles?**\n**No.** There are no dimensions, notes, or clearances marked anywhere on this plan indicating the distance between storm drain structures and overhead electric poles.\n\n**5) What is the minimum clearance you can observe between any manhole and any pole? Please be specific about locations and use cardinal directions and building references.**\nBecause there are no dimensions provided for these specific relationships, an exact numerical minimum clearance cannot be determined. \n*   Visually, the closest interaction between a manhole and a utility line/pole occurs at the southern property line. The \"SD Manhole\" (Rim: 681.02) located south of Bldg. 4 is situated near the \"OHE\" line. \n*   While the manhole is visually close to the OHE line itself, the nearest indicated *pole* symbol on that OHE line is situated significantly further east along the southern boundary (south of the Bldg. 7 area). Based strictly on the visual layout without given dimensions, it appears to be several dozen feet away, but a precise clearance cannot be verified from this document.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1449,"outputTokens":709,"totalTokens":4755,"reasoningTokens":2597},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2279472]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"This is the Storm Sewer Plan. Please examine and describe: 1) Where are the storm drain manholes located on this plan? List each by location relative to buildings. 2) Are there any Austin Energy utility poles marked on this plan? If so, where are they located? 3) What is the horizontal distance between each st