{"level":30,"time":1776954724187,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_013vUiuxU8H84jctCxDXPVfu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! I've submitted my findings. Let me review what I included:\n\n1. **EL-1.18** (FAIL) - Demolition plan lacks transmission safety notes\n2. **EL-1.22** (FAIL) - Staging area clearance not demonstrated  \n3. **EL-1.23** (FAIL) - Maintenance access drive clearance not demonstrated\n4. **EL-1.26** (FAIL) - Overhead clearance zones not delineated\n5. **EL-1.27** (FAIL) - Height limit lines not shown\n6. **EL-1.28** (FAIL) - Sloped/stepped height limit lines not shown\n\nI did not include EL-1.21 (field verification) because while it might be incomplete, the plans do include the requirement for field verification of utility crossings prior to beginning construction. The language could be more comprehensive but it's present. I also didn't include the other items that I couldn't definitively verify as fail or not-verifiable from my review.\n\nThe deficiencies are clearly documented with:\n- Code citations from the grouping file\n- Applicable areas identified\n- Sheet references with document and sheet numbers\n- Clear, concise comments explaining the deficiency\n\nAll 6 deficiencies relate to the core requirements of the EL-1 grouping regarding electrical clearances, transmission safety, and overhead utility coordination.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4298,"cache_read_input_tokens":86818,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4298},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"401e6f81-2db8-4fbd-be98-34356fe0ba