{"level":30,"time":1776954724191,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":19,"prompt":"Please analyze the utility tap plan and identify: (1) The routing path of the proposed water and wastewater lines from the site to the public utility connection points (indicating whether they route through Valley View Road). (2) Identify any private utilities that may be shown routing into or through the public right-of-way. (3) Check whether the water or wastewater lines route through or under any parking areas on the site. (4) Identify any references to easements or coordinate with Austin Energy. (5) Note any annotations about coordination with public utilities or relocation of existing utilities.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided Utility Tap Plan, here are the findings corresponding to your requests:\n\n**(1) Routing path of proposed water and wastewater lines from the site to the public utility connection points:**\n*   **Water:** A proposed water line (marked as a solid blue line with \"W\" symbols) routes from the central drive aisle of the site westward, crossing the property boundary to connect to an existing water main within the public right-of-way labeled **\"Valley View Road (60' R.O.W.)\"**. The connection point includes an annotation to \"Install 8\\\" Gate Valve on Existing 8\\\" Water Line\".\n*   **Wastewater:** A proposed wastewater line (marked as a solid purple line with \"WW\" symbols) routes westward from the site's central drive aisle, parallel to the water line, crossing into the **\"Valley View Road (60' R.O.W.)\"**. It connects to the public system with an annotation reading: \"Connect to Existing Wastewater Stub Contractor to Verify Location and Depth Prior to Construction\". \n\n**(2) Private utilities routing into or through the public right-of-way:**\n*   The plans do not explicitly label the tap lines extending into Valley View Road as \"private.\" However, \"Utility Notes\" #3 and #4 state that branch lines to the buildings are private (\"All Private Domestic Water branches to the buildings...\" and \"All Private Wastewater branches to the buildings...\").\n*   The main water line connecting to the public ROW passes through a meter vault located just inside the property line (labeled **\"8\\\" Fire Demand Meter in 8' x 12' Vault\"**). The tap lines connecting this vault and the wastewater stub to the main public lines in Valley View Road are shown crossing through the public right-of-way. \n\n**(3) Water or wastewater lines routing through or under any parking areas on the site:**\n*   **Yes.** The primary proposed water and wastewater lines run horizontally through the center of the site's main drive aisle. \n*   Branch service lines are shown routing directly through/under the marked parking spaces located in front of the buildings to connect the main lines to the units.\n*   *Wastewater:* Purple branch lines (annotated nearby as **\"6\\\" PVC Wastewater Service Line Minimum 1% Slope Per Detail 520-AW-01C (Typ)\"**) are shown crossing directly through the parking spaces in front of Buildings 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7.\n*   *Water:* Blue branch lines (annotated as **\"2\\\" HDPE Service Service Tubing Per Detail 520-AW-01B (Typ)\"**) are also shown routing directly through the parking spaces to service the buildings.\n\n**(4) References to easements or coordinate with Austin Energy:**\n*   **Easements:** There are multiple easements explicitly labeled on the plan, including:\n    *   **\"Sidewalk Easement\"** (along Valley View Road)\n    *   **\"Exclusive Water Line Vault Easement Doc#\"** (around the water meter vault near the entrance)\n    *   **\"Wastewater Easement\"** (top left)\n    *   **\"25' Drainage Easement\"** (right side)\n    *   **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement\"** (bottom right)\n*   **Austin Energy:** There are **no specific text annotations or notes** found on this sheet explicitly instructing the contractor to \"coordinate with Austin Energy.\" Proposed underground electric lines (red line with \"E\") are shown, but no direct reference to Austin Energy coordination is present in the text blocks.\n\n**(5) Annotations about coordination with public utilities or relocation of existing utilities:**\n*   **\"Water Tap Note\"** (bottom left): *\"The existing AC pipe must be replaced with DI pipe and a Tee cut into the DI pipe. The AC pipe must be worked on by a certified company that is licensed to handle AC pipes and the pipe disposed of in a pre-approved landfill for Asbestos pipe. Dispose of AC pipe per STATE regulations.\"*\n*   **\"Utility Notes\"** (bottom center): \n    *   *\"1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\"*\n    *   *\"2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\"*\n*   **Texas 811 Call Before You Dig Note** (bottom center): *\"The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\"*\n*   **Specific Relocation/Coordination Callouts on the Plan (Valley View Road):**\n    *   A callout box pointing to the water connection in the ROW reads: *\"Replace AC pipe with DI Pipe per Note this Sheet Contractor to Verify Location and Depth Prior to Construction 8\\\"x8\\\" Swivel Cut-In Tee 8\\\" Gate Valve\"*\n    *   *\"Replace Existing Fire Hydrant with New Fire Hydrant\"* is noted on the existing water line in Valley View Road.\n    *   *\"Connect to Existing Wastewater Stub Contractor to Verify Location and Depth Prior to Construction\"* is noted at the wastewater connection point.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1427,"outputTokens":1151,"totalTokens":5907,"reasoningTokens":3329},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2591576]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please analyze the utility tap plan and identify: (1) The routing path of the proposed water and wastewater lines from the site to the public utility connection points (indicating whether they route through Valley View Road). (2) Identify any private utilities that may be shown routing into or through the public right-of-way. (3) Check whether the water or wastewater lines route through or under any parking areas on the site. (4) Identify any references to easements or coordinate with Austin Energy. (5) Note any annotations about coordination with public utilities or relocation of existing utilities."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-25jW5a2l3nNdcw6iI6YElyXx","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 14:30:30 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::dz52p-1776954557097-fb4bc3b1be75"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided Utility Tap Plan, here are the findings corresponding to your requests:\n\n**(1) Routing path of proposed water and wastewater lines from the site to the public utility connection points:**\n*   **Water:** A proposed water line (marked as a solid blue line with \"W\" symbols) routes from the central drive aisle of the site westward, crossing the property boundary to connect to an existing water main within the public right-of-way labeled **\"Valley View Road (60' R.O.W.)\"**. The connection point includes an annotation to \"Install 8\\\" Gate Valve on Existing 8\\\" Water Line\".\n*   **Wastewater:** A proposed wastewater line (marked as a solid purple line with \"WW\" symbols) routes westward from the site's central drive aisle, parallel to the water line, crossing into the **\"Valley View Road (60' R.O.W.)\"**. It connects to the public system with an annotation reading: \"Connect to Existing Wastewater Stub Contractor to Verify Location and Depth Prior to Construction\". \n\n**(2) Private utilities routing into or through the public right-of-way:**\n*   The plans do not explicitly label the tap lines extending into Valley View Road as \"private.\" However, \"Utility Notes\" #3 and #4 state that branch lines to the buildings are private (\"All Private Domestic Water branches to the buildings...\" and \"All Private Wastewater branches to the buildings...\").\n*   The main water line connecting to the public ROW passes through a meter vault located just inside the property line (labeled **\"8\\\" Fire Demand Meter in 8' x 12' Vault\"**). The tap lines connecting this vault and the wastewater stub to the main public lines in Valley View Road are shown crossing through the public right-of-way. \n\n**(3) Water or wastewater lines routing through or under any parking areas on the site:**\n*   **Yes.** The primary proposed water and wastewater lines run horizontally through the center of the site's main drive aisle. \n*   Branch service lines are shown routing directly through/under the marked parking spaces located in front of the buildings to connect the main lines to the units.\n*   *Wastewater:* Purple branch lines (annotated nearby as **\"6\\\" PVC Wastewater Service Line Minimum 1% Slope Per Detail 520-AW-01C (Typ)\"**) are shown crossing directly through the parking spaces in front of Buildings 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7.\n*   *Water:* Blue branch lines (annotated as **\"2\\\" HDPE Service Service Tubing Per Detail 520-AW-01B (Typ)\"**) are also shown routing directly through the parking spaces to service the buildings.\n\n**(4) References to easements or coordinate with Austin Energy:**\n*   **Easements:** There are multiple easements explicitly labeled on the plan, including:\n    *   **\"Sidewalk Easement\"** (along Valley View Road)\n    *   **\"Exclusive Water Line Vault Easement Doc#\"** (around the water meter vault near the entrance)\n    *   **\"Wastewater Easement\"** (top left)\n    *   **\"25' Drainage Easement\"** (right side)\n    *   **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement\"** (bottom right)\n*   **Austin Energy:** There are **no specific text annotations or notes** found on this sheet explicitly instructing the contractor to \"coordinate with Austin Energy.\" Proposed underground electric lines (red line with \"E\") are shown, but no direct reference to Austin Energy coordination is present in the text blocks.\n\n**(5) Annotations about coordination with public utilities or relocation of existing utilities:**\n*   **\"Water Tap Note\"** (bottom left): *\"The existing AC pipe must be replaced with DI pipe and a Tee cut into the DI pipe. The AC pipe must be worked on by a certified company that is licensed to handle AC pipes and the pipe disposed of in a pre-approved landfill for Asbestos pipe. Dispose of AC pipe per STATE regulations.\"*\n*   **\"Utility Notes\"** (bottom center): \n    *   *\"1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\"*\n    *   *\"2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\"*\n*   **Texas 811 Call Before You Dig Note** (bottom center): *\"The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beg