s in Valley View Road are shown crossing through the public right-of-way. \n\n**(3) Water or wastewater lines routing through or under any parking areas on the site:**\n*   **Yes.** The primary proposed water and wastewater lines run horizontally through the center of the site's main drive aisle. \n*   Branch service lines are shown routing directly through/under the marked parking spaces located in front of the buildings to connect the main lines to the units.\n*   *Wastewater:* Purple branch lines (annotated nearby as **\"6\\\" PVC Wastewater Service Line Minimum 1% Slope Per Detail 520-AW-01C (Typ)\"**) are shown crossing directly through the parking spaces in front of Buildings 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7.\n*   *Water:* Blue branch lines (annotated as **\"2\\\" HDPE Service Service Tubing Per Detail 520-AW-01B (Typ)\"**) are also shown routing directly through the parking spaces to service the buildings.\n\n**(4) References to easements or coordinate with Austin Energy:**\n*   **Easements:** There are multiple easements explicitly labeled on the plan, including:\n    *   **\"Sidewalk Easement\"** (along Valley View Road)\n    *   **\"Exclusive Water Line Vault Easement Doc#\"** (around the water meter vault near the entrance)\n    *   **\"Wastewater Easement\"** (top left)\n    *   **\"25' Drainage Easement\"** (right side)\n    *   **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement\"** (bottom right)\n*   **Austin Energy:** There are **no specific text annotations or notes** found on this sheet explicitly instructing the contractor to \"coordinate with Austin Energy.\" Proposed underground electric lines (red line with \"E\") are shown, but no direct reference to Austin Energy coordination is present in the text blocks.\n\n**(5) Annotations about coordination with public utilities or relocation of existing utilities:**\n*   **\"Water Tap Note\"** (bottom left): *\"The existing AC pipe must be replaced with DI pipe and a Tee cut into the DI pipe. The AC pipe must be worked on by a certifie