standard utility tap practice. However, I need to check if the plans show these as properly licensed or designated as temporary/permanent easements.\n\n**EL-2.24: Utilities in parking (Table B)**\nThe vision shows that water and wastewater branch lines route \"directly through the parking spaces\" to service the buildings. \n\nSince this site is MF-2 residential zoning at 2.16 acres, Table B requirements don't apply—they only govern nonresidential projects ≥3 acres or surface parking between buildings and principal streets. So EL-2.24 is not a concern here. The most pressing issue appears to be EL-2.22, where the transformer pad lacks clearance zone markings, AE easement annotations, and truck access notes on Sheets 21 and 9—this represents a clear deficiency.\n\nI should also examine whether utility infrastructure licensing within easements under EL-2.16 presents additional problems, then cross-reference the project review form or master comment report to identify any existing utility-related deficiency notes.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1717,"cache_read_input_tokens":79752,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1717},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5916cd46-093b-4cec-ae5c-02d81ed2e2c9","uuid":"fbfe2c7a-e50c-4bc4-b598-be93df782098"}
