jects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/07-land-development-engineering.md","content":"# Land Development Engineering\n\n*Identifies items needing a License Agreement and requires adjustments to a driveway detail.*\n\nLand Development Engineering – William Bennett william.bennett@austintexas.gov\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information, and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy, and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for code compliance by city engineers.\n\nLDE1: A License Agreement is needed for the existing remaining concrete retaining wall adjacent to the street. Provide existing document number, if existing agreement exists. \nU1: Items remove. Comment cleared.\n\nLDE2: Additional comments may follow subject to final land plan design.\nU1: No additional comments, clear.\n\nLDE3: Driveway detail must show sidewalk connecting within the driveway radius instead of at the throat location. Please revise.\nU1: Comment cleared.\n","numLines":17,"startLine":1,"totalLines":17}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776954740198,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_014hff1E5UTdFEwd34e27RCR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! The measurements show buildings and transformers are well over 15 feet from the overhead line, confirming EL-1.2 and EL-1.3 are technically satisfied. However, this doesn't change the fact that clearance zones are not graphically delineated. Let me now compile my final findings based on all the research.\n\n## COMPREHENSIVE EVALUATION SUMMARY\n\nBased on my thorough research of the site plan for Valley View Townhomes, here are my findings for the electrical clearances grouping:\n\n**Items with FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE Status:**\n\n1. **EL-1.4** - Vault clearance/AE approval: NOT-VERIFIABLE (utility plan shows vault but no clearance dimensions or AE approval letter)\n\n2. **EL-1.18** - Demolition plan transmission safety: FAIL (Sheet 8 demolition notes don't address required 48-hr safety meeting, barricades, warning signs, or spoils restrictions)\n\n3. **EL-1.20** - Demolition contractor caution notes: FAIL (Sheet 8 lacks required caution language for at-grade utility appurtenances)\n\n4. **EL-1.21** - Field verification requirement: NOT-VERIFIABLE (Sheet 21 utility notes address verification of existing utility LOCATIONS but not compliance verification of proposed clearances/separations during construction)\n\n5. **EL-1.22** - SCM staging area 14-ft clearance: FAIL (Sheet 5 shows staging area but no 14-ft vertical clearance dimension; biofiltration pond volume exceeds 5,000 cu ft threshold making requirement applicable)\n\n6. **EL-1.23** - Maintenance access drive 14-ft clearance: FAIL (No labeled maintenance access drive shown on plans; no 14-ft clearance demonstrated; requirement applies to residential development SCMs)\n\n7. **EL-1.26** - Overhead clearance zones not delineated: FAIL (No 7.5-ft horizontal sky-to-ground or 15-ft radius clearance envelopes shown; no AE-provided transmission clearance envelope analysis)\n\n8. **EL-1.27** - Horizontal height limit lines: FAIL (No dashed height limit lines shown on site plan or utility plan to delineate overhead conductor clearance envelope boundaries)\n\n9. **EL-1.28** - Sloped height limit lines: FAIL (No sloped or stepped dashed height limit lines shown on grading/utility plans despite variable site elevation)\n\nNow let me prepare the structured output with these findings:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3640,"cache_read_input_tokens":71785,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3640},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e121e67-5008-4f73-b228-82e438cca3a3","uuid":"e7597589-0be9-4116-9a33-93c39e36e13a"}
{"level":30,"time":1776954757106,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_014hff1E5UTdFEwd34e27RCR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WDaSiWEnR8hzZgZiYSPVDc","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Utility plan showing meter vault near proposed water service tap"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":20}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility plan shows a fire demand meter vault near the water service entrance but does not label the vertical clearance from the top of the vault structure to the sag of the lowest overhead power line. Written clearance approval from Austin Energy is not referenced in the project file."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM 1.14.9"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site; demolition and construction operations adjacent to transmission structures"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":8}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site Demolition Notes on Sheet 8 do not address four required safety clearances for demolition near transmission lines per UCM 1.14.9: (1) pre-construction safety meeting with Austin Energy at least 48 hours before commencement, (2) barricades erected 10 feet from all transmission structures including guys and anchors within construction area, (3) warning signs placed under overhead electric transmission facilities, and (4) prohibition on materials or spoils storage within the transmission easement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site; demolition operations in proximity to at-grade utility appurtenances"]