{"level":30,"time":1776954798989,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_018YotPWCirAzsbXeB1WZ3nC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! The Electric Review section lists several critical UCM requirements including:\n- UCM § 1.3.16 - **Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites**\n- UCM § 1.10.4 - **Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults**\n\nThe review references a Bluebeam link for Austin Energy comments, which would have the specific requirements. However, I don't have access to that link.\n\nThe Land Development Engineering section notes that \"A License Agreement is needed for the existing remaining concrete retaining wall adjacent to the street.\"\n\nNow I have enough information to complete my evaluation. Let me go through the checklist items systematically and determine which ones are FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE:\n\n**FINAL EVALUATION:**\n\n1. **EL-2.1** - NOT APPLICABLE (not on CTC)\n2. **EL-2.2** - NOT VERIFIABLE (Hill Country Roadway status not explicitly stated in facts.md; need to determine if within 1,000 feet of named corridors) - However, given that the site is in southwest Austin on Valley View Road, which is far from Loop 360, RM 620, RM 2222, RM 2244, and Southwest Parkway, I'll mark this as NOT APPLICABLE due to geographic location\n3. **EL-2.3** - NOT APPLICABLE (not on CTC)\n4. **EL-2.4** - NOT APPLICABLE (not on Urban Roadway)\n5. **EL-2.5** - NOT APPLICABLE (not in Plaza Saltillo TOD)\n6. **EL-2.6** - NOT APPLICABLE (not in Plaza Saltillo TOD)\n7. **EL-2.7** - NOT APPLICABLE (not in Plaza Saltillo TOD)\n8. **EL-2.8** - NOT APPLICABLE (not in NBG district)\n\n\n9. **EL-2.9** - NOT APPLICABLE (only applies to CTC/Urban Roadway/Plaza Saltillo/NBG sites)\n10. **EL-2.10** - NOT APPLICABLE (storm drain infrastructure integral to pond design, not utilities routed under pond)\n11. **EL-2.11** - NOT APPLICABLE (no ROW street trees identified in vision analysis)\n12. **EL-2.12** - NOT APPLICABLE (no utility exclusion planting zones labeled on plans)\n13. **EL-2.13** - NOT APPLICABLE (site in parkland deficient area, but no actual parkland on site)\n14. **EL-2.14** - NOT VERIFIABLE (light rail proximity cannot be confirmed without referencing city mapping or Project Connect materials)\n15. **EL-2.15** - NOT VERIFIABLE or POSSIBLY FAIL (easements appear on site plan, though it's unclear whether they extend into the proposed ROW; requires cross-check with ROW dedication documents)\n16. **EL-2.16** - POSSIBLY FAIL (water meter vault sits within the \"Exclusive Water Line Vault Easement\" without a visible License Agreement; transformer pads occupy \"Vault Easement\" areas but lack documented AE easement or license)\n17. **EL-2.17** - NOT APPLICABLE (private water and wastewater connections through ROW follow standard utility practice, not a routing concern)\n18. **EL-2.18** - NOT VERIFIABLE (sheet 8 indicates abandoned utilities are being removed, though documentation of their complete removal status remains unclear)\n19. **EL-2.19** - NOT VERIFIABLE (unclear whether all existing public utilities in ROW are being removed or abandoned per the plans)\n20. **EL-2.20** - NOT APPLICABLE (no underground storage tanks present)\n21. **EL-2.21** - NOT VERIFIABLE (poles marked as existing without relocation documentation or coordination correspondence)\n22. **EL-2.22** - FAIL (clearance zones per UCM § 1.10.4 are not marked; no dedicated AE easement for transformer pads; truck access requirements undocumented; master comment report references UCM § 1.10.4 compliance but provides no supporting documentation)\n23. **EL-2.23** - NOT VERIFIABLE (tree wells noted on Sheet 21 with reference to \"need to look up appropriate detail\"\n\nThe landscape plan shows no tree wells and no electrical outlets are indicated. **EL-2.24** - NOT APPLICABLE (Table B doesn't apply to MF-2 residential zoning).\n\nThe most significant deficiency is **EL-2.22** — transformer pad clearances are missing, no dedicated AE easement documentation exists, and truck access requirements haven't been documented. I should examine EL-2.15, EL-2.16, EL-2.18, EL-2.19, EL-2.21, and EL-2.23 more closely to determine whether they warrant definitive FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE ratings. For EL-2.16 specifically, I need to verify if a license agreement is required for the water meter vault, particularly since the site plan shows an \"Exclusive Water Line Vault Easement\" labeled\n\n. The water vault easement is a utility easement rather than an AE easement, so the AE licensing requirement under UCM § 1.10.10.3 may not directly apply, though broader utility easement rules could govern structures placed within recorded easements. The requirement appears to address items like structures, paving, landscaping, and retaining walls placed within utility easements that need proper licensing per UCM § 1.10.10.3 and § 14-11-41.\n\nFor private utility easements like the water vault, a License Agreement would typically be required unless the infrastructure belongs to the utility itself. Since the meter vault is the customer's responsibility per UCM § 1.5.2.6, it must either sit within a dedicated easement or have appropriate licensing documentation. The site plan indicates the vault is positioned within an \"Exclusive Water Line Vault Easement,\" but I don't see evidence of a License Agreement in the provided documentation.\n\nWithout visible confirmation of the required License Agreement on the plans, this represents a deficiency. The padmount transformer pads present a similar issue—they're labeled within vault easements but lack any AE easement or License Agreement notation, and per code requirements, all padmount equipment must remain on customer property rather than in public ROW or dedicated parkland.\n\nFor t