uments rather than plan notations.\n\nFor the transformer pads, the critical issue is the absence of any AE easement shown on the site plan. Per UCM § 1.10.4, each pad must be encumbered by a dedicated AE easement. Without this shown, EL-2.22 becomes a failure item. The transformer pad clearances, AE easement requirements, and truck access documentation are all unverified.\n\nRegarding EL-2.16, the water meter vault sits within a water line vault easement on the plans, but I cannot confirm whether the required License Agreement documentation has been submitted. Since the agreement isn't visible in the submitted materials, this remains not-verifiable—the plans show the utility easement, but the licensing documentation itself is absent from what I can review. them. The standard applies specifically to non-utility items like buildings, retaining walls, paving, and landscaping within utility easements.\n\nI need to check the site plan for any such encroachments. While the vision analysis identified multiple easements on Sheet 9, it didn't specifically document whether buildings or structures overlap easement boundaries. Without clear evidence of encroachments or corresponding License Agreements, I can't definitively verify compliance. I'll mark EL-2.16 as not verifiable given the available information.\n\nFor EL-2.22, the evidence is much stronger—the vision analysis clearly shows no clearance annotations, no AE easement, and no truck access documentation. Regarding EL-2.21 on power pole relocation, the demolition plan mentions coordination with Austin Energy for pole removal, but I don't see evidence of actual relocation to a new location. If poles are simply being removed rather than relocated, this requirement may not apply.\n\nLooking at the site plan, there are existing poles noted (Guy Pole and AT&T Pole), but without documentation showing these are being moved to different locations, I can't establish that EL-2.21 applies. I'll mark it as not applicable.\n\nFor EL-2.14 regarding light rail, the grouping indicates this cannot be determined from the plans alone and requires human verification unless Capital Metro coordination letters or a Downtown Rail Corridor Permit are provided in the submission.\n\nI haven't located any light rail coordination letters in the documents. The project is located at 3759 Valley View Road in southwest Austin, and while Project Connect is developing corridors like E. Riverside and MLK, I'm uncertain whether Valley View intersects with planned light rail. I'll flag this as not verifiable due to missing coordination documentation.\n\nFor EL-2.18 on abandoned utilities, the demolition plan shows utilities being abandoned with specific procedures like pipe plugging and meter removal. However, there's no explicit evaluation of whether these abandoned utilities create clearance conflicts with the proposed improvements. The grouping specifically requires analysis of clearance conflicts. Since the plans don't demonstrate this analysis, I'll mark it as not verifiable.\n\nFor EL-2.19, the demolition plan documents removal of the existing fire hydrant and water main modifications, but doesn't clearly confirm that all public utilities in the right-of-way affected by proposed improvements are being removed. I'll mark as not verifiable.\n\nFor EL-2.23 regarding tree wells with electrical outlets, the landscape plan shows no tree wells proposed—only parking lot trees in islands and peninsulas. The electrical sheet references a tree well detail that isn't provided on the submitted sheets, and electrical outlets aren't shown at tree locations. I'll mark as not verifiable since tree wells lack detailed documentation and electrical provisions aren't shown.\n\n**FAIL:** EL-2.22 — Transformer pad clearances, AE easement, and truck access not documented.\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE:** EL-2.14, EL-2.18, EL-2.19, EL-2.23 — Light rail coordination, clearance conflicts with abandoned utilities, public utilities disposition, and tree well electrical outlets respectively. EL-2.16 requires reconsideration since the master comment report explicitly requires License Agreements for items within utility easements like the existing retaining wall. If site plan items within easements lack License Agreement documentation, this becomes a failure rather than unverifiable. I need to identify which specific items within utility easements are shown without corresponding License Agreements.\n\nThe vision tool identified water meter vaults and transformer pads within easements, but these are utility infrastructure themselves. The critical question is whether non-utility elements—buildings, paving, landscaping, or retaining walls—encroach into easements without proper documentation. Since the available documents don't clearly show non-utility item encroachments into easements, I'll mark EL-2.16 as NOT-VERIFIABLE rather than FAIL, as I cannot definitively confirm from the submitted plans whether such encroachments exist without License Agreement coverage.\n\nHowever, facts.md reveals a more fundamental problem: several recorded easements (Greenbelt Access & Use Easement and City of Austin Drainage Easement) are not depicted on the submitted site plan at all. This omission itself represents a deficiency in the submission, though it's distinct from EL-2.15, which specifically addresses easements encroaching into proposed public right-of-way rather than easements simply missing from the plans. .15 might not apply unless the submitted plans actually show an easement boundary crossing into the proposed ROW. The facts mention Easement 5 runs across the NE boundary of Lot 1, which could potentially overlap with ROW improvements in that area, but I'd need to verify the specific boundary alignment on the plat against the ROW lines to confirm a conflict exists. Since the site plan doesn't clearly demonstrate an easement encroaching into the proposed ROW, I shouldn't flag EL-2.15 as a deficiency—the missing easement depictions are more of a general completeness concern rather than a specific encroachment violation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1128,"cache_read_input_tokens":83847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1128},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5916cd46-093b-4cec-ae5c-02d81ed2e2c9","uuid":"152c5a78-de48-48ff-aacb-152b00c01d38"}
