**Bldg. 8**. It is marked with a circle symbol containing a dot and the letters \"**FH**\", with a callout box reading \"Proposed Fire Hydrant\".\n*   **Southwest Entrance Location:** There is another \"Proposed Fire Hydrant\" located near the southwest vehicle entrance to the site. It is positioned near the western boundary line adjacent to Valley View Road, just north of the southern property line boundary. A callout box points to its location reading \"Proposed Fire Hydrant\".\n*   *Note on Existing:* There is an \"Existing Fire Hydrant\" located entirely off-site in the top-left corner of the document, situated along the curved right-of-way north of the main property.\n\n**2) Is there a transmission easement or transmission structure marked on this plan? If so, where is it located?**\n**No.** There are no features explicitly labeled as a \"transmission easement\" or \"transmission structure\" on this plan. \n\nThere are, however, standard utility and electric easements marked along the property boundaries:\n*   \"**5' Electric Easement**\" is marked near the eastern boundary line, adjacent to Bldg. 6.\n*   \"**5' Elec. & Tele. Easement**\" is marked outside the southern boundary line at the bottom right.\n*   \"**5' Elec. Easement**\" is marked outside the southern boundary line at the bottom center.\n*   Various \"**5' P.U.E.**\" (Public Utility Easement) markings are located along the northern boundary.\n\n**3) What is the distance from the fire hydrant to any transmission structure or the transmission easement boundary? Is this distance marked or dimensioned?**\nBecause there are no transmission structures or transmission easements marked on the plan, there are no distances dimensioned to them. Furthermore, there are no distance lines or dimensions drawn between the proposed fire hydrants and the standard \"Electric Easements\" listed in the previous answer.\n\n**4) What is the layout of fire lanes and fire zones?**\nThe fire lane follows the continuous internal roadway loop that provides access to all eight building blocks. \n*   The text \"**Fire Lane**\" is explicitly written on the drive aisle north of buildings 2, 4, and 5.\n*   The text \"**Fire Lane**\" is explicitly written on the drive aisle south of buildings 8 and 7.\n\nRegarding Fire Zones, the physical plan does not show specific shaded or hatched areas labeled \"Fire Zone,\" but the requirements for delineating these zones are detailed in the \"**Fire Zone Notes**\" table on the left side of the plan, reproduced exactly here:\n> 1. Restricted Zone signage to be placed on front of lockers and along boat slip retaining walls as necessary or required.\n> 2. Stencil the words 'FIRE ZONE- TOW-AWAY ZONE' in white letters at least 4\" high at 30 foot intervals along the curb and the entire curb shall be painted red to serve as the background for the white letters.\n> 3. Signs stating 'FIRE ZONE- TOW-AWAY ZONE' shall be posted at both ends of a fire zone and at each entry and exit point which constitutes a portion of the fire zone or fire lane. Signs shall comply with Standard City of Austin Detail 901S-6.\n\nAdditionally, a detail drawing titled \"**NO PARKING FIRE ZONE / TOW-AWAY ZONE**\" (Standard No. 901S-6) is provided in the bottom left corner to specify the required signage.\n\n**5) Are there any utility poles, overhead electric lines (OHE), or transmission structures marked on this plan?**\n**No.** There are no overhead electric lines (OHE), transmission structures, or standard electric utility pole symbols drafted on or crossing the subject property. \n\n*Minor off-site utility notations:* In the top-left corner, off the property property near the existing street layout, there are callouts for an \"**AT&T Ped**\" (pedestal) and an \"**AT&T Vault**\".\n\n**6) Are there any clearance dimensions or annotations related to the fire hydrant placement near utilities?**\n**No.** There are no dimension lines showing required clearance distances between the fire hydrants and any other utilities (water lines, electric lines, etc.) marked on the plan. \n\nThe \"**Notes**\" section addresses the installation of the hydrants but does not mention specific clearance distances to utilities. It is reproduced exactly here:\n> **Notes**\n> 1. Underground mains feeding NFPA 13 sprinkler systems must be installed and tested in accordance with NFPA 13 and the Fire Code, by a licensed sprinkler contractor with a plumbing permit. The entire main must be hydrostatically tested at one time, unless isolation valves are provided between tested sections.\n> 2. Underground mains feeding private hydrants must be installed and tested in accordance with NFPA 24, and the Fire Code, by a licensed contractor with a plumbing permit. The entire main must be hydrostatically tested at one time, unless isolation valves are provided between tested sections.\n> 3. The Knox-box is to be located at exterior fire riser room door (non-hinged side).","providerOptions":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}]}]},"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":254032.298539,"endTime":291872.125846,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"pS3qabuAGZ