 but no clearances to poles marked\n7. **Fire Hydrants:** 2 proposed fire hydrants shown on Sheet 10, but no transmission structure clearance verification\n8. **Crossing Details:** NO crossing methods (open-cut vs. \n\ntrenchless) specified\n9. **Encasement Specs:** NO encasement specifications provided for utility crossings\n10. **Height Limit Lines:** NO dashed height limit lines or clearance envelopes shown on any site plan\n11. **Street Classification:** Valley View Road is LOCAL STREET (not CTC or Urban Roadway per facts.md)\n\n**What Was NOT Found / Could NOT Be Verified:**\n1. Transmission easement boundary not delineated on any site plan\n2. Transmission structure locations not shown (referenced in notes but not on drawings)\n3. Clearance dimensions from buildings to OHE lines (EL-1.2\n\n, EL-1.3) and from staging area to OHE/transmission structures (20-ft requirement). Missing clearance dimensions between service entrance equipment and poles (10-ft requirement), at utility crossing points, and for service drops. Texas Gas Service line coordination not documented, nor are AE underground facility separations (12-inch), joint-trench agreements, or AULCC ROW assignment changes for utilities in close proximity. Utility crossing methods and encasement specs remain unspecified. Field verification language absent from general notes. SCM staging area and maintenance access drive vertical clearances (14-ft) not addressed despite pond volume exceeding threshold. Demolition plan lacks transmission safety notes.\n\nSince the building's already demolished, no demolition plan is needed. The transmission ROW access corridor (25-ft wide, 16-ft clearance) isn't shown on the plans. Clearance zones around electrical infrastructure need graphical delineation, and horizontal height limit lines should be added to the plans, with sloped or stepped lines where grade variations occur.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1763,"cache_read_input_tokens":80382,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1763},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51587e83-ba72-4647-83cb-6d408affd332","uuid":"33d6ed3e-d1fc-4759-9c65-e19a7c1cbdfd"}
{"level":30,"time":1776954876049,"pid":39427,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01JEwnza5Yd3zfF13FrJeaVa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me compile my comprehensive findings and evaluate each checklist item. Let me create a summary table of my research:\n\nBased on my detailed research across all relevant site plan sheets (3, 5, 8, 9, 10, 12, 15, 19, 20, 21), here are my findings for each checklist item:\n\n**KEY RESEARCH FINDINGS SUMMARY:**\n\n| Finding | Status |\n|---------|--------|\n| Transmission easement boundary graphically shown | NOT FOUND |\n| Overhead Electric (OHE) lines shown | FOUND - western & southern boundaries |\n| Underground electric lines shown | FOUND - throughout site |\n| Transmission structures/towers identified | NOT FOUND |\n| Staging area shown with clearance dimensions | PARTIAL - staging area shown but NO dimensions |\n| Storm drain manholes with clearances to poles | PARTIAL - manholes shown but NO dimensions |\n| Utility crossing clearance dimensions | NOT FOUND |\n| Crossing methods (open-cut/trenchless) specified | NOT FOUND |\n| Encasement specifications provided | NOT FOUND |\n| Fire hydrants with transmission clearance verification | PARTIAL - hydrants shown but NO transmission structure shown |\n| Height limit lines delineated | NOT FOUND |\n| Field verification requirement in notes | NEEDS VERIFICATION |\n| Valley View Road street classification | LOCAL STREET (not CTC/Urban Roadway) |\n| Demolition activities planned | NO (building demolished June 2022) |\n| SCM staging area (pond >5,000 cf) | YES - 6,388 cf provided, 3.65 ft depth |\n\nNow I'll systematically evaluate each checklist item:\n\n## **CHECKLIST ITEM EVALUATIONS:**\n\n**EL-1.1** - Building or structure located within 10-ft radius of energized overhead conductors, or overhead utility zone not graphically delineated\n- **Applicability Check:** Only applies if site fronts CTC or Urban Roadway. Valley View Road is LOCAL STREET.\n- **Status:** **n/a** - Not applicable to this site\n\n**EL-1.2** - Customer facilities not maintaining minimum 7-ft 6-in horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from AE overhead conductors\n- **Applicability Check:** Applies only if overhead distribution utilities present\n- **Overhead utilities present:** Yes (OHE lines on boundaries)\n- **Clearance dimensions shown:** No horizontal clearances from buildings to OHE conductor marked\n- **Status:** **not-verifiable** - Horizontal clearances from customer facilities (buildings, transformers, pull boxes) to OHE conductors not dimensioned\n\n**EL-1.3** - Customer facilities not maintaining minimum 15-ft radius clearance from AE overhead distribution conductors\n- **Applicability Check:** Applies only if overhead distribution conductors present\n- **Clearance envelopes shown:** No 15-ft radial clearance zones delineated\n- **Status:** **not-verifiable** - 15-ft radial clearance zones from OHE conductors to customer facilities not shown\n\n**EL-1.4** - Vault vertical clearance from top of proposed structure to sag of lowest overhead power line not labeled; or AE written clearance approval not obtained\n- **Applicability Check:** Only if vaults proposed near overhead power lines\n- **Vaults shown:** No indication of vaults near overhead lines on plans reviewed\n- **Status:** **pass** - No vaults identified near overhead power lines requiring clearance labeling or approval\n\n**EL-1.5** - Clearance dimensions shown measured from utility pole centerline rather than outermost conductor\n- **Applicability Check:** Only if EL-1.2, EL-1.3, or EL-1.4 apply\n- **Finding:** No clearance dimensions shown on any plans (measured from either pole or conductor)\n- **Status:** **pass** - No clearance dimensions shown; therefore pole-centerline measurement error not applicable\n\n**EL-1.6** - Customer service entrance facilities not maintaining minimum 10-ft horizontal clearance from AE poles and overhead lines\n- **Applicability Check:** If service entrance facilities and AE poles/lines present\n- **Service entrance facilities shown:** Meters shown attached to buildings on Sheet 21; FDCs not clearly identified\n- **Clearance dimensions:** No 10-ft horizontal clearances marked from service equipment to poles\n- **Status:** **not-verifiable** - Service entrance facility clearances from AE poles not dimensioned\n\n**EL-1.7** - Overhead service-drop conductors crossing truck traffic areas not demonstrating minimum 18-ft vertical clearance\n- **Applicability Check:** If service drops cross truck traffic areas\n- **Service drops identified:** OHE lines shown on boundaries but specific service drops not identified\n- **Clearance dimensions:** No vertical clearances marked for service drops\n- **Status:** **not-verifiable** - Service-drop vertical clearances not shown or dimensioned\n\n**EL-1.8** - Utilities crossing Texas Gas Service lines without 2-ft vertical clearance; or TGS coordination not documented\n- **Applicability Check:** Only if TGS lines crossed\n- **TGS lines identified:** Not shown on utility plans\n- **Status:** **pass** - No evidence of TGS line crossings on site\n\n**EL-1.9** - AE underground facilities not maintaining minimum 12-inch clearance from other utilities at perpendicular crossings\n- **Applicability Check:** If AE underground facilities cross other utilities\n- **Crossings shown:** Yes - red dashed electric lines cross blue water, purple wastewater, green storm drain lines on Sheet 19\n- **Clearance dimensions:** No 12-inch clearances dimensioned at any crossing point\n- **Status:** **fail** - Multiple electric-utility crossings shown but clearance dimensions not provided\n\n**EL-1.10** - Non-AE utilities proposed in joint trench without written AE joint-trench agreement\n- **Applicability Check:** If non-AE utilities shown in parallel trenches with AE conduit\n- **Parallel runs identified:** Sheet 19 shows utility lines but no explicit joint trench designations\n- **Joint-trench agreement:** No agreement referenced on plans or noted\n- **Status:** **not-verifiable** - Cannot determine from plan if joint trenches are proposed vs. separate trenches\n\n**EL-1.11** - Proposed utility in public ROW within 24 inches of existing ROW facility without AULCC ROW assignment change approval\n- **Applicability Check:** If utilities proposed within public ROW\n- **ROW utilities shown:** Water tap connection shown on Sheet 20 in ROW\n- **24-inch spacing marked:** No dimensions showing distances between proposed utilities and existing ROW facilities\n- **AULCC approval:** Not referenced in project file excerpt reviewed\n- **Status:** **not-verifiable** - Cannot verify spacing from proposed ROW utilities to existing ROW facilities\n\n**EL-1.12** - Utility crossing method (trenchless vs. open-cut) not identified; prevents verification of separation standard\n- **Applicability Check:** If utility crossings over/under water or wastewater mains\n- **Crossings identified:** Multiple crossings shown on Sheet 19 (water/wastewater/storm/electric)\n- **Crossing methods specified:** No open-cut or trenchless designation shown\n- **Status:** **fail** - Utility crossing methods not identified on plans; cannot verify applicable separation standards\n\n**EL-1.13** - Encasement specifications not provided for utilities crossing under roads, structures, or barriers\n- **Applicability Check:** If utilities bored/encased under roads or structures\n- **Crossing details examined:** Sheet 20 shows utility tap but no encasement specifications\n- **Encasement notes:** None found in construction details or utility notes\n- **Status:** **fail** - Encasement specifications not provided for utility crossings\n\n**EL-1.14** - Large-diameter cleanouts (8-12\" wastewater service) not maintaining 5-ft horizontal separation from utility poles\n- **Applicability Check:** If 8\"-12\" wastewater service lines with required large-diameter cleanouts\n- **Large-diameter wastewater lines:** 6\" PVC wastewater branches shown (not 8\"-12\")\n- **Cleanout locations:** Sheet 26 shows cleanout details but application to this site not confirmed\n- **Status:** **pass** - Wastewater service lines are 6\" (not 8\"-12\"), so large-diameter cleanout requirement does not apply\n\n**EL-1.15** - Storm drain manholes less than 5-ft horizontal clearance from AE overhead poles\n- **Applicability Check:** If storm drain manholes near AE poles\n- **Manholes shown:** 3 SD Manholes on Sheet 12 (central, east-central, southern)\n- **AE poles identified:** OHE poles shown on southern boundary (Sheet 12 shows southern manhole near OHE line)\n- **Clearance dimensions:** No horizontal distances dimensioned between any manhole and any pole\n- **Status:** **fail** - Storm drain manhole locations shown relative to OHE lines, but clearance dimensions not provided; cannot verify 5-ft minimum\n\n**EL-1.16** - Non-electrical utilities routed parallel within electrical/PUE easement boundaries\n- **Applicability Check:** If non-AE utilities run parallel within easement boundaries\n- **Easements shown:** Electric easements and PUE shown on plans (5' electric, 10' PUE, etc.)\n- **Parallel routing within easements:** Sheet 19 shows water, wastewater, storm lines routing through site but easement-specific parallel routing not clearly documented\n- **Status:** **not-verifiable** - Cannot clearly determine from plans if non-electrical utilities are routed parallel within easement boundaries vs. crossing perpendicularly\n\n**EL-1.17** - Electric utility poles proposed within water easements or within 10 ft of transmission structures\n- **Applicability Check:** If poles proposed near water easements or transmission structures\n- **Poles proposed on site:** Only transformer pads and pull boxes shown; no new poles proposed\n- **Status:** **pass** - No new utility poles proposed on site\n\n**EL-1.18** - Demolition plan sequence notes do not address transmission line safety clearances (48-hr meeting, barricades, signs, material storage)\n- **Applicability Check:** Only if demolition near transmission lines\n- **Demolition status:** Building already demolished in June 2022; NO demolition activities proposed\n- **Status:** **n/a** - Not applicable; no demolition proposed; building pre-demolished\n\n**EL-1.19** - Construction plans do not demonstrate 25-ft-wide access corridor with 16-ft vertical clearance along transmission ROW\n- **Applicability Check:** If construction adjacent to transmission ROW\n- **Transmission ROW shown:** Transmission easement referenced in notes but boundary not delineated on construction/staging plans\n- **Access corridor dimensions:** No 25-ft x 16-ft clearance corridor shown on plans\n- **Status:** **fail** - Transmission ROW access corridor with 25-ft width and 16-ft vertical clearance not shown on construction plans\n\n**EL-1.20** - Demolition plan does not include caution note for at-grade utility appurtenances\n- **Applicability Check:** Only if demolition proposed\n- **Demolition proposed:** No; building already demolished\n- **Status:** **n/a** - Not applicable; no demolition proposed\n\n**EL-1.21** - Plans do not include field verification requirement for utility separations and clearances\n- **Applicability Check:** All sites with proposed utilities\n- **Utilities proposed:** Yes - extensive utilities shown\n- **Field verification language:** Sheet 21, Block 6 (Utility Notes) states: \"Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\" General notes on Sheet 3 do not explicitly include requirement for field verification of separations/clearances prior to final acceptance.\n- **Status:** **not-verifiable** - Some contractor verification language exists, but explicit requirement for field verification of ALL utility separations/clearances prior to final acceptance not clearly stated in general notes\n\n**EL-1.22** - SCM staging area vertical clearance not demonstrated at minimum 14 ft\n- **Applicability Check:** If SCM staging area and pond volume >5,000 cu ft AND depth >3 ft\n- **Pond volume:** 6,388 cf (exceeds 5,000 cu ft threshold)\n- **Ponding depth:** 3.65 ft (exceeds 3 ft threshold)\n- **Requirement applies:** YES\n- **Staging area identified:** Yes - shown on Sheet 5 on western side of property\n- **Vertical clearance dimensions:** NO 14-ft clearance labeled from staging area to vegetation/objects above\n- **Status:** **fail** - SCM staging area shown, pond exceeds exemption threshold, but 14-ft vertical clearance not demonstrated\n\n**EL-1.23** - Maintenance access drive vertical clearance not demonstrated at minimum 14 ft\n- **Applicability Check:** If SCM maintenance access required and pond >5,000 cf, >3 ft depth\n- **Requirement applies:** YES (pond exceeds both thresholds)\n- **Maintenance access shown:** Site has access driveways but explicit \"maintenance access drive\" designation not clearly identified\n- **Clearance dimensions:** No 14-ft vertical clearance labeled on any driveway\n- **Status:** **fail** - Maintenance access requirements not addressed; no 14-ft vertical clearances demonstrated\n\n**EL-1.24** - Work zone/construction access driveway vertical clearance not demonstrated\n- **Applicability Check:** If construction zones below overhead service drops or distribution lines\n- **Overhead utilities present:** Yes - OHE lines on boundaries\n- **Construction zones shown:** Staging area and construction entrances shown (Sheet 5)\n- **Clearance dimensions:** No 18-ft or 16-ft clearances marked at construction zones\n- **Status:** **not-verifiable** - Construction zones shown but vertical clearances under overhead utilities not dimensioned\n\n**EL-1.25** - Staging or temporary spoils areas overlapping utility alignments or within transmission easement\n- **Applicability Check:** If staging/spoils areas shown\n- **Staging area shown:** Yes - western side, Sheet 5\n- **Transmission easement boundary:** Not delineated on plans\n- **Utility alignment conflicts:** Cannot determine without transmission easement shown\n- **Status:** **fail** - Staging area shown but transmission easement boundary not delineated; cannot verify compliance with transmission easement protection\n\n**EL-1.26** - Overhead electrical clearance zones not graphically delineated (7.5-ft horizontal and 15-ft radial for distribution; AE-provided site-specific for transmission)\n- **Applicability Check:** If overhead utilities present\n- **Clearance zones delineated:** NO - no dashed boundary lines, hatched zones, or annotations showing clearance envelopes\n- **Status:** **fail** - Overhead electrical clearance zones (distribution and transmission) not graphically delineated on any site plan or utility plan sheets\n\n**EL-1.27** - Horizontal dashed height limit lines not shown to delineate clearance envelope boundaries\n- **Applicability Check:** If overhead utilities present\n- **Height limit lines shown:** NO - no dashed horizontal lines shown on site plan, utility plan, or grading plan\n- **Status:** **fail** - Height limit lines not shown on plans to delineate overhead utility clearance boundaries\n\n**EL-1.28** - Sloped or stepped dashed height limit lines not shown where overhead utilities present on non-uniform grade sites\n- **Applicability Check:** If overhead utilities on sloped/stepped terrain\n- **Site topography:** Site has varied elevations (488.52' to 681.08' benchmarks, buildings at different FFEs 683-687.5')\n- **Height limit lines:** NO sloped or stepped dashed lines shown\n- **Status:** **fail** - Sloped/stepped height limit lines not shown to reflect grade changes beneath overhead conductor spans\n\n---\n\nNow let me prepare the structured output with only the fail and not-verifiable items:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_detai